\s1 Saul’s Death Reported to David
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb After|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb the death|מ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb David|וְדָוִ֣ד\rb* \rb returned|שָׁ֔ב\rb* \rb from the slaughter|מֵהַכּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Amalekites|הָעֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb* \rb and stayed|וַיֵּ֧שֶׁב\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb in Ziklag|בְּצִקְלָ֖ג\rb* \rb two|שְׁנָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֥ים\rb*. \v 2 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb On the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֗י\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb a man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb with torn|קְרֻעִ֔ים\rb* \rb clothes|וּבְגָדָ֣יו\rb* \rb and dust|וַאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb arrived|בָּ֤א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶה֙\rb*.\rb |מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb When he came|בְּבֹא֣וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, \rb he fell|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb to pay him homage|וַיִּשְׁתָּֽחוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 “\rb Where|אֵ֥י\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb have you come from|תָּב֑וֹא\rb*?” \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb I have escaped|נִמְלָֽטְתִּי׃\rb* \rb from the Israelite|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb camp|מִמַּחֲנֵ֥ה\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb*.
\p \v 4 “\rb What|מֶה־\rb* \rb was the outcome|הָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb*?” \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*.\rb |אֵלָ֥יו\rb* “\rb Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb tell|הַגֶּד־\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb*.”
\p “\rb The troops|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb fled|נָ֨ס\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֗ה\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb*.\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |וְגַם־\rb* “\rb Many|הַרְבֵּ֞ה\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb them|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb fell|נָפַ֤ל\rb* \rb and died|וַיָּמֻ֔תוּ\rb*. \rb And|וְגַ֗ם\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jonathan|וִיהוֹנָתָ֥ן\rb* \rb are also dead|מֵֽתוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the young man|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb who had brought him the report|הַמַּגִּ֣יד\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb*, “\rb How|אֵ֣יךְ\rb* \rb do you know|יָדַ֔עְתָּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Jonathan|וִיהֽוֹנָתָ֥ן\rb* \rb are dead|מֵ֥ת\rb*?”
\p \v 6 “\rb I happened|נִקְרֹ֤א\rb*\rb |נִקְרֵ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb to be on Mount|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Gilboa|הַגִּלְבֹּ֔עַ\rb*,” \rb he|הַנַּ֣עַר׀\rb*\rb |הַמַּגִּ֣יד\rb*\rb |ל֗וֹ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb*, “\rb and there|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb was Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*, \rb leaning|נִשְׁעָ֣ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his spear|חֲנִית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb with|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb the chariots|הָרֶ֛כֶב\rb*\rb |וּבַעֲלֵ֥י\rb* \rb and the cavalry|הַפָּרָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb closing in on him|הִדְבִּקֻֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb When he turned around|וַיִּ֥פֶן\rb*\rb |אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb* \rb and saw me|וַיִּרְאֵ֑נִי\rb*, \rb he called out|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֔י\rb*, \rb and I answered|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*, ‘\rb Here I am|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb*!’
\p \v 8 ‘\rb Who|מִי־\rb* \rb are you|אָ֑תָּה\rb*?’ \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb So I told|וַיֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, ‘\rb I am|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb* \rb an Amalekite|עֲמָלֵקִ֖י\rb*.’
\p \v 9 \rb Then he begged me|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb* ‘\rb Stand|עֲמָד־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb over me|עָלַי֙\rb* \rb and kill me|וּמֹ֣תְתֵ֔נִי\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb agony|הַשָּׁבָ֑ץ\rb* \rb has seized me|אֲחָזַ֖נִי\rb*, \rb but|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb*\rb |בִּֽי׃\rb* \rb still|כָל־\rb* \rb lingers|ע֥וֹד\rb*.’
\p \v 10 \rb So I stood|וָאֶעֱמֹ֤ד\rb* \rb over him|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and killed him|וַאֲמֹ֣תְתֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I knew|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb he had fallen|נִפְל֑וֹ\rb* \rb he could not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb survive|יִֽחְיֶ֖ה\rb*. \rb And I took|וָאֶקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb the crown|הַנֵּ֣זֶר׀\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and the band|וְאֶצְעָדָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was on|עַל־\rb* \rb his arm|זְרֹע֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and I have brought them|וָאֲבִיאֵ֥ם\rb* \rb here|הֵֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb took hold|וַיַּחֲזֵ֥ק\rb* \rb of his own clothes|בִּבְגָדוֹ\rb* \rb and tore them|וַיִּקְרָעֵ֑ם\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb did the same|וְגַ֥ם\rb*. \v 12 \rb They mourned|וַֽיִּסְפְּדוּ֙\rb* \rb and wept|וַיִּבְכּ֔וּ\rb* \rb and fasted|וַיָּצֻ֖מוּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֞וּל\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb*, \rb and for the people|עַ֤ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they had fallen|נָפְל֖וּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb inquired|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the young man|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb who had brought him the report|הַמַּגִּ֣יד\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb Where|אֵ֥י\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb are you from|אָ֑תָּה\rb*?”
\p “\rb I am the son|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb of a foreigner|גֵּ֥ר\rb*,” \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*. “\rb I am|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb* \rb an Amalekite|עֲמָלֵקִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*, “\rb Why|אֵ֚יךְ\rb* \rb were you not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb afraid|יָרֵ֔אתָ\rb* \rb to lift|לִשְׁלֹ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb your hand|יָֽדְךָ֔\rb* \rb to destroy|לְשַׁחֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb anointed|מְשִׁ֥יחַ\rb*?” \v 15 \rb Then David|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb one|לְאַחַד֙\rb* \rb of the young men|מֵֽהַנְּעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go|גַּ֣שׁ\rb*, \rb execute|פְּגַע־\rb* \rb him|בּ֑וֹ\rb*!” \rb So the young man struck him down|וַיַּכֵּ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb and he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb For David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb had said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to the Amalekite|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb Your blood|דָּמֶיךָ\rb* \rb be on|עַל־\rb* \rb your own head|רֹאשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb your own mouth|פִ֗יךָ\rb* \rb has testified|עָנָ֤ה\rb* \rb against you|בְךָ֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb killed|מֹתַ֖תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb anointed|מְשִׁ֥יחַ\rb*.’”
\s1 David’s Song for Saul and Jonathan
\p \v 17 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb took up|וַיְקֹנֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb lament|הַקִּינָ֖ה\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֥ן\rb*, \v 18 \rb and he ordered|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb that the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb be taught|לְלַמֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb the Song of the Bow|קָ֑שֶׁת\rb*.\f + \fr 1:18 \ft Or \fqa be taught the use of the bow\ft ; literally \fqa be taught the bow\f*\rb |הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb It is written|כְתוּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of Jashar|הַיָּשָֽׁר׃\rb*:\f + \fr 1:18 \ft Or \fqa the Book of the Upright One\ft , commonly cited as \fqa Jasher\ft ; note that \fqa the Song of the Bow \ft that follows is not found in known manuscripts attributed to Jasher.\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 19 “\rb Your glory|הַצְּבִי֙\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb lies slain|חָלָ֑ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your heights|בָּמוֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb*.
\q2 \rb How|אֵ֖יךְ\rb* \rb the mighty|גִבּוֹרִֽים׃\rb* \rb have fallen|נָפְל֥וּ\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb Tell it|תַּגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb in Gath|בְגַ֔ת\rb*;
\q2 \rb proclaim it|תְּבַשְּׂר֖וּ\rb* \rb not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb in the streets|בְּחוּצֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of Ashkelon|אַשְׁקְל֑וֹן\rb*,
\q1 \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb the daughters|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb rejoice|תִּשְׂמַ֙חְנָה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the daughters|בְּנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the uncircumcised|הָעֲרֵלִֽים׃\rb* \rb exult|תַּעֲלֹ֖זְנָה\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb O mountains|הָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gilboa|בַגִּלְבֹּ֗עַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb may you have|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb no|אַל־\rb* \rb dew|טַ֧ל\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or rain|מָטָ֛ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb no fields|וּשְׂדֵ֣י\rb* \rb yielding offerings of grain|תְרוּמֹ֑ת\rb*.\f + \fr 1:21 \ft Or \fqa no showers falling on your terraced fields\ft ; LXX \fqa no fields of firstfruits\ft ; Hebrew \fqa no fields of offerings\f*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb the shield|מָגֵ֣ן\rb* \rb of the mighty|גִּבּוֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb was defiled|נִגְעַל֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the shield|מָגֵ֣ן\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb no longer|בְּלִ֖י\rb* \rb anointed|מָשִׁ֥יחַ\rb* \rb with oil|בַּשָּֽׁמֶן׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb From the blood|מִדַּ֣ם\rb* \rb of the slain|חֲלָלִ֗ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb from the fat|מֵחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb* \rb of the mighty|גִּבּוֹרִ֔ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb the bow|קֶ֚שֶׁת\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb retreat|נָשׂ֖וֹג\rb*\rb |אָח֑וֹר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the sword|וְחֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb return|תָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb empty|רֵיקָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb and Jonathan|וִיהוֹנָתָ֗ן\rb*, \rb beloved|הַנֶּאֱהָבִ֤ים\rb* \rb and delightful|וְהַנְּעִימִם֙\rb* \rb in life|בְּחַיֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb were not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb divided|נִפְרָ֑דוּ\rb* \rb in death|וּבְמוֹתָ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb They were swifter|קַ֔לּוּ\rb* \rb than eagles|מִנְּשָׁרִ֣ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb they were stronger|גָּבֵֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb than lions|מֵאֲרָי֖וֹת\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 24 \rb O daughters|בְּנוֹת֙\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb weep|בְּכֶ֑ינָה\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*,
\q1 \rb who clothed you|הַמַּלְבִּֽשְׁכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb in scarlet|שָׁנִי֙\rb* \rb and|עִם־\rb* \rb luxury|עֲדָנִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb who decked|הַֽמַּעֲלֶה֙\rb* \rb your garments|לְבוּשְׁכֶֽן׃\rb* \rb with|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb ornaments|עֲדִ֣י\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb How|אֵ֚יךְ\rb* \rb the mighty|גִבֹּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb have fallen|נָפְל֣וּ\rb* \rb in the thick|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb of battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*!
\q2 \rb Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb lies slain|חָלָֽל׃\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your heights|בָּמוֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 26 \rb I grieve|צַר־\rb*\rb |לִ֣י\rb* \rb for you|עָלֶ֗יךָ\rb*, \rb Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*, \rb my brother|אָחִי֙\rb*.
\q2 \rb You were delightful|נָעַ֥מְתָּ\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֖י\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb*;
\q1 \rb your love|אַהֲבָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb was extraordinary|נִפְלְאַ֤תָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb surpassing the love|מֵאַהֲבַ֖ת\rb* \rb of women|נָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb How|אֵ֚יךְ\rb* \rb the mighty|גִבּוֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb have fallen|נָפְל֣וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the weapons|כְּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחָמָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb have perished|וַיֹּאבְד֖וּ\rb*!”
\c 2
\s1 David Anointed King of Judah
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb Some time later|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַל֩\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֤ה׀\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֙\rb*, “\rb Should I go up|הַאֶעֱלֶ֗ה\rb* \rb to one|בְּאַחַת֙\rb* \rb of the towns|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*?”
\p “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֑ה\rb*,” \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*.\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb*
\p \rb Then David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Where|אָ֥נָה\rb* \rb should I go|אֶעֱלֶ֖ה\rb*?”
\p “\rb To Hebron|חֶבְרֹֽנָה׃\rb*,” \rb replied the LORD|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb So David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb went|וַיַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb with his two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb wives|נָשָׁ֑יו\rb*, \rb Ahinoam|אֲחִינֹ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb of Jezreel|הַיִּזְרְעֵלִ֔ית\rb* \rb and Abigail|וַאֲבִיגַ֕יִל\rb* \rb the widow|אֵ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb of Nabal|נָבָ֥ל\rb* \rb of Carmel|הַֽכַּרְמְלִֽי׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb David also|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb took|הֶעֱלָ֥ה\rb* \rb the men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֧יו\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were with him|עִמּ֛וֹ\rb*, \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb with his household|וּבֵית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and they settled|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in the towns|בְּעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb near Hebron|חֶבְרֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb came to Hebron|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb*, \rb and there|שָׁ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb they anointed|וַיִּמְשְׁחוּ־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And they told|וַיַּגִּ֤דוּ\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִד֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb It was the men|אַנְשֵׁי֙\rb* \rb of Jabesh-gilead|יָבֵ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb who buried|קָבְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb So David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of Jabesh-gilead|יָבֵ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb* \rb to tell|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*, “\rb The LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb bless|בְּרֻכִ֤ים\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you showed|עֲשִׂיתֶ֜ם\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb kindness|הַחֶ֣סֶד\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb your lord|אֲדֹֽנֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb when you buried him|וַֽתִּקְבְּר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb show|יַֽעַשׂ־\rb* \rb you|עִמָּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֣סֶד\rb*\f + \fr 2:6 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb and faithfulness|וֶאֱמֶ֑ת\rb*, \rb and I|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb will also|וְגַ֣ם\rb* \rb show|אֶעֱשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb you|אִתְּכֶם֙\rb* \rb the same|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb favor|הַטּוֹבָ֣ה\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have done|עֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb*. \v 7 \rb Now then|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb be strong|תֶּחֱזַ֣קְנָה\rb*\rb |יְדֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |וִֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb and courageous|לִבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |חַ֔יִל\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb though Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*\rb |וְגַם־\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb your lord|אֲדֹנֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb is dead|מֵ֖ת\rb*, \rb the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb has anointed me|מָשְׁח֧וּ\rb* \rb as their king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Ish-bosheth Made King of Israel
\p \v 8 \rb Meanwhile, Abner|וְאַבְנֵ֣ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of Saul’s|לְשָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb army|צָבָ֖א\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb took|לָקַ֗ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֙שֶׁת֙\rb*,\f + \fr 2:8 \fqa Ish-bosheth \ft is also called \fqa Esh-baal\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 8:33.\f* \rb moved him|וַיַּעֲבִרֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to Mahanaim|מַחֲנָֽיִם׃\rb*, \v 9 \rb and made him king|וַיַּמְלִכֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֔ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Asher|הָאֲשׁוּרִ֖י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶ֑אל\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֔ן\rb*— \rb over|וְעַל־\rb* \rb all|כֻּלֹּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb was forty|אַרְבָּעִ֨ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֜ה\rb* \rb when he began to reign|בְּמָלְכוֹ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb for two|וּשְׁתַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb*.
\p \rb The house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb however|אַ֚ךְ\rb*, \rb followed|הָי֖וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb David|דָוִֽד׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And the length|מִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of time|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb*\rb |הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֥ד\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb was seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and six|וְשִׁשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִֽׁים׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Battle of Gibeon
\p \v 12 \rb One day Abner|אַבְנֵ֣ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵ֔ר\rb* \rb and the servants|וְעַבְדֵ֖י\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb marched out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb from Mahanaim|מִֽמַּחֲנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to Gibeon|גִּבְעֽוֹנָה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb So Joab|וְיוֹאָ֨ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֜ה\rb* \rb and the servants|וְעַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb marched out|יָֽצְא֔וּ\rb* \rb and met them|וַֽיִּפְגְּשׁ֛וּם\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the pool|בְּרֵכַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Gibeon|גִּבְע֖וֹן\rb*.\rb |יַחְדָּ֑ו\rb* \rb And the two groups|אֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb took up positions|וַיֵּ֨שְׁב֜וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb opposite sides|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |הַבְּרֵכָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מִזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb of the pool|הַבְּרֵכָה֙\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Then Abner|אַבְנֵר֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, “\rb Let us have the young men|הַנְּעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb get up|יָק֤וּמוּ\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb* \rb and compete|וִֽישַׂחֲק֖וּ\rb* \rb before us|לְפָנֵ֑ינוּ\rb*.”
\p “\rb Let them get up|יָקֻֽמוּ׃\rb*,” \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb So they got up|וַיָּקֻ֖מוּ\rb*\rb |וַיַּעַבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb and were counted off|בְמִסְפָּ֑ר\rb* — \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֧ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb for Benjamin|לְבִנְיָמִ֗ן\rb*\rb |וּלְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb and Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb and twelve|וּשְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb for David|דָוִֽד׃\rb*\rb |מֵעַבְדֵ֥י\rb*. \v 16 \rb Then each man|אִ֣ישׁ׀\rb* \rb grabbed|וַֽיַּחֲזִ֜קוּ\rb* \rb his opponent|רֵעֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb by the head|בְּרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb and thrust his sword|וְחַרְבּוֹ֙\rb* \rb into his opponent’s|רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb side|בְּצַ֣ד\rb*, \rb and they all fell|וַֽיִּפְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֑ו\rb*. \rb So this|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb place|לַמָּק֣וֹם\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is in Gibeon|בְּגִבְעֽוֹן׃\rb*, \rb is called|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb*\rb |חֶלְקַ֥ת\rb* \rb Helkath-hazzurim|הַצֻּרִ֖ים\rb*.\f + \fr 2:16 \fqa Helkath-hazzurim \ft means \fqa the Field of Swords\ft .\f*
\p \v 17 \rb The battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֧י\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb intense|קָשָׁ֥ה\rb*, \rb and Abner|אַבְנֵר֙\rb* \rb and the men|וְאַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb were defeated|וַיִּנָּ֤גֶף\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb The three|שְׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֔ה\rb* \rb were|וַיִּֽהְיוּ־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֗ם\rb*: \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֥ב\rb*, \rb Abishai|וַאֲבִישַׁ֖י\rb*, \rb and Asahel|וַעֲשָׂהאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Now Asahel|וַעֲשָׂהאֵל֙\rb* \rb was fleet|קַ֣ל\rb* \rb of foot|בְּרַגְלָ֔יו\rb* \rb like a|כְּאַחַ֥ד\rb* \rb wild|בַּשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb* \rb gazelle|הַצְּבָיִ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*, \v 19 \rb and he|עֲשָׂהאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb chased|וַיִּרְדֹּ֥ף\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֑ר\rb*, \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb turning|נָטָ֣ה\rb*\rb |לָלֶ֗כֶת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb to the right|הַיָּמִין֙\rb*\rb |וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb or to the left|הַשְּׂמֹ֔אול\rb*\rb |מֵאַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb in his pursuit|אַבְנֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb And Abner|אַבְנֵר֙\rb* \rb glanced|וַיִּ֤פֶן\rb* \rb back|אַֽחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is that|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb you|הַאַתָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb Asahel|עֲשָׂהאֵ֑ל\rb*?”
\p “\rb It is|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb*,” \rb Asahel replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb So Abner|אַבְנֵ֗ר\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb*, “\rb Turn|נְטֵ֤ה\rb* \rb to|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb your|עַל־\rb* \rb right|יְמִֽינְךָ֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb your left|שְׂמֹאלֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb seize|וֶאֱחֹ֣ז\rb* \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb of the young men|מֵֽהַנְּעָרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and take|וְקַח־\rb* \rb his equipment|חֲלִצָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֖\rb*.”\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \rb But Asahel|עֲשָׂהאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb would|אָבָ֣ה\rb* \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb stop|לָס֖וּר\rb* \rb chasing him|מֵאַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Once again|וַיֹּ֧סֶף\rb*\rb |ע֣וֹד\rb*, \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֗ר\rb* \rb warned|לֵאמֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Asahel|עֲשָׂהאֵ֔ל\rb*, “\rb Stop|ס֥וּר\rb* \rb chasing me|מֵאַֽחֲרָ֑י\rb*. \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb should I strike|אַכֶּ֙כָּה֙\rb* \rb you to the ground|אַ֔רְצָה\rb*? \rb How|וְאֵיךְ֙\rb* \rb could I show|אֶשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb my face|פָנַ֔י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb*?”
\p \v 23 \rb But Asahel refused|וַיְמָאֵ֣ן\rb* \rb to turn away|לָס֗וּר\rb*. \rb So Abner|אַבְנֵר֩\rb* \rb thrust|וַיַּכֵּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the butt|בְּאַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of his spear|הַחֲנִ֜ית\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb his stomach|הַחֹ֗מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and it|הַֽחֲנִית֙\rb* \rb came out|וַתֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb his back|מֵאַחֲרָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and he fell|וַיִּפָּל־\rb* \rb dead|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb*\rb |תַּחַתוֹ\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb on the spot|שָׁ֖ם\rb*. \rb And every man|כָּל־\rb* \rb paused|וַֽיַּעֲמֹֽדוּ׃\rb* \rb when he came|הַבָּ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּקוֹם֩\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Asahel|עֲשָׂהאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb had fallen|נָ֨פַל\rb*\rb |שָׁ֧ם\rb* \rb and died|וַיָּמֹ֖ת\rb*. \v 24 \rb But Joab|יוֹאָ֥ב\rb* \rb and Abishai|וַאֲבִישַׁ֖י\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb pursued|וַֽיִּרְדְּפ֛וּ\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֑ר\rb*. \rb By sunset|וְהַשֶּׁ֣מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |בָּ֔אָה\rb*, \rb they|וְהֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb had gone|בָּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as the hill|גִּבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Ammah|אַמָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb opposite|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵי־\rb* \rb Giah|גִ֔יחַ\rb* \rb on the way|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb to the wilderness|מִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of Gibeon|גִּבְעֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb The Benjamites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִן֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb rallied|וַיִּֽתְקַבְּצ֤וּ\rb* \rb to Abner|אַבְנֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb formed|וַיִּהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb a single|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb unit|לַאֲגֻדָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb and took their stand|וַיַּ֣עַמְד֔וּ\rb*\rb |עַ֥ל\rb* \rb atop|רֹאשׁ־\rb* \rb a|אֶחָֽת׃\rb* \rb hill|גִּבְעָ֖ה\rb*. \v 26 \rb Then Abner|אַבְנֵ֜ר\rb* \rb called out|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb*: “\rb Must the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb devour forever|תֹּ֣אכַל\rb*\rb |הֲלָנֶ֙צַח֙\rb*? \rb Do you not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb realize|יָדַ֔עְתָּה\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this will only end|בָּאַחֲרוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb in bitterness|מָרָ֥ה\rb*?\rb |תִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb How long|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַי֙\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb before you tell|תֹאמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the troops|לָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb to stop|לָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb pursuing|מֵאַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*?”
\p \v 27 “\rb As surely as God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb lives|חַ֚י\rb*,” \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb if you had not|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |לוּלֵ֖א\rb* \rb spoken up|דִּבַּ֑רְתָּ\rb*,\rb |כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אָ֤ז\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb would have continued|נַעֲלָ֣ה\rb* \rb pursuing|מֵאַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb their brothers|אָחִֽיו׃\rb* \rb until morning|מֵֽהַבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb So Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb blew|וַיִּתְקַ֤ע\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb stopped|וַיַּֽעַמְדוּ֙\rb*; \rb they no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb pursued|יִרְדְּפ֥וּ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb or continued|יָסְפ֥וּ\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵֽם׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb And all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb night|הַלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb Abner|וְאַבְנֵ֣ר\rb* \rb and his men|וַֽאֲנָשָׁ֗יו\rb* \rb marched|הָֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb through the Arabah|בָּֽעֲרָבָ֔ה\rb*. \rb They crossed|וַיַּעַבְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֗ן\rb*, \rb marched|וַיֵּֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb morning|הַבִּתְר֔וֹן\rb*,\f + \fr 2:29 \ft See LXX; Hebrew \fqa marched all through Bithron\f* \rb and arrived|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb at Mahanaim|מַחֲנָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb When Joab|וְיוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb returned|שָׁ֚ב\rb* \rb from pursuing|מֵאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb he gathered|וַיִּקְבֹּ֖ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb In addition to Asahel|וַעֲשָׂה־\rb*\rb |אֵֽל׃\rb*, \rb nineteen|תִּשְׁעָֽה־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb of David’s|דָוִ֛ד\rb* \rb servants|מֵעַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb were missing|וַיִּפָּ֨קְד֜וּ\rb*, \v 31 \rb but they|וְעַבְדֵ֣י\rb*\rb |דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb had struck down|הִכּוּ֙\rb* \rb 360|שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֧וֹת\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשִּׁ֛ים\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |מֵֽתוּ׃\rb*\rb |וּבְאַנְשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb Benjamites|מִבִּנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb who were with Abner|אַבְנֵ֑ר\rb*. \v 32 \rb And they took|וַיִּשְׂאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Asahel|עֲשָׂהאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and buried him|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb in his father’s|אָבִ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb tomb|בְּקֶ֣בֶר\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb in Bethlehem|לָ֑חֶם\rb*. \rb Then Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb and his men|וַֽאֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb marched|וַיֵּלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb night|הַלַּ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb and reached|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb Hebron|בְּחֶבְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb at daybreak|וַיֵּאֹ֥ר\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 The House of David Strengthened
\p \v 1 \rb Now the war|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֚ין\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֖ין\rb* \rb and the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb protracted|אֲרֻכָּ֔ה\rb*. \rb And David|וְדָוִד֙\rb* \rb grew stronger|הֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and stronger|וְחָזֵ֔ק\rb*, \rb while the house|וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb grew weaker|הֹלְכִ֥ים\rb* \rb and weaker|וְדַלִּֽים׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb were born|וַיֵּלְדוּ\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֛ד\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֑וֹן\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb His firstborn|בְכוֹרוֹ֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֔וֹן\rb*, \rb by Ahinoam|לַאֲחִינֹ֖עַם\rb* \rb of Jezreel|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִֽת׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 3 \rb his second|וּמִשְׁנֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was Chileab|כִלְאָ֔ב\rb*,\f + \fr 3:3 \ft LXX \fqa Daluia\ft ; some translators \fqa Daniel\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 3:1.\f* \rb by Abigail|לַאֲבִיגֵל\rb* \rb the widow|אֵ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb of Nabal|נָבָ֣ל\rb* \rb of Carmel|הַֽכַּרְמְלִ֑י\rb*;
\li1 \rb his third|וְהַשְּׁלִשִׁי֙\rb* \rb was Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֣וֹם\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Maacah|מַעֲכָ֔ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of King|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Talmai|תַּלְמַ֖י\rb* \rb of Geshur|גְּשֽׁוּר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 4 \rb his fourth|וְהָרְבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb was Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Haggith|חַגִּ֑ית\rb*;
\li1 \rb his fifth|וְהַחֲמִישִׁ֖י\rb* \rb was Shephatiah|שְׁפַטְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Abital|אֲבִיטָֽל׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 5 \rb and his sixth|וְהַשִּׁשִּׁ֣י\rb* \rb was Ithream|יִתְרְעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb by David’s|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb Eglah|לְעֶגְלָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \rb These sons|אֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb were born|יֻלְּד֥וּ\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְרֽוֹן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Abner Joins David
\p \v 6 \rb During|וַיְהִ֗י\rb*\rb |בִּֽהְיוֹת֙\rb* \rb the war|הַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֚ין\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֖ין\rb* \rb and the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb Abner|וְאַבְנֵ֛ר\rb*\rb |הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb had continued to strengthen his position|מִתְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Now Saul|וּלְשָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb had a concubine|פִּלֶ֔גֶשׁ\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמָ֖הּ\rb* \rb Rizpah|רִצְפָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Aiah|אַיָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb So Ish-bosheth questioned|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Why|מַדּ֥וּעַ\rb* \rb did you sleep with|בָּ֖אתָה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb my father’s|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb concubine|פִּילֶ֥גֶשׁ\rb*?”
\p \v 8 \rb Abner|לְאַבְנֵ֨ר\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֜ד\rb* \rb was furious|וַיִּחַר֩\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb Ish-bosheth’s|בֹּ֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb accusation|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb*. “\rb Am I|אָנֹ֘כִי֮\rb* \rb the head|הֲרֹ֨אשׁ\rb* \rb of a dog|כֶּ֥לֶב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb belongs to Judah|לִֽיהוּדָה֒\rb*?” \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*. “\rb All this time|הַיּ֨וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb I have been loyal|חֶ֜סֶד\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית׀\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֗יךָ\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָיו֙\rb*, \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb his friends|מֵ֣רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb*. \rb I have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb delivered you|הִמְצִיתִ֖ךָ\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb but now|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb you accuse|וַתִּפְקֹ֥ד\rb* \rb me|עָלַ֛י\rb* \rb of wrongdoing|עֲוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb with this woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*! \v 9 \rb May God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb punish|כֹּֽה־\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb Abner|לְאַבְנֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֖ה\rb* \rb severely|יֹסִ֣יף\rb*, \rb if|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb I do not do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb what|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has sworn to him|נִשְׁבַּ֤ע\rb*: \v 10 \rb to transfer|לְהַֽעֲבִ֥יר\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb and to establish|וּלְהָקִ֞ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb of David|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb from Dan|מִדָּ֖ן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָֽׁבַע׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb And for fear|מִיִּרְאָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb of Abner|אֹתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*, \rb Ish-bosheth did not dare|יָכֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |ע֔וֹד\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb to say|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb another word|דָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb to him|אַבְנֵ֖ר\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Then Abner|אַבְנֵ֨ר\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֧ים׀\rb* \rb on his behalf|תַּחַתוֹ\rb* \rb to say|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*, “\rb To whom does|לְמִי־\rb* \rb the land belong|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*?\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb Make|כָּרְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb your covenant|בְרִֽיתְךָ֙\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb and surely|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb my hand will be|יָדִ֣י\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb to bring|לְהָסֵ֥ב\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb over to you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 13 “\rb Good|ט֔וֹב\rb*,” \rb replied David|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb will make|אֶכְרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֑ית\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּךָ֖\rb*. \rb But|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb there is one|אֶחָ֡ד\rb* \rb thing|דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִי֩\rb* \rb require|שֹׁאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb of you|מֵאִתְּךָ֤\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹר֙\rb* \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb appear|תִרְאֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before me|פָּנַ֔י\rb* \rb unless|אִם־\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb you bring|הֱבִיאֲךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb Michal|מִיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb when you come|בְּבֹאֲךָ֖\rb* \rb to see me|לִרְא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פָּנָֽי׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Then David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to say|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*, “\rb Give|תְּנָ֤ה\rb* \rb me|אֶת־\rb* \rb back my wife|אִשְׁתִּי֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Michal|מִיכַ֔ל\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb I betrothed|אֵרַ֣שְׂתִּי\rb* \rb to myself|לִ֔י\rb* \rb for a hundred|בְּמֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb Philistine|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb foreskins|עָרְל֥וֹת\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb So Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb and took Michal|וַיִּקָּחֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb from|מֵ֣עִֽם\rb* \rb her husband|אִ֑ישׁ\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֖ם\rb* \rb Paltiel|פַּלְטִיאֵ֥ל\rb*\f + \fr 3:15 \fqa Paltiel \ft is a variant of \fqa Palti\ft ; see 1 Samuel 25:44.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Laish|לוּשׁ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Her husband|אִישָׁ֗הּ\rb*\rb |הָל֧וֹךְ\rb* \rb followed|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֜הּ\rb* \rb her|אַחֲרֶ֖יהָ\rb*, \rb weeping|וּבָכֹ֛ה\rb* \rb all the way to|עַד־\rb* \rb Bahurim|בַּֽחֻרִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Then Abner|אַבְנֵ֛ר\rb*\rb |לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֥יו\rb*, “\rb Go back|שׁ֖וּב\rb*.” \rb So he returned home|וַיָּשֹֽׁב׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Now Abner|אַבְנֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb conferred|וּדְבַר־\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb In the past|תְּמוֹל֙\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֹׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |הֱיִיתֶ֞ם\rb* \rb you sought|מְבַקְשִׁ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb as your king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb take action|עֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb has said|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Through|בְּיַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֗י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb I will save|הוֹשִׁ֜יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֤י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and|וּמִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their enemies|אֹיְבֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 19 \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb spoke to|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb the Benjamites|בִנְיָמִ֑ין\rb*. \rb Then he went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*\rb |אַבְנֵ֗ר\rb* \rb to Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֔וֹן\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to tell|לְדַבֵּ֞ר\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb seemed good|טוֹב֙\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb to Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וּבְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb and to the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִֽן׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb When Abner|אַבְנֵ֤ר\rb* \rb and twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb of his men|אֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb at Hebron|חֶבְר֔וֹן\rb*,\rb |וְאִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֧ד\rb* \rb held|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb a feast|מִשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb for them|לְאַבְנֵ֛ר\rb*\rb |וְלַאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Then Abner|אַבְנֵ֣ר\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֡ד\rb*,\rb |אָק֣וּמָה׀\rb* “\rb Let me go at once|וְֽאֵלֵ֡כָה\rb*, \rb and I will gather|וְאֶקְבְּצָה֩\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֨י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that they may make|וְיִכְרְת֤וּ\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּךָ֙\rb*, \rb and that you may rule|וּמָ֣לַכְתָּ֔\rb* \rb over all|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your heart|נַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb desires|תְּאַוֶּ֖ה\rb*.”
\p \rb So David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb dismissed|וַיְּשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֖ר\rb*, \rb and he went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\s1 Joab Murders Abner
\p \v 22 \rb Just then|וְהִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִ֤ד\rb* \rb soldiers|עַבְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb and Joab|וְיוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb returned|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb from a raid|מֵֽהַגְּד֔וּד\rb*, \rb bringing|הֵבִ֑יאוּ\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּ֣ם\rb* \rb a great|רָ֖ב\rb* \rb plunder|וְשָׁלָ֥ל\rb*. \rb But Abner was|וְאַבְנֵ֗ר\rb* \rb not|אֵינֶ֤נּוּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb David had sent him|שִׁלְּח֖וֹ\rb* \rb on his way|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb When Joab|וְיוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his troops|הַצָּבָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb arrived|בָּ֑אוּ\rb*, \rb he|לְיוֹאָב֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb was informed|וַיַּגִּ֤דוּ\rb*, “\rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֤ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵר֙\rb* \rb came|בָּֽא־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb see the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb who sent him|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb on his way|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb So Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֑יתָה\rb*? \rb Look|הִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb Abner|אַבְנֵר֙\rb* \rb came|בָ֤א\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*. \rb Why|לָמָּה־\rb*\rb |זֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb did you dismiss him|שִׁלַּחְתּ֖וֹ\rb*? \rb Now he is getting away|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָלֽוֹךְ׃\rb*! \v 25 \rb Surely you realize|יָדַ֙עְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֣ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵ֔ר\rb* \rb came|בָּ֑א\rb* \rb to deceive you|לְפַתֹּתְךָ֖\rb* \rb and to track|וְלָדַ֜עַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your movements|מוֹצָֽאֲךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |מְבוֹאֶךָ\rb*\rb |וְלָדַ֕עַת\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you are|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb doing|עֹשֶֽׂה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb As soon as Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb had left|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, \rb he sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִים֙\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb who brought him back|וַיָּשִׁ֥בוּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb from the well|מִבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of Sirah|הַסִּרָ֑ה\rb*. \rb But David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb was unaware|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb of it|יָדָֽע׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb When Abner|אַבְנֵר֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb to Hebron|חֶבְר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb pulled him aside|וַיַּטֵּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the gateway|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb*, \rb as if to speak|לְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to him privately|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |בַּשֶּׁ֑לִי\rb*, \rb and there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb Joab stabbed him|וַיַּכֵּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb in the stomach|הַחֹ֔מֶשׁ\rb*. \rb So Abner died|וַיָּ֕מָת\rb* \rb on account of the blood|בְּדַ֖ם\rb* \rb of Joab’s brother|אָחִֽיו׃\rb*\rb |עֲשָׂה־\rb* \rb Asahel|אֵ֥ל\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb Afterward|כֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb about this|מֵאַ֣חֲרֵי\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֧י\rb* \rb and my kingdom|וּמַמְלַכְתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb are forever|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb guiltless|נָקִ֨י\rb* \rb before|מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb concerning the blood|מִדְּמֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Abner|אַבְנֵ֥ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb May it whirl|יָחֻ֙לוּ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb and over|וְאֶ֖ל\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb*, \rb and may the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֡ב\rb* \rb never|וְֽאַל־\rb* \rb be without|יִכָּרֵ֣ת\rb* \rb one having a discharge|זָ֠ב\rb* \rb or skin disease|וּמְצֹרָ֞ע\rb*, \rb or one who leans|וּמַחֲזִ֥יק\rb* \rb on a staff|בַּפֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb or falls|וְנֹפֵ֥ל\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb or lacks|וַחֲסַר־\rb* \rb food|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 30 (\rb Joab|וְיוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb and his brother|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb Abishai|וַאֲבִישַׁ֣י\rb* \rb murdered|הָרְג֖וּ\rb* \rb Abner|לְאַבְנֵ֑ר\rb* \rb because|עַל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb he had killed|הֵמִ֜ית\rb* \rb their brother|אֲחִיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb Asahel|עֲשָׂהאֵ֧ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb at Gibeon|בְּגִבְע֖וֹן\rb*.)
\s1 David Mourns for Abner
\p \v 31 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֜ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Tear|קִרְע֤וּ\rb* \rb your clothes|בִגְדֵיכֶם֙\rb*, \rb put on|וְחִגְר֣וּ\rb* \rb sackcloth|שַׂקִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and mourn|וְסִפְד֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֑ר\rb*.” \rb And King|וְהַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David himself|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb walked|הֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb behind|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the funeral bier|הַמִּטָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb When they buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wept|וַיֵּבְךְּ֙\rb* \rb aloud|וַיִשָּׂ֧א\rb*\rb |קוֹל֗וֹ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abner’s|אַבְנֵ֔ר\rb* \rb tomb|קֶ֣בֶר\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃פ\rb* \rb wept|וַיִּבְכּ֖וּ\rb*. \v 33 \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb sang this lament|וַיְקֹנֵ֥ן\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Should Abner|אַבְנֵֽר׃\rb* \rb die|יָמ֥וּת\rb*
\q2 \rb the death|הַכְּמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of a fool|נָבָ֖ל\rb*?
\q1 \v 34 \rb Your hands|יָדֶ֣ךָ\rb* \rb were not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb bound|אֲסֻר֗וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb your feet|וְרַגְלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb were not|לֹא־\rb* \rb fettered|לִנְחֻשְׁתַּ֣יִם\rb*.\rb |הֻגָּ֔שׁוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb As a man falls|כִּנְפ֛וֹל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb the wicked|עַוְלָ֖ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb so also you fell|נָפָ֑לְתָּ\rb*.”
\p \rb And all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb wept|לִבְכּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb over him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \rb even more|וַיֹּסִ֥פוּ\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb Then all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb and urged David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb to eat|לְהַבְר֧וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb something|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb while it was still|בְּע֣וֹד\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*, \rb but David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb took an oath|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֨ע\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, “\rb May God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb punish|כֹּ֣ה\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֤י\rb*, \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely|יֹסִ֔יף\rb*,\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb I taste|אֶטְעַם־\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb anything else|כָל־\rb*\rb |מְאֽוּמָה׃\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֛מֶשׁ\rb* \rb sets|בֽוֹא־\rb*!”
\p \v 36 \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb took note|הִכִּ֔ירוּ\rb* \rb and|וַיִּיטַ֖ב\rb* \rb were pleased|בְּעֵֽינֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb In fact, everything|כְּכֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb pleased|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb them|כָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |טֽוֹב׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb So on that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb were convinced|וַיֵּדְע֧וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the king|מֵֽהַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb had no|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb part|הָיְתָה֙\rb* \rb in the murder|לְהָמִ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Abner|אַבְנֵ֥ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵֽר׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb*, “\rb Do you not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb realize|תֵדְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb a great|וְגָד֗וֹל\rb* \rb prince|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb has fallen|נָפַ֛ל\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*? \v 39 \rb And I am|וְאָנֹכִ֨י\rb* \rb weak|רַךְ֙\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*, \rb though anointed|וּמָשׁ֣וּחַ\rb* \rb as king|מֶ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and these|הָאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb are too fierce|קָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb for me|מִמֶּ֑נִּי\rb*. \rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb repay|יְשַׁלֵּ֧ם\rb* \rb the evildoer|לְעֹשֵׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |הָרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb according to his evil|כְּרָעָתֽוֹ׃פ\rb*!”
\c 4
\s1 The Murder of Ish-bosheth
\p \v 1 \rb Now when Ish-bosheth son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵר֙\rb* \rb had died|מֵ֤ת\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb he lost|וַיִּרְפּ֖וּ\rb* \rb courage|יָדָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb was dismayed|נִבְהָֽלוּ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֟וּל\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb had two|וּשְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb who were leaders|שָׂרֵֽי־\rb* \rb of raiding parties|גְדוּדִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָי֪וּ\rb*. \rb One was|הָאֶחָ֨ד\rb* \rb named|שֵׁם֩\rb* \rb Baanah|בַּֽעֲנָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֧ם\rb* \rb and the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֣י\rb* \rb Rechab|רֵכָ֗ב\rb*; \rb they were sons|בְּנֵ֛י\rb* \rb of Rimmon|רִמּ֥וֹן\rb* \rb the Beerothite|הַבְּאֶֽרֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb of the tribe|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb*—\rb |כִּ֚י\rb* \rb Beeroth|בְּאֵר֔וֹת\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb is considered|תֵּחָשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb part of|עַל־\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִֽן׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb because the Beerothites|הַבְּאֵרֹתִ֖ים\rb* \rb fled|וַיִּבְרְח֥וּ\rb* \rb to Gittaim|גִּתָּ֑יְמָה\rb* \rb and have lived|וַֽיִּהְיוּ־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb as foreigners|גָּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb And Jonathan|וְלִיהֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb had a son who was|בֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb lame in|נְכֵ֣ה\rb* \rb his feet|רַגְלָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb He was|הָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb five|חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֣ים\rb* \rb when the report|שְׁמֻעַת֩\rb* \rb about Saul|שָׁא֨וּל\rb* \rb and Jonathan|וִיהֽוֹנָתָ֜ן\rb* \rb came|בְּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb from Jezreel|מִֽיִּזְרְעֶ֗אל\rb*. \rb His nurse|אֹֽמַנְתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb picked him up|וַתִּשָּׂאֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb and fled|וַתָּנֹ֔ס\rb*,\rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb but as she was hurrying|בְּחָפְזָ֥הּ\rb* \rb to escape|לָנ֛וּס\rb*, \rb he fell|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb and became lame|וַיִּפָּסֵ֖חַ\rb*. \rb His name|וּשְׁמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb was Mephibosheth|מְפִיבֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Now Rechab|רֵכָ֣ב\rb* \rb and Baanah|וּבַעֲנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Rimmon|רִמּ֤וֹן\rb* \rb the Beerothite|הַבְּאֵֽרֹתִי֙\rb*, \rb set out|וַיֵּ֨לְכ֜וּ\rb* \rb and arrived|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb in the heat|כְּחֹ֣ם\rb* \rb of the day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*, \rb while the king|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb was taking his midday|הַֽצָּהֳרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb nap|שֹׁכֵ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |מִשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb*. \v 6 \rb |וְ֠הֵנָּה\rb* \rb They entered|בָּ֜אוּ\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb the interior|תּ֤וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the house|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb as if to get|לֹקְחֵ֣י\rb* \rb some wheat|חִטִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and they stabbed him|וַיַּכֻּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the stomach|הַחֹ֑מֶשׁ\rb*. \rb Then Rechab|וְרֵכָ֛ב\rb* \rb and his brother|אָחִ֖יו\rb* \rb Baanah|וּבַעֲנָ֥ה\rb* \rb slipped away|נִמְלָֽטוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb They had entered|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb while Ish-bosheth|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb was lying|שֹׁכֵ֤ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his bed|מִטָּתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |בַּחֲדַ֣ר\rb*\rb |מִשְׁכָּב֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and having stabbed|וַיַּכֻּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיְמִתֻ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb they beheaded|וַיָּסִ֖ירוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb took|וַיִּקְחוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and traveled|וַיֵּֽלְכ֛וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb night|הַלָּֽיְלָה׃\rb* \rb by way|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Arabah|הָעֲרָבָ֖ה\rb*. \v 8 \rb They brought|וַ֠יָּבִאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֨אשׁ\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֮\rb* \rb at Hebron|חֶבְרוֹן֒\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Here is|הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*, \rb your enemy|אֹֽיִבְךָ֔\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb sought|בִּקֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Today|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb* \rb has granted|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb vengeance|נְקָמוֹת֙\rb* \rb to my lord|לַֽאדֹנִ֨י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb against Saul|מִשָּׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb and his offspring|וּמִזַּרְעֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 The Execution of Rechab and Baanah
\p \v 9 \rb But David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb Rechab|רֵכָ֣ב׀\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֗יו\rb* \rb Baanah|בַּעֲנָ֣ה\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֛י\rb* \rb of Rimmon|רִמּ֥וֹן\rb* \rb the Beerothite|הַבְּאֵֽרֹתִ֖י\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb*, “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֕ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has redeemed|פָּדָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb distress|צָרָֽה׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb when|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb someone told|הַמַּגִּיד֩\rb* \rb me|לִ֨י\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֜ר\rb* ‘\rb Look|הִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb is dead|מֵ֣ת\rb*,’ \rb and thought|בְּעֵינָ֔יו\rb* \rb he|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb a bearer of good news|כִמְבַשֵּׂר֙\rb*, \rb I seized|וָאֹחֲזָ֣ה\rb* \rb him|ב֔וֹ\rb* \rb and put him to death|וָאֶהְרְגֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb at Ziklag|בְּצִֽקְלָ֑ג\rb*. \rb That|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb was his reward|לְתִתִּי־\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb for his news|בְּשֹׂרָֽה׃\rb*! \v 11 \rb How much more|אַ֞ף\rb*, \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb wicked|רְשָׁעִ֗ים\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb kill|הָרְג֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a righteous|צַדִּ֛יק\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb in his own house|בְּבֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb and on|עַל־\rb* \rb his own bed|מִשְׁכָּב֑וֹ\rb*, \rb shall I not now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |הֲל֨וֹא\rb* \rb require|אֲבַקֵּ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his blood|דָּמוֹ֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb your hands|מִיֶּדְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and remove you|וּבִעַרְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 12 \rb So David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַו֩\rb* \rb his young men|הַנְּעָרִ֜ים\rb*, \rb and they killed Rechab and Baanah|וַיַּהַרְג֗וּם\rb*. \rb They cut off|וַֽיְקַצְּצ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and feet|רַגְלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and hung|וַיִּתְל֥וּ\rb* \rb their bodies by|עַל־\rb* \rb the pool|הַבְּרֵכָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֑וֹן\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb but they took|לָקָ֔חוּ\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֤אשׁ\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Ish-bosheth|בֹּ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb and buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb it in Abner’s|אַבְנֵ֖ר\rb* \rb tomb|בְקֶֽבֶר־\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְרֽוֹן׃פ\rb*.
\c 5
\s1 David Anointed King of All Israel
\p \v 1 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb at Hebron|חֶבְר֑וֹנָה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Here|הִנְנ֛וּ\rb* \rb we are|אֲנָֽחְנוּ׃\rb*, \rb your own flesh|וּֽבְשָׂרְךָ֖\rb* \rb and blood|עַצְמְךָ֥\rb*. \v 2 \rb Even|גַּם־\rb*\rb |אֶתְמ֣וֹל\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb in times past|שִׁלְשׁ֗וֹם\rb*, \rb while Saul|שָׁא֥וּל\rb* \rb was|בִּהְי֨וֹת\rb* \rb king|מֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb over us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb were the one|הָיִיתָה\rb* \rb who led Israel out|מוֹצִיא\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and brought them back|וְהַמֵּבִי\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb And to you|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb You|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb will shepherd|תִרְעֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb will be|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb ruler|לְנָגִ֖יד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb them|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 3 \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb came|וַ֠יָּבֹאוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb at Hebron|חֶבְר֔וֹנָה\rb*, \rb where|בְּחֶבְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb* \rb made|וַיִּכְרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶם֩\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֛ית\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And they anointed|וַיִּמְשְׁח֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb was thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֛ה\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*. \v 5 \rb In Hebron|בְּחֶבְרוֹן֙\rb* \rb he reigned|מָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and six|וְשִׁשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb and in Jerusalem|וּבִירוּשָׁלִַ֣ם\rb* \rb he reigned|מָלַ֗ךְ\rb* \rb thirty-three|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׁלֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb over|עַ֥ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 David Conquers Jerusalem
\p \v 6 \rb Now the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his men|וַֽאֲנָשָׁיו֙\rb* \rb marched|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Jebusites|הַיְבֻסִ֖י\rb* \rb who inhabited|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb The Jebusites said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֤ד\rb*: “\rb You will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb get in|תָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb here|הֵ֔נָּה\rb*. \rb Even|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the blind|הַעִוְרִ֤ים\rb* \rb and lame|וְהַפִּסְחִים֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb can repel you|הֱסִֽירְךָ֗\rb*.” \rb For they thought|לֵאמֹר֙\rb*, “\rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb get in|יָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb here|הֵֽנָּה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Nevertheless , David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֣ד\rb* \rb the fortress|מְצֻדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֑וֹן\rb* (\rb that is|הִ֖יא\rb*, \rb the City|עִ֥יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*). \v 8 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb he|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Whoever attacks|מַכֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Jebusites|יְבֻסִי֙\rb* \rb must use the water shaft|בַּצִּנּ֔וֹר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb to reach|וְיִגַּ֣ע\rb* \rb the lame|הַפִּסְחִים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and blind|הַ֣עִוְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb who are despised|שָׂנְאוּ\rb*\rb |נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb by David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*.\f + \fr 5:8 \ft Or \fqa who are enemies of David\f*” \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֙\rb* \rb it is said|יֹֽאמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb The blind|עִוֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb and the lame|וּפִסֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb enter|יָב֖וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the palace|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb So David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb took up residence|וַיֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the fortress|בַּמְּצֻדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and called|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb it|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb the City|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*. \rb He|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb built it up|וַיִּ֤בֶן\rb* \rb all the way around|סָבִ֔יב\rb*, \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the supporting terraces|הַמִּלּ֖וֹא\rb*\f + \fr 5:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Millo\f* \rb inward|וָבָֽיְתָה׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb And David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb became|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb greater|הָל֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb and greater|וְגָד֑וֹל\rb*, \rb for the LORD|וַיהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb was with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Now Hiram|חִירָ֨ם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹ֥ר\rb* \rb sent|וַ֠יִּשְׁלַח\rb* \rb envoys|מַלְאָכִים֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֒\rb*, \rb along with cedar|אֲרָזִ֔ים\rb* \rb logs|וַעֲצֵ֣י\rb*, \rb carpenters|וְחָרָשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |עֵ֔ץ\rb*, \rb and stonemasons|וְחָֽרָשֵׁ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶ֣בֶן\rb*,\rb |קִ֑יר\rb* \rb and they built|וַיִּבְנֽוּ־\rb* \rb a palace|בַ֖יִת\rb* \rb for David|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb*.
\s1 David’s Family Grows
\p \v 12 \rb And David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb realized|וַיֵּ֣דַע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had established him|הֱכִינ֧וֹ\rb* \rb as king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְכִי֙\rb* \rb and had exalted|נִשֵּׂ֣א\rb* \rb his kingdom|מַמְלַכְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb for the sake of|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb he had arrived|בֹּא֣וֹ\rb* \rb from Hebron|מֵחֶבְר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb more|ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb concubines|פִּֽלַגְשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb and wives|וְנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb and more|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֥ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb were born|וַיִּוָּ֥לְדּוּ\rb* \rb to him|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb*. \v 14 \rb These|וְאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמ֛וֹת\rb* \rb of the children born|הַיִּלֹּדִ֥ים\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*: \rb Shammua|שַׁמּ֣וּעַ\rb*,\f + \fr 5:14 \fqa Shammua \ft is a variant of \fqa Shimea\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 3:5.\f* \rb Shobab|וְשׁוֹבָ֔ב\rb*, \rb Nathan|וְנָתָ֖ן\rb*, \rb Solomon|וּשְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb Ibhar|וְיִבְחָ֥ר\rb*, \rb Elishua|וֶאֱלִישׁ֖וּעַ\rb*, \rb Nepheg|וְנֶ֥פֶג\rb*, \rb Japhia|וְיָפִֽיעַ׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb Elishama|וֶאֱלִישָׁמָ֥ע\rb*, \rb Eliada|וְאֶלְיָדָ֖ע\rb*, \rb and Eliphelet|וֶאֱלִיפָֽלֶט׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Two Victories over the Philistines
\p \v 17 \rb When the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb had been anointed|מָשְׁח֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb they|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb went|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb in search of|לְבַקֵּ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*; \rb but David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb learned of this|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb and went down|וַיֵּ֖רֶד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the stronghold|הַמְּצוּדָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Now the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb had come|בָּ֑אוּ\rb* \rb and spread out|וַיִּנָּטְשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּעֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Rephaim|רְפָאִֽים׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb So David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַ֨ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָה֙\rb*, “\rb Should I go up|הַאֶֽעֱלֶה֙\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*? \rb Will You deliver them|הֲתִתְּנֵ֖ם\rb* \rb into my hand|בְּיָדִ֑י\rb*?”
\p “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֔ה\rb*,” \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |דָּוִד֙\rb*, “\rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will surely deliver|נָתֹ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֶתֵּ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistines|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb So David|דָוִ֥ד\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb*\rb |בְּבַֽעַל־\rb* \rb to Baal-perazim|פְּרָצִים֮\rb*, \rb where he defeated the Philistines|וַיַּכֵּ֣ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֣ם\rb*\rb |דָּוִד֒\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Like a bursting|כְּפֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb flood|מָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has burst out|פָּרַ֨ץ\rb* \rb against my enemies|אֹיְבַ֛י\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנַ֖י\rb*.” \rb So|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb he called|קָרָ֛א\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |בַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb Baal-perazim|פְּרָצִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 5:20 \fqa Baal-perazim \ft means \fqa The Lord Bursts Out\ft .\f* \v 21 \rb There|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb the Philistines abandoned|וַיַּעַזְבוּ־\rb* \rb their idols|עֲצַבֵּיהֶ֑ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָֽׁיו׃פ\rb* \rb carried them away|וַיִּשָּׂאֵ֥ם\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Once again|וַיֹּסִ֥פוּ\rb*\rb |ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb came up|לַֽעֲל֑וֹת\rb* \rb and spread out|וַיִּנָּֽטְשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּעֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Rephaim|רְפָאִֽים׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb So David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַ֤ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb who answered|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb march straight up|תַעֲלֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb but circle|הָסֵב֙\rb* \rb around|אֶל־\rb* \rb behind them|אַ֣חֲרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and attack|וּבָ֥אתָ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in front|מִמּ֥וּל\rb* \rb of the balsam trees|בְּכָאִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 5:23 \ft Or \fqa aspen trees \ft or \fqa poplar trees\ft ; also in verse 24\f* \v 24 \rb As soon as|וִ֠יהִי\rb* \rb you hear|בְּשָׁמְעֲךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sound|ק֧וֹל\rb* \rb of marching|צְעָדָ֛ה\rb* \rb in the tops|בְּרָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the balsam trees|הַבְּכָאִ֖ים\rb*, \rb move quickly|תֶּחֱרָ֑ץ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this will mean that|אָ֗ז\rb*\rb |אָ֣ז\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has gone out|יָצָ֤א\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to strike|לְהַכּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb the camp|בְּמַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb So David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |כֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb had commanded him|צִוָּ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb and he struck down|וַיַּךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb all the way from Gibeon|מִגֶּ֖בַע\rb*\f + \fr 5:25 \ft LXX (see also 1 Chronicles 14:16); Hebrew \fqa Geba\f* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |בֹּאֲךָ֥\rb* \rb Gezer|גָֽזֶר׃פ\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 David Fetches the Ark
\p \v 1 \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb again|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb assembled|וַיֹּ֨סֶף\rb* \rb the chosen men|בָּח֥וּר\rb* \rb of Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb*. \v 2 \rb |וַיָּ֣קָם׀\rb* \rb And he|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his troops|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb set out|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |מִֽבַּעֲלֵ֖י\rb* \rb for Baale of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 6:2 \ft That is, Kiriath-jearim; see 1 Chronicles 13:6.\f* \rb to bring up|לְהַעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is called|נִקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb by the Name|שֵׁ֗ם\rb*—\f + \fr 6:2 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate do not include \fqa the Name—\f* \rb the name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֛וֹת\rb*, \rb who is enthroned|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb between the cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִ֖ים\rb* \rb that are on it|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb They set|וַיַּרְכִּ֜בוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb a new|חֲדָשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb cart|עֲגָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and brought it|וַיִּשָּׂאֻ֔הוּ\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Abinadab|אֲבִינָדָ֖ב\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was on the hill|בַּגִּבְעָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Uzzah|וְעֻזָּ֣א\rb* \rb and Ahio|וְאַחְי֗וֹ\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb of Abinadab|אֲבִ֣ינָדָ֔ב\rb*, \rb were guiding|נֹהֲגִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the new|חֲדָשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb cart|הָעֲגָלָ֥ה\rb*, \v 4 \rb bringing|וַיִּשָּׂאֻ֗הוּ\rb* \rb with it|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*\rb |מִבֵּ֤ית\rb*\rb |אֲבִֽינָדָב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |בַּגִּבְעָ֔ה\rb*.\f + \fr 6:4 \ft DSS and some LXX manuscripts; MT includes \fqa from the house of Abinadab, which was on the hill\ft .\f* \rb And Ahio|וְאַחְי֕וֹ\rb* \rb was walking|הֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the ark|הָאָרֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\s1 Uzzah Touches the Ark
\p \v 5 \rb David|וְדָוִ֣ד׀\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb were celebrating|מְשַֽׂחֲקִים֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb with all kinds|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb of wood instruments|עֲצֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בְרוֹשִׁ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 6:5 \ft Literally \fqa before the LORD with all woods of cypress\ft ; LXX \fqa playing before the Lord on well-tuned instruments mightily, and with songs\ft ; some of the instruments in this verse are uncertain; see 1 Chronicles 13:8.\f* \rb harps|וּבְכִנֹּר֤וֹת\rb*, \rb stringed instruments|וּבִנְבָלִים֙\rb*, \rb tambourines|וּבְתֻפִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb sistrums|וּבִמְנַֽעַנְעִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and cymbals|וּֽבְצֶלְצֶלִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb When they came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the threshing floor|גֹּ֣רֶן\rb* \rb of Nacon|נָכ֑וֹן\rb*,\f + \fr 6:6 \fqa Nacon \ft is a variant of \fqa Chidon\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 13:9.\f* \rb Uzzah|עֻזָּ֜א\rb* \rb reached out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb and took hold|וַיֹּ֣אחֶז\rb* \rb of|בּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the oxen|הַבָּקָֽר׃\rb* \rb had stumbled|שָׁמְט֖וּ\rb*. \v 7 \rb And the anger|אַ֤ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Uzzah|בְּעֻזָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb and God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb struck him down|וַיַּכֵּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb on the spot|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb his irreverence|הַשַּׁ֑ל\rb*,\f + \fr 6:7 \ft MT; DSS \fqa for this\f* \rb and he died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb beside|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Then David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb became angry|וַיִּ֣חַר\rb* \rb because|עַל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had burst forth|פָּרַ֧ץ\rb*\rb |פֶּ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb against Uzzah|בְּעֻזָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb So he named|וַיִּקְרָ֞א\rb* \rb that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb place|לַמָּק֤וֹם\rb*\rb |פֶּ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb Perez-uzzah|עֻזָּ֔ה\rb*,\f + \fr 6:8 \fqa Perez-uzzah \ft means \fqa outbreak against Uzzah\ft .\f* \rb as it is called to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb That|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb feared|וַיִּרָ֥א\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb How|אֵ֛יךְ\rb* \rb can the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb ever come|יָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*?” \v 10 \rb So he|דָוִ֗ד\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb was unwilling|אָבָ֣ה\rb* \rb to move|לְהָסִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֛יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the City|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*; \rb instead, he took|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb it aside|וַיַּטֵּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |עֹבֵֽד־\rb* \rb of Obed-edom|אֱד֖וֹם\rb* \rb the Gittite|הַגִּתִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Thus the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb remained|וַיֵּשֶׁב֩\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |עֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb of Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֛ם\rb* \rb the Gittite|הַגִּתִּ֖י\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֧רֶךְ\rb*\rb |עֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb him|אֱדֹ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his household|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 The Ark Brought to Jerusalem
\p \v 12 \rb Now it was reported|וַיֻּגַּ֗ד\rb* \rb to King|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has blessed|בֵּרַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֨ית\rb*\rb |עֹבֵ֤ד\rb* \rb of Obed-edom|אֱדֹם֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb belongs to him|ל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because of|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*.”
\p \rb So David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and had the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb brought up|וַיַּעַל֩\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֨ית\rb*\rb |עֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb of Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֛ם\rb* \rb into the City|עִ֥יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb with rejoicing|בְּשִׂמְחָֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb those carrying|נֹשְׂאֵ֥י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרוֹן־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had advanced|צָעֲד֛וּ\rb* \rb six|שִׁשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb paces|צְעָדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb he sacrificed|וַיִּזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb an ox|שׁ֖וֹר\rb* \rb and a fattened calf|וּמְרִֽיא׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb And David|וְדָוִ֛ד\rb*,\rb |וְדָוִ֕ד\rb* \rb wearing|חָג֖וּר\rb* \rb a linen|בָּֽד׃\rb* \rb ephod|אֵפ֥וֹד\rb*, \rb danced|מְכַרְכֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his might|עֹ֖ז\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \v 15 \rb while he|וְדָוִד֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb brought up|מַעֲלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb with shouting|בִּתְרוּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the sounding|וּבְק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of the ram’s horn|שׁוֹפָֽר׃\rb*.
\s1 Michal’s Contempt for David
\p \v 16 \rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb As the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb was entering|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb the City|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb Michal|וּמִיכַ֨ל\rb* \rb looked down|נִשְׁקְפָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb from|בְּעַ֣ד\rb* \rb a window|הַחַלּ֗וֹן\rb* \rb and saw|וַתֵּ֨רֶא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb leaping|מְפַזֵּ֤ז\rb* \rb and dancing|וּמְכַרְכֵּר֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and she despised|וַתִּ֥בֶז\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb in her heart|בְּלִבָּֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb So they brought|וַיָּבִ֜אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and set|וַיַּצִּ֤גוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in its place|בִּמְקוֹמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb inside|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the tent|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb had pitched|נָטָה־\rb* \rb for it|ל֖וֹ\rb*. \rb Then David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb* \rb offered|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֛וֹת\rb* \rb and peace offerings|וּשְׁלָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb When David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb had finished|וַיְכַ֣ל\rb* \rb sacrificing|מֵהַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb the burnt offerings|הָעוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and peace offerings|וְהַשְּׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb he blessed|וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Then he distributed|וַיְחַלֵּ֨ק\rb* \rb to every|לְכָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb man|לְמֵאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁה֒\rb* \rb among|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the multitude|הֲמ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֮\rb* \rb a|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb loaf|חַלַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*, \rb a|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb date cake|וְאֶשְׁפָּ֣ר\rb*,\f + \fr 6:19 \ft Or \fqa a portion of meat\f* \rb and a|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb raisin cake|וַאֲשִׁישָׁ֖ה\rb*. \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb*, \rb each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his own home|לְבֵיתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb When David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb home to bless|לְבָרֵ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his own household|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb Saul’s|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb Michal|מִיכַ֤ל\rb* \rb came out|וַתֵּצֵ֞א\rb* \rb to meet him|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*. “\rb How|מַה־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb has distinguished himself|נִּכְבַּ֨ד\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb*!” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*. “\rb He|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has uncovered himself|נִגְלָ֤ה\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the maidservants|אַמְה֣וֹת\rb* \rb of his subjects|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb*, \rb like a|אַחַ֥ד\rb* \rb vulgar person|הָרֵקִֽים׃\rb* \rb would do|כְּהִגָּל֥וֹת\rb*\rb |נִגְל֖וֹת\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb But David|דָּוִד֮\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Michal|מִיכַל֒\rb*, “\rb I was dancing before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb chose|בָּֽחַר־\rb* \rb me|בִּ֤י\rb* \rb over your father|מֵֽאָבִיךְ֙\rb* \rb and all|וּמִכָּל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb* \rb when He appointed|לְצַוֺּ֨ת\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb ruler|נָגִ֛יד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb people|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb I will celebrate|וְשִׂחַקְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*, \v 22 \rb and I will humiliate|וּנְקַלֹּ֤תִי\rb*\rb |וְהָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb and humble|שָׁפָ֖ל\rb* \rb myself|בְּעֵינָ֑י\rb* \rb even more|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb than this|מִזֹּ֔את\rb*. \rb Yet I will be honored|אִכָּבֵֽדָה׃\rb* \rb by|וְעִם־\rb* \rb the maidservants|הָֽאֲמָהוֹת֙\rb* \rb of whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have spoken|אָמַ֔רְתְּ\rb*\rb |עִמָּ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb And Michal|וּלְמִיכַל֙\rb* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb had|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb children|יָ֑לֶד\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb of her death|מוֹתָֽהּ׃פ\rb*.
\c 7
\s1 God’s Covenant with David
\p \v 1 \rb After|וַיְהִ֕י\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb had settled|יָשַׁ֥ב\rb* \rb into his palace|בְּבֵית֑וֹ\rb* \rb and the LORD|וַיהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had given him rest|הֵנִֽיחַ־\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb his enemies|אֹיְבָֽיו׃\rb*\rb |ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb around him|מִסָּבִ֖יב\rb*, \v 2 \rb he|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*, “\rb Here|רְאֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |נָ֔א\rb* \rb I am|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb*, \rb living|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in a house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of cedar|אֲרָזִ֑ים\rb*, \rb while the ark|וַֽאֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb remains|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb a tent|הַיְרִיעָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb And Nathan|נָתָן֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and do|עֲשֵׂ֑ה\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in your heart|בִּֽלְבָבְךָ֖\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb But that|הַה֑וּא\rb*\rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֖ן\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 5 “\rb Go|לֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: \rb Are you the one|הַאַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb to build|תִּבְנֶה־\rb* \rb for Me|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb a house|בַ֖יִת\rb* \rb to dwell in|לְשִׁבְתִּֽי׃\rb*? \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I have not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb dwelt|יָשַׁ֙בְתִּי֙\rb* \rb in a house|בְּבַ֔יִת\rb* \rb from the day|לְ֠מִיּוֹם\rb* \rb I brought|הַעֲלֹתִ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites up|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb until|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb but I have|וָאֶֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb moved about|מִתְהַלֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb with a tent|בְּאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb as My dwelling|וּבְמִשְׁכָּֽן׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb In all|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb My journeys|הִתְהַלַּכְתִּי֮\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*, \rb have I ever asked|דִּבַּ֗רְתִּי\rb*\rb |הֲדָבָ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb any|אַחַד֙\rb* \rb of the leaders|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 7:7 \ft Or \fqa tribes\f*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I appointed|צִוִּ֗יתִי\rb* \rb to shepherd|לִרְע֛וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* ‘\rb Why|לָ֛מָּה\rb* \rb haven’t|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb you built|בְנִיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb Me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb a house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of cedar|אֲרָזִֽים׃\rb*?’
\p \v 8 \rb Now|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb* \rb then|כֹּֽה־\rb*, \rb you are to tell|תֹאמַ֞ר\rb* \rb My servant|לְעַבְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb took you|לְקַחְתִּ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the pasture|הַנָּוֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb from following|מֵאַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֑אן\rb*, \rb to be|לִֽהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb the ruler|נָגִ֔יד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb I have been|וָאֶהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֗\rb*\rb |בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb wherever|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have gone|הָלַ֔כְתָּ\rb*, \rb and I have cut off|וָאַכְרִ֥תָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from before you|מִפָּנֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb Now I will make|וְעָשִׂ֤תִֽי\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb like that of|כְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb*\rb |הַגְּדֹלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the greatest|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb And I will provide|וְשַׂמְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb a place|מָ֠קוֹם\rb* \rb for My people|לְעַמִּ֨י\rb* \rb Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb and will plant them|וּנְטַעְתִּיו֙\rb* \rb so that they may dwell in|וְשָׁכַ֣ן\rb* \rb a place of their own|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb* \rb and be disturbed|יִרְגַּ֖ז\rb* \rb no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb more|ע֑וֹד\rb*. \rb No|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|יֹסִ֤יפוּ\rb* \rb will the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of wickedness|עַוְלָה֙\rb* \rb oppress them|לְעַנּוֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb as they did|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb at the beginning|בָּרִאשׁוֹנָֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb and have done since|וּלְמִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I appointed|צִוִּ֤יתִי\rb* \rb judges|שֹֽׁפְטִים֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*. \rb I will give you rest|וַהֲנִיחֹ֥תִי\rb*\rb |לְךָ֖\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֑יךָ\rb*.
\p \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb declares|וְהִגִּ֤יד\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb that He Himself|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb will establish|יַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb a house|בַ֖יִת\rb* \rb for you|לְּךָ֥\rb*. \v 12 \rb And when|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb your days|יָמֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb are fulfilled|יִמְלְא֣וּ\rb* \rb and you rest|וְשָֽׁכַבְתָּ֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb I will raise up|וַהֲקִימֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your descendant|זַרְעֲךָ֙\rb* \rb after you|אַחֲרֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb will come|יֵצֵ֖א\rb* \rb from your own body|מִמֵּעֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb and I will establish|וַהֲכִינֹתִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his kingdom|מַמְלַכְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb He|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb will build|יִבְנֶה־\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִ֑י\rb*, \rb and I will establish|וְכֹנַנְתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb* \rb of his kingdom|מַמְלַכְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will be|אֶהְיֶה־\rb* \rb his|לּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Father|לְאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶה־\rb* \rb My|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb son|לְבֵ֑ן\rb*.\f + \fr 7:14 \ft Cited in Hebrews 1:5\f* \rb When|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb he does wrong|בְּהַ֣עֲוֺת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb I will discipline him|וְהֹֽכַחְתִּיו֙\rb* \rb with the rod|בְּשֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of men|אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and with the blows|וּבְנִגְעֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men|אָדָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb But My loving devotion|וְחַסְדִּ֖י\rb* \rb will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb be removed from him|יָס֣וּר\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I removed|הֲסִרֹ֙תִי֙\rb* \rb it from|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I removed from|הֲסִרֹ֖תִי\rb* \rb before you|מִלְּפָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Your house|בֵּיתְךָ֧\rb* \rb and kingdom|וּמַֽמְלַכְתְּךָ֛\rb* \rb will endure|וְנֶאְמַ֨ן\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Me|עַד־\rb*,\f + \fr 7:16 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts and LXX; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa you\f* \rb and your throne|כִּֽסְאֲךָ֔\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb established|נָכ֖וֹן\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb So|כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb relayed|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽד׃ס\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb entire|וּכְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb revelation|הַחִזָּי֣וֹן\rb*.
\s1 David’s Prayer of Thanksgiving
\p \v 18 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb went in|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb*, \rb sat|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb am I|אָנֹכִ֞י\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֤י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֙\rb*, \rb and what|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb is my house|בֵיתִ֔י\rb*, \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb You have brought me|הֲבִיאֹתַ֖נִי\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb this far|הֲלֹֽם׃\rb*? \v 19 \rb And as if|ע֨וֹד\rb* \rb this|זֹ֤את\rb* \rb was a small thing|וַתִּקְטַן֩\rb* \rb in Your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb You have also|גַּ֥ם\rb* \rb spoken|וַתְּדַבֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb the future|לְמֵֽרָח֑וֹק\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb*. \rb Is this|וְזֹ֛את\rb* \rb Your custom|תּוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb with man|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*?\f + \fr 7:19 \ft Or \fqa And this is Your instruction for mankind, O Lord GOD.\f* \v 20 \rb What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb more|יּוֹסִ֥יף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb can David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb say|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*? \rb For You|וְאַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֥עְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb For the sake|בַּעֲב֤וּר\rb* \rb of Your word|דְּבָֽרְךָ֙\rb* \rb and according to Your own heart|וּֽכְלִבְּךָ֔\rb*, \rb You have accomplished|עָשִׂ֕יתָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb great thing|הַגְּדוּלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and revealed it|לְהוֹדִ֖יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Your servant|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb How|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb great You are|גָּדַ֖לְתָּ\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*! \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb there is none|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb like You|כָּמ֗וֹךָ\rb*, \rb and there is no|וְאֵ֤ין\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb but You|זֽוּלָתֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb according to everything|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb we have heard|שָׁמַ֖עְנוּ\rb* \rb with our own ears|בְּאָזְנֵֽינוּ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And who|וּמִ֤י\rb* \rb is like Your people|כְעַמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb Israel|כְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* — \rb the one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb nation|גּ֥וֹי\rb* \rb on earth|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb God|אֱ֠לֹהִים\rb* \rb went out|הָלְכֽוּ־\rb* \rb to redeem|לִפְדּֽוֹת־\rb* \rb as a people|לְעָ֜ם\rb* \rb for Himself|ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb and to make|וְלָשׂ֧וּם\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֗ם\rb* \rb for Himself|ל֣וֹ\rb*? \rb You performed|וְלַעֲשׂ֨וֹת\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדוּלָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and awesome wonders|וְנֹֽרָאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |לְאַרְצֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb by driving out nations|גּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb and their gods|וֵאלֹהָֽיו׃\rb* \rb from before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֗\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb You redeemed|פָּדִ֤יתָ\rb* \rb for Yourself|לְּךָ֙\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb*.\f + \fr 7:23 \ft See LXX and 1 Chronicles 17:21; Hebrew \fqa You performed for Yourself great and awesome wonders for Your land, before Your people, whom You have redeemed for Yourself from Egypt, from nations and their gods.\f* \v 24 \rb For You have established|וַתְּכ֣וֹנֵֽן\rb*\rb |לְ֠ךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֨\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל׀\rb* \rb as Your very own|לְךָ֛\rb*\rb |לְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and You|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb have become|הָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb And now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb confirm|הָקֵ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb the word|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb You have spoken|דִּבַּ֤רְתָּ\rb* \rb concerning|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and his house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*. \rb Do|וַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You have promised|דִּבַּֽרְתָּ׃\rb*, \v 26 \rb so that Your name|שִׁמְךָ֤\rb* \rb will be magnified|וְיִגְדַּ֨ל\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb when it is said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb is God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.’ \rb And the house|וּבֵית֙\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb established|נָכ֖וֹן\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּה֩\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb have revealed this|גָּלִ֜יתָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֹ֤זֶן\rb* \rb to Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb when You said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb I will build|אֶבְנֶה־\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb for you|לָּ֑ךְ\rb*.’ \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has found|מָצָ֤א\rb* \rb the courage|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb to offer|לְהִתְפַּלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb prayer|הַתְּפִלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb*, \rb You|אַתָּה־\rb* \rb are|הוּא֙\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*! \rb Your words|וּדְבָרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb are|יִהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb true|אֱמֶ֑ת\rb*, \rb and You have promised|וַתְּדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb goodness|הַטּוֹבָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 29 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb may it please You|הוֹאֵל֙\rb* \rb to bless|וּבָרֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb*, \rb that it may continue|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֞ה\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֤י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֙\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּ֔רְתָּ\rb*, \rb and with Your blessing|וּמִבִּרְכָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb will be blessed forever|יְבֹרַ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָֽם׃פ\rb*.”
\c 8
\s1 David’s Triumphs
\p \v 1 \rb Some time later|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb defeated|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb subdued them|וַיַּכְנִיעֵ֑ם\rb*, \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מֶ֥תֶג\rb* \rb Metheg-ammah|הָאַמָּ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 8:1 \fqa Metheg-ammah \ft means \fqa bridle of the mother city\ft .\f* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb David also defeated|וַיַּ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Moabites|מוֹאָ֗ב\rb*, \rb made them lie down|הַשְׁכֵּ֣ב\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֣ם\rb* \rb on the ground|אַ֔רְצָה\rb*, \rb and measured them off|וַֽיְמַדְּדֵ֤ם\rb* \rb with a cord|בַּחֶ֙בֶל֙\rb*. \rb He measured off|וַיְמַדֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb with two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb lengths|חֲבָלִים֙\rb* \rb those to be put to death|לְהָמִ֔ית\rb*, \rb and with one|וּמְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb length|הַחֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb those to be spared|לְהַחֲי֑וֹת\rb*. \rb So the Moabites|מוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb became|וַתְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb subject|לַעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb and brought him|נֹשְׂאֵ֥י\rb* \rb tribute|מִנְחָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb also defeated|וַיַּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעֶ֥זֶר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Rehob|רְחֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Zobah|צוֹבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb who had marched out|בְּלֶכְתּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb to restore|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb his dominion|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb along the Euphrates River|בִּֽנְהַר־׃\rb*.\f + \fr 8:3 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate (see also 1 Chronicles 18:3); Hebrew \fqa along the River\ft , or an alternate reading \fqa along the Euphrates\f* \v 4 \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֨ד\rb* \rb from him|מִמֶּ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb a thousand chariots|אֶ֤לֶף\rb*, \rb seven|וּשְׁבַע־\rb* \rb thousand|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb charioteers|פָּרָשִׁ֔ים\rb*,\f + \fr 8:4 \ft LXX (see also DSS and 1 Chronicles 18:4); MT \fqa captured from him seventeen hundred charioteers\f* \rb and twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb foot soldiers|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |רַגְלִ֑י\rb*, \rb and he|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hamstrung|וַיְעַקֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the horses|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb except a hundred|מֵ֥אָה\rb* \rb he kept|וַיּוֹתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb for the chariots|רָֽכֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When the Arameans|אֲרַ֣ם\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַּמֶּ֔שֶׂק\rb* \rb came|וַתָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to help|לַעְזֹ֕ר\rb* \rb King|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hadadezer|לַהֲדַדְעֶ֖זֶר\rb* \rb of Zobah|צוֹבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb struck down|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִֽים־\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb of their|בַּֽאֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Then he|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb placed|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb* \rb garrisons|נְצִבִים֙\rb* \rb in Aram|בַּאֲרַ֣ם\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַּמֶּ֔שֶׂק\rb*, \rb and the Arameans|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb became|וַתְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb subject|לַעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb and brought him|נוֹשְׂאֵ֣י\rb* \rb tribute|מִנְחָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb victorious|וַיֹּ֤שַׁע\rb* \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he went|הָלָֽךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb And David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb shields|שִׁלְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb belonged|הָי֔וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶ֖ל\rb* \rb the officers|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעָ֑זֶר\rb* \rb and brought them|וַיְבִיאֵ֖ם\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb And from Betah|וּמִבֶּ֥טַח\rb*\f + \fr 8:8 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa Tebah\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 18:8.\f* \rb and Berothai|וּמִבֵּֽרֹתַ֖י\rb*, \rb cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעָ֑זֶר\rb*, \rb King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb took|לָקַ֞ח\rb* \rb a large|מְאֹֽד׃ס\rb* \rb amount|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb When King|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Toi|תֹּ֖עִי\rb*\f + \fr 8:9 \fqa Toi \ft is a variant of \fqa Tou\ft ; also in verse 10; see 1 Chronicles 18:9.\f* \rb of Hamath|חֲמָ֑ת\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֕ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb had defeated|הִכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|חֵ֥יל\rb* \rb of Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעָֽזֶר׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb he|תֹּ֣עִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Joram|יֽוֹרָם־\rb*\f + \fr 8:10 \fqa Joram \ft is a variant of \fqa Hadoram\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 18:10.\f* \rb to greet|לִשְׁאָל־\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb David|דָּ֠וִד\rb*\rb |ל֨וֹ\rb*\rb |לְשָׁל֜וֹם\rb* \rb and bless him|וּֽלְבָרֲכ֗וֹ\rb* \rb for|עַל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb fighting|נִלְחַ֤ם\rb* \rb and defeating|וַיַּכֵּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb Hadadezer|בַּהֲדַדְעֶ֙זֶר֙\rb*, \rb who|כִּי־\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |הֲדַדְעָ֑זֶר\rb* \rb had been|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb at war|מִלְחֲמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb with Toi|תֹּ֖עִי\rb*. \rb Joram brought|הָי֛וּ\rb* \rb with him|וּבְיָד֗וֹ\rb* \rb articles|כְּלֵֽי־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶ֥סֶף\rb* \rb and|וּכְלֵֽי־\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb and|וּכְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb dedicated|הִקְדִּ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb these|אֹתָ֕ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb along with|עִם־\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְהַזָּהָב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had dedicated|הִקְדִּ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had subdued|כִּבֵּֽשׁ׃\rb*— \v 12 \rb from Edom|מֵאֲרָ֤ם\rb*\f + \fr 8:12 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Syriac (see also verse 14 and 1 Chronicles 18:11); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Aram\f* \rb and Moab|וּמִמּוֹאָב֙\rb*, \rb from the Ammonites|וּמִבְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and Philistines|וּמִפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and Amalekites|וּמֵֽעֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb*, \rb and from the spoil|וּמִשְּׁלַ֛ל\rb* \rb of Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעֶ֥זֶר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Rehob|רְחֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Zobah|צוֹבָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a name for himself|שֵׁ֔ם\rb* \rb when he returned|בְּשֻׁב֕וֹ\rb* \rb from striking down|מֵהַכּוֹת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb eighteen|שְׁמוֹנָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb thousand|אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb Edomites|אֲרָ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 8:13 \ft A few Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Syriac (see also verse 14 and 1 Chronicles 18:12); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Arameans\f* \rb in the Valley of Salt|בְּגֵיא־\rb*.\rb |מֶ֑לַח\rb* \v 14 \rb He placed|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb* \rb garrisons|נְצִבִ֗ים\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb Edom|בֶּאֱד֜וֹם\rb*, \rb and all|כָל־\rb*\rb |אֱד֖וֹם\rb* \rb the Edomites|אֱדוֹם֙\rb*\rb |שָׂ֣ם\rb*\rb |נְצִבִ֔ים\rb* \rb were|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb subject|עֲבָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֑ד\rb*. \rb So the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb victorious|וַיּ֤וֹשַׁע\rb* \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he went|הָלָֽךְ׃\rb*.
\s1 David’s Officers
\p \v 15 \rb Thus David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb*\rb |דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb and administered|עֹשֶׂ֛ה\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb* \rb and righteousness|וּצְדָקָ֖ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his people|עַמּֽוֹ׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 16 \rb Joab|וְיוֹאָ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֖ה\rb* \rb was over|עַל־\rb* \rb the army|הַצָּבָ֑א\rb*;
\li1 \rb Jehoshaphat|וִיהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahilud|אֲחִיל֖וּד\rb* \rb was the recorder|מַזְכִּֽיר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 17 \rb Zadok|וְצָד֧וֹק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahitub|אֲחִיט֛וּב\rb* \rb and Ahimelech|וַאֲחִימֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֖ר\rb* \rb were priests|כֹּהֲנִ֑ים\rb*;
\li1 \rb Seraiah|וּשְׂרָיָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 8:17 \fqa Seraiah \ft is also called \fqa Sheva\ft , \fqa Shisha\ft , and \fqa Shavsha\ft ; see 2 Samuel 20:25, 1 Kings 4:3, and 1 Chronicles 18:16.\f* \rb was the scribe|סוֹפֵֽר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 18 \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada was over|יְה֣וֹיָדָ֔ע\rb* \rb the Cherethites|וְהַכְּרֵתִ֖י\rb* \rb and Pelethites|וְהַפְּלֵתִ֑י\rb*;
\li1 \rb and David’s|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb were|הָיֽוּ׃פ\rb* \rb priestly leaders|כֹּהֲנִ֥ים\rb*.\f + \fr 8:18 \ft Literally \fqa priests\ft , or possibly \fqa chief officials\ft ; see LXX, Targum Yonaton, and 1 Chronicles 18:17.\f*
\c 9
\s1 David and Mephibosheth
\p \v 1 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |הֲכִ֣י\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is there|יֶשׁ־\rb*\rb |ע֔וֹד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb anyone left|נוֹתַ֖ר\rb* \rb from the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb to whom|עִמּוֹ֙\rb* \rb I can show|וְאֶעֱשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֔סֶד\rb* \rb for the sake|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָֽן׃\rb*?”
\p \v 2 \rb And there was a servant|עֶ֙בֶד֙\rb* \rb of the house|וּלְבֵ֨ית\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֥וּל\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Ziba|צִיבָ֔א\rb*. \rb They summoned|וַיִּקְרְאוּ־\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb and the king|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb inquired|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֛יו\rb*, “\rb Are you|הַאַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Ziba|צִיבָ֖א\rb*?”
\p “\rb I am your servant|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הַאֶ֨פֶס\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is there anyone|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb left|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb of the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb to whom|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb I can show|וְאֶעֱשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb the kindness|חֶ֣סֶד\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*?”
\p \rb Ziba|צִיבָא֙\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb There is still|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb Jonathan’s|לִיהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֥ן\rb*, \rb who is lame|נְכֵ֥ה\rb* \rb in both feet|רַגְלָֽיִם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 “\rb Where|אֵיפֹ֣ה\rb* \rb is he|ה֑וּא\rb*?” \rb replied|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |ל֥וֹ\rb*.
\p \rb And Ziba|צִיבָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Indeed|הִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb he is|ה֗וּא\rb*\rb |בְּל֥וֹ\rb* \rb in Lo-debar|דְבָֽר׃\rb* \rb at the house|בֵּ֛ית\rb* \rb of Machir|מָכִ֥יר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ammiel|עַמִּיאֵ֖ל\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb |וַיִּשְׁלַ֖ח\rb* \rb So King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb had him brought|וַיִּקָּחֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֛ית\rb* \rb of Machir|מָכִ֥יר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ammiel|עַמִּיאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |מִלּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb in Lo-debar|דְבָֽר׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb And when Mephibosheth|מְפִיבֹ֨שֶׁת\rb*\f + \fr 9:6 \fqa Mephibosheth \ft is also called \fqa Merib-baal\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 8:34.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֤ן\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*, \rb came|וַ֠יָּבֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, \rb he fell facedown|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb in reverence|וַיִּשְׁתָּ֑חוּ\rb*.
\p \rb Then David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Mephibosheth|מְפִיבֹ֔שֶׁת\rb*!”
\p “\rb I am your servant|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.\rb |הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 7 “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֗א\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֜ד\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb surely I will show|עָשֹׂה֩\rb*\rb |אֶעֱשֶׂ֨ה\rb* \rb you|עִמְּךָ֥\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֙סֶד֙\rb* \rb for the sake|בַּֽעֲבוּר֙\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb*. \rb I will restore|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֣י\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|שְׂדֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of your grandfather|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb*, \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb will always|תָּמִֽיד׃\rb* \rb eat|תֹּ֥אכַל\rb*\rb |לֶ֛חֶם\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb my table|שֻׁלְחָנִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Mephibosheth bowed down|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֕חוּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb is your servant|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you should show regard|פָנִ֔יתָ\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb a dead|הַמֵּ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb dog|הַכֶּ֥לֶב\rb* \rb like me|כָּמֽוֹנִי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 9 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb servant|נַ֥עַר\rb* \rb Ziba|צִיבָ֛א\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb to him|אֶל־\rb*, “\rb I have given|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb to your master’s|אֲדֹנֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb grandson|לְבֶן־\rb* \rb all|כֹּל֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb belonged to|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb Saul|לְשָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb and to all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*. \v 10 \rb You|אַתָּה֩\rb* \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb and servants|וַעֲבָדֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb are to work|וְעָבַ֣דְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאֲדָמָ֡ה\rb* \rb for him|לּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb and bring in the harvest|וְהֵבֵ֗אתָ\rb*, \rb so that your master’s|אֲדֹנֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb grandson|לְבֶן־\rb* \rb may have|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb food|לֶּ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb to eat|וַאֲכָל֔וֹ\rb*. \rb But Mephibosheth|וּמְפִיבֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb*, \rb your master’s|אֲדֹנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb grandson|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb is always|תָּמִ֛יד\rb*\rb |לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb to eat|יֹאכַ֥ל\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb my table|שֻׁלְחָנִ֑י\rb*.”
\p \rb Now Ziba|וּלְצִיבָ֗א\rb* \rb had fifteen|חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֛ר\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb servants|עֲבָדִֽים׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And Ziba|צִיבָא֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Your servant|עַבְדּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹל֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֤י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has commanded|יְצַוֶּ֜ה\rb*.”
\p \rb So Mephibosheth|וּמְפִיבֹ֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb ate|אֹכֵל֙\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb David’s table|שֻׁלְחָנִ֔י\rb*\f + \fr 9:11 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa my table\f* \rb like one|כְּאַחַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb own sons|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb*. \v 12 \rb And Mephibosheth|וְלִמְפִיבֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb had a young|קָטָ֖ן\rb* \rb son|בֵּן־\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Mica|מִיכָ֑א\rb*,\f + \fr 9:12 \fqa Mica \ft is a variant of \fqa Micah\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 8:34.\f* \rb and all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb who dwelt|מוֹשַׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Ziba|צִיבָ֔א\rb* \rb were servants|עֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb of Mephibosheth|לִמְפִיבֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb So Mephibosheth|וּמְפִיבֹ֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb lived|יֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb always|תָּמִ֖יד\rb* \rb ate|אֹכֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb table|שֻׁלְחַ֥ן\rb*, \rb and he was lame|פִסֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb in both|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb feet|רַגְלָֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 David’s Messengers Disgraced
\p \v 1 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb Some time later|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*,\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֕מָת\rb* \rb and was succeeded by|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Hanun|חָנ֥וּן\rb*. \v 2 \rb And David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will show|אֶעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֣סֶד׀\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb Hanun|חָנ֣וּן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nahash|נָחָ֗שׁ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֤יו\rb* \rb showed|עָשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֔סֶד\rb* \rb to me|עִמָּדִי֙\rb*.”
\p \rb So David|דָּוִ֧ד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb some of his servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb to console Hanun|לְנַחֲמ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּיַד־\rb* \rb concerning|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb*. \rb But when they|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb*\rb |דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb in the land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb the princes|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֜וֹן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hanun|חָנ֣וּן\rb* \rb their lord|אֲדֹֽנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*, “\rb Just because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb David has sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb comforters|מְנַֽחֲמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb do you really believe|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb he is|דָּוִ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb showing respect|הַֽמְכַבֵּ֨ד\rb* \rb for your father|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb*? \rb Has not|הֲ֠לוֹא\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb instead sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*\rb |בַּעֲב֞וּר\rb* \rb to explore|חֲק֤וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb*, \rb spy it out|וּלְרַגְּלָ֣הּ\rb*, \rb and overthrow it|וּלְהָפְכָ֔הּ\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb So Hanun|חָנ֜וּן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb*, \rb shaved off|וַיְגַלַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֣י\rb* \rb of each man’s beard|זְקָנָ֔ם\rb*, \rb cut off|וַיִּכְרֹ֧ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their garments|מַדְוֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |בַּחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb at|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb the hips|שְׁתֽוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and sent them away|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֵֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When this was reported|וַיַּגִּ֤דוּ\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִד֙\rb*, \rb he sent messengers|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb to meet the men|לִקְרָאתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they had been|הָי֥וּ\rb*\rb |הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb thoroughly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb humiliated|נִכְלָמִ֣ים\rb*. \rb The king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb told them|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Stay|שְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb in Jericho|בִֽירֵח֔וֹ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb your beards|זְקַנְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb have grown back|יְצַמַּ֥ח\rb*, \rb and then return|וְשַׁבְתֶּֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb When the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb realized that|וַיִּרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb they had become a stench|נִבְאֲשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb to David|בְּדָוִ֑ד\rb*,\rb |וַיִּשְׁלְח֣וּ\rb* \rb they|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֡וֹן\rb* \rb hired|וַיִּשְׂכְּרוּ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb Aramean|אֲרַ֨ם\rb* \rb foot soldiers|רַגְלִ֔י\rb*\rb |בֵּית־\rb* \rb from Beth-rehob|רְח֜וֹב\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲרַ֣ם\rb* \rb Zoba|צוֹבָ֗א\rb*, \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֣לֶף\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb from the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Maacah|מַֽעֲכָה֙\rb* \rb and twelve|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb thousand|אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb men|וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb from Tob|ט֔וֹב\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb On hearing this|וַיִּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|הַצָּבָ֖א\rb* \rb of mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb The Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb marched out|וַיֵּֽצְאוּ֙\rb* \rb and arrayed themselves|וַיַּעַרְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb for battle|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the city gate|הַשָּׁ֑עַר\rb*, \rb while the Arameans|וַאֲרַ֨ם\rb* \rb of Zobah|צוֹבָ֤א\rb* \rb and Rehob|וּרְחוֹב֙\rb* \rb and the men|וְאִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Tob|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb and Maacah|וּמַֽעֲכָ֔ה\rb* \rb were by themselves|לְבַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb in the open country|בַּשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 David Defeats Ammon and Aram
\p \v 9 \rb When Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |הָיְתָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb the battle lines|הַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb before him|מִפָּנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and behind him|וּמֵֽאָח֑וֹר\rb*, \rb he selected|וַיִּבְחַ֗ר\rb* \rb some of|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the best|בְּחוּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb men of Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל\rb* \rb and arrayed them|וַֽיַּעֲרֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb against|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb And|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb he placed|נָתַ֕ן\rb* \rb the rest|יֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb under the command|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of his brother|אָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb Abishai|אַבְשַׁ֣י\rb*, \rb who arrayed them|וַֽיַּעֲרֹ֕ךְ\rb* \rb against|לִקְרַ֖את\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb are too strong|תֶּחֱזַ֤ק\rb* \rb for me|מִמֶּ֔נִּי\rb*,” \rb said Joab|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb then you will come|וְהָיִ֥תָה\rb* \rb to my rescue|לִֽישׁוּעָ֑ה\rb*\rb |לִּ֖י\rb*. \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |עַמּוֹן֙\rb* \rb are too strong|יֶחֱזְק֣וּ\rb* \rb for you|מִמְּךָ֔\rb*, \rb then I will come|וְהָלַכְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to your rescue|לְהוֹשִׁ֥יעַֽ\rb*\rb |לָֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Be strong|חֲזַ֤ק\rb* \rb and let us fight bravely|וְנִתְחַזַּק֙\rb* \rb for|בְּעַד־\rb* \rb our people|עַמֵּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and for|וּבְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb May the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb do|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb what is good|הַטּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb in His sight|בְּעֵינָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb So Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb and his troops|וְהָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb advanced|וַיִּגַּ֣שׁ\rb* \rb to fight|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb the Arameans|בַּֽאֲרָ֑ם\rb*, \rb who fled|וַיָּנֻ֖סוּ\rb* \rb before him|מִפָּנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb When the Ammonites|וּבְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֤וֹן\rb* \rb saw|רָאוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb had fled|נָ֣ס\rb*, \rb they too fled|וַיָּנֻ֙סוּ֙\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֔י\rb*, \rb and they entered|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*. \rb So Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb from fighting against|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb When the Arameans|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they had been defeated|נִגַּ֖ף\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb they regrouped|וַיֵּאָסְפ֖וּ\rb*\rb |יָֽחַד׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעֶ֗זֶר\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb messengers to bring|וַיֹּצֵ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb more Arameans|אֲרָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb from beyond|מֵעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֔ר\rb*,\f + \fr 10:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\f* \rb and they came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Helam|חֵילָ֑ם\rb* \rb with Shobach|וְשׁוֹבַ֛ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 10:16 \fqa Shobach \ft is a variant of \fqa Shophach\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 19:16.\f* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of Hadadezer’s|הֲדַדְעֶ֖זֶר\rb* \rb army|צְבָ֥א\rb* \rb leading them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb When this was reported|וַיֻּגַּ֣ד\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֗דס\rb*, \rb he gathered|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֤ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb crossed|וַיַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to Helam|חֵלָ֑אמָה\rb*. \rb Then the Arameans|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb arrayed themselves|וַיַּעַרְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb against|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb But the Arameans|אֲרָם֮\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּ֣נָס\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*, \rb and David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb*\rb |מֵאֲרָ֗ם\rb* \rb killed|וַיַּהֲרֹ֨ג\rb* \rb seven|שְׁבַ֤ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb charioteers|רֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb foot soldiers|פָּרָשִׁ֑ים\rb*.\f + \fr 10:18 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also 1 Chronicles 19:18); Hebrew \fqa horsemen\f*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb He also struck down|הִכָּ֖ה\rb* \rb Shobach|שׁוֹבַ֧ךְ\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of their army|צְבָא֛וֹ\rb*, \rb who died|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb When all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb the kings who were|הַמְּלָכִ֜ים\rb* \rb subject|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb to Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעֶ֗זֶר\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֨וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they had been defeated|נִגְּפוּ֙\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb they made peace|וַיַּשְׁלִ֥מוּ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and became subject to them|וַיַּֽעַבְד֑וּם\rb*. \rb So the Arameans|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb were afraid|וַיִּֽרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb to help|לְהוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃פ\rb* \rb anymore|ע֖וֹד\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\c 11
\s1 David and Bathsheba
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb In the spring|לִתְשׁוּבַ֨ת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנָ֜ה\rb*,\f + \fr 11:1 \ft Literally \fqa At the turn of the year\f* \rb at the time when|לְעֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb kings|הַמַּלְאֿכִ֗ים\rb* \rb march out to war|צֵ֣את\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֡ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָב֩\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֨יו\rb*\rb |עִמּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the whole army|כָּל־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*. \rb They destroyed|וַיַּשְׁחִ֙תוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and besieged|וַיָּצֻ֖רוּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Rabbah|רַבָּ֑ה\rb*, \rb but David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb remained|יוֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |לְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb One evening|הָעֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb his bed|מִשְׁכָּבוֹ֙\rb* \rb and strolled around|וַיִּתְהַלֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the roof|גַּ֣ג\rb* \rb of the palace|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*. \rb And from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the roof|הַגָּ֑ג\rb* \rb he saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb a woman|אִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb bathing|רֹחֶ֖צֶת\rb*— \rb a very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb beautiful|טוֹבַ֥ת\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb woman|וְהָ֣אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*. \v 3 \rb So David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb and inquired|וַיִּדְרֹ֖שׁ\rb* \rb about the woman|לָֽאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb and he was told|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*,\rb |הֲלוֹא־\rb* “\rb This|זֹאת֙\rb*\rb |בַּת־\rb* \rb is Bathsheba|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Eliam|אֱלִיעָ֔ם\rb*\f + \fr 11:3 \fqa Eliam \ft is a variant of \fqa Ammiel\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 3:5.\f* \rb and the wife|אֵ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb of Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֜ים\rb* \rb to get her|וַיִּקָּחֶ֗הָ\rb*, \rb and when she came|וַתָּב֤וֹא\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, \rb he slept|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb with her|עִמָּ֔הּ\rb*. (\rb Now she|וְהִ֥יא\rb* \rb had just purified herself|מִתְקַדֶּ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb from her uncleanness|מִטֻּמְאָתָ֑הּ\rb*.) \rb Then she returned|וַתָּ֖שָׁב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb home|בֵּיתָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb conceived|וַתַּ֖הַר\rb* \rb and sent word|וַתִּשְׁלַח֙\rb*\rb |וַתַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb*, \rb saying|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb* \rb am pregnant|הָרָ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb At this, David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb sent orders|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*: “\rb Send|שְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Uriah|אֽוּרִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּ֑י\rb*.” \rb So Joab|יוֹאָ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb him|אֽוּרִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb When Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*\rb |לִשְׁל֤וֹם\rb* \rb asked|וַיִּשְׁאַ֣ל\rb* \rb how Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb and the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb were doing|וְלִשְׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb and how the war|הַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb* \rb was going|וְלִשְׁל֖וֹם\rb*. \v 8 \rb Then he|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Uriah|לְא֣וּרִיָּ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Go down|רֵ֥ד\rb* \rb to your house|לְבֵיתְךָ֖\rb* \rb and wash|וּרְחַ֣ץ\rb* \rb your feet|רַגְלֶ֑יךָ\rb*.”
\p \rb So Uriah|אֽוּרִיָּה֙\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb the palace|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and a gift|מַשְׂאַ֥ת\rb* \rb from the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb followed|וַתֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb him|אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb*. \v 9 \rb But Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֗ה\rb* \rb slept|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb at the door|פֶּ֚תַח\rb* \rb of the palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb with|אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his master’s|אֲדֹנָ֑יו\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb*; \rb he did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb go down|יָרַ֖ד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb And David|לְדָוִד֙\rb* \rb was told|וַיַּגִּ֤דוּ\rb*, “\rb Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|יָרַ֥ד\rb* \rb home|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*.”
\p “\rb Haven’t you|הֲל֤וֹא\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb just arrived|בָ֔א\rb* \rb from a journey|מִדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*?” \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֗ה\rb*. “\rb Why|מַדּ֖וּעַ\rb* \rb didn’t you|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|יָרַ֥דְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb home|בֵּיתֶֽךָ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 11 \rb Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֜ה\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֗ד\rb*, “\rb The ark|הָ֠אָרוֹן\rb* \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb are dwelling|יֹשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb in tents|בַּסֻּכּ֗וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 11:11 \ft Or \fqa staying at Sukkoth\f* \rb and my master|וַאדֹנִ֨י\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֜ב\rb* \rb and his|אֲדֹנִ֨י\rb* \rb soldiers|וְעַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb are camped|חֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the open field|פְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb*. \rb How can I|וַאֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb go|אָב֧וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my house|בֵּיתִ֛י\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb and drink|וְלִשְׁתּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and sleep|וְלִשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb my wife|אִשְׁתִּ֑י\rb*? \rb As surely as you live|חַיֶּ֙ךָ֙\rb*, \rb and as your soul|נַפְשֶׁ֔ךָ\rb* \rb lives|וְחֵ֣י\rb*, \rb I will not|אִֽם־\rb* \rb do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb such a thing|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*!”
\p \v 12 “\rb Stay|שֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb here|בָּזֶ֛ה\rb* \rb one more day|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*,” \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֗ה\rb*, “\rb and tomorrow|וּמָחָ֣ר\rb* \rb I will send you back|אֲשַׁלְּחֶ֑ךָּ\rb*.” \rb So Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֧ה\rb* \rb stayed|וַיֵּ֨שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb and the next|וּמִֽמָּחֳרָֽת׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then David|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb invited|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb Uriah|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb to eat|וַיֹּ֧אכַל\rb* \rb and drink|וַיֵּ֖שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb with him|לְפָנָ֛יו\rb*, \rb and he got Uriah drunk|וַֽיְשַׁכְּרֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb And in the evening|בָעֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb Uriah went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to lie down|לִשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb on his cot|בְּמִשְׁכָּבוֹ֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his master’s|אֲדֹנָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb*, \rb but he did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go|יָרָֽד׃\rb* \rb home|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb*.
\s1 David Arranges Uriah’s Death
\p \v 14 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb The next morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb wrote|וַיִּכְתֹּ֥ב\rb* \rb a letter|סֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \rb and sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֖ח\rb*\rb |בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb it with Uriah|אוּרִיָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb In the letter|בַּסֵּ֖פֶר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb he wrote|וַיִּכְתֹּ֥ב\rb*: “\rb Put|הָב֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Uriah|אֽוּרִיָּ֗ה\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front|מוּל֙\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the fiercest|הַֽחֲזָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb battle|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb*; \rb then withdraw|וְשַׁבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb from him|מֵאַחֲרָ֖יו\rb*, \rb so that he may be struck down|וְנִכָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and killed|וָמֵֽת׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So as|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb besieged|בִּשְׁמ֥וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb he assigned|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Uriah|א֣וּרִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he knew|יָדַ֔ע\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the strongest enemy soldiers were|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb*\rb |חַ֖יִל\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And when the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb came out|וַיֵּ֨צְא֜וּ\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּחֲמ֣וּ\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִ֑ד\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb servants|מֵעַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb*, \rb and Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּֽי׃\rb* \rb also|גַּ֖ם\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֕מָת\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֖ח\rb*\rb |וַיַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a full account|כָּל־\rb*\rb |דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb* \v 19 \rb and instructed|וַיְצַ֥ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the messenger|הַמַּלְאָ֖ךְ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb When you have finished|כְּכַלּוֹתְךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb giving|לְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb a full|כָּל־\rb* \rb account|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*, \v 20 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb if|אִֽם־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb anger|חֲמַ֣ת\rb* \rb flares|תַּעֲלֶה֙\rb*, \rb he may ask|וְאָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb*, ‘\rb Why|מַדּ֛וּעַ\rb* \rb did you get so close|נִגַּשְׁתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֑ם\rb*? \rb Did you not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb realize|יְדַעְתֶּ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they would shoot|יֹר֖וּ\rb* \rb from atop|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the wall|הַחוֹמָֽה׃\rb*? \v 21 \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb struck|הִכָּ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jerubbesheth|יְרֻבֶּ֗שֶׁת\rb*\f + \fr 11:21 \fqa Jerubbesheth \ft is also known as \fqa Jerubbaal\ft , that is, Gideon.\f*? \rb Was it not|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb a woman|אִשָּׁ֡ה\rb* \rb who dropped|הִשְׁלִ֣יכָה\rb* \rb an upper millstone|פֶּ֨לַח\rb*\rb |רֶ֜כֶב\rb* \rb on him|עָלָיו֩\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb the wall|הַֽחוֹמָה֙\rb*, \rb so that he died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb in Thebez|בְּתֵבֵ֔ץ\rb*? \rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb did you get so close|נִגַּשְׁתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wall|הַֽחוֹמָ֑ה\rb*?’
\p \rb If he asks you this, then you are to say|וְאָ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb*, ‘\rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֛\rb* \rb Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb is dead|מֵֽת׃\rb* \rb as well|גַּ֗ם\rb*.’”
\p \v 22 \rb So the messenger|הַמַּלְאָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb set out|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb and reported|וַיַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָֽב׃\rb* \rb had sent him to say|שְׁלָח֖וֹ\rb*. \v 23 \rb The messenger|הַמַּלְאָךְ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*,\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* “\rb The men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb overpowered us|גָבְר֤וּ\rb*\rb |עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and came out|וַיֵּצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb against us|אֵלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb in the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb but we drove them back|וַנִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb* \rb of the gate|הַשָּֽׁעַר׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb Then the archers|וַיֹּרְאוּ\rb* \rb shot|הַמּוֹרְאִים\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֙ךָ֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the wall|הַחוֹמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and some of the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb servants|מֵעַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb were killed|וַיָּמ֖וּתוּ\rb*. \rb And your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֛\rb* \rb Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb is dead|מֵֽת׃ס\rb* \rb as well|וְגַ֗ם\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the messenger|הַמַּלְאָ֗ךְ\rb*, “\rb Say|תֹאמַ֤ר\rb* \rb this|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb*: ‘\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb matter|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb upset|יֵרַ֤ע\rb* \rb you|בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the sword|הֶחָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb devours|תֹּאכַ֣ל\rb* \rb one|וְכָזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb as well as another|כָזֹ֥ה\rb*. \rb Strengthen|הַחֲזֵ֨ק\rb* \rb your attack|מִלְחַמְתְּךָ֧\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֛יר\rb* \rb and demolish it|וְהָרְסָ֖הּ\rb*.’ \rb Encourage him with these words|וְחַזְּקֵֽהוּ׃\rb*.”
\s1 David Marries Bathsheba
\p \v 26 \rb When Uriah’s|אֽוּרִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb heard|וַתִּשְׁמַע֙\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb her husband|אִישָׁ֑הּ\rb*\rb |אוּרִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֖ת\rb*, \rb she mourned|וַתִּסְפֹּ֖ד\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb him|בַּעְלָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb And when the time of mourning|הָאֵ֗בֶל\rb*\rb |וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb was over|וַיַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb had her brought|וַיַּאַסְפָ֤הּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּיתוֹ֙\rb*, \rb and she became|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb wife|לְאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb and bore|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֑ן\rb*.
\p \rb But the thing|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb was evil|וַיֵּ֧רַע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 12
\s1 Nathan Rebukes David
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֧ח\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb and when he arrived|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb There were|הָיוּ֙\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb in a certain|אֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb city|בְּעִ֣יר\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb rich|עָשִׁ֖יר\rb* \rb and the other|וְאֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb poor|רָֽאשׁ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb The rich|לְעָשִׁ֗יר\rb* \rb man had|הָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb a great number of|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֥אן\rb* \rb and cattle|וּבָקָ֖ר\rb*, \v 3 \rb but the poor|וְלָרָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb man had nothing|אֵֽין־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֗ל\rb* \rb except|כִּי֩\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֤ת\rb* \rb small|קְטַנָּה֙\rb* \rb ewe lamb|כִּבְשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had bought|קָנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb He raised it|וַיְחַיֶּ֕הָ\rb*, \rb and it grew up|וַתִּגְדַּ֥ל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |וְעִם־\rb* \rb and his children|בָּנָ֖יו\rb*. \rb It shared|יַחְדָּ֑ו\rb*\rb |תֹאכַ֜ל\rb* \rb his food|מִפִּתּ֨וֹ\rb* \rb and drank|תִשְׁתֶּה֙\rb* \rb from his cup|וּמִכֹּס֤וֹ\rb*; \rb it slept|תִשְׁכָּ֔ב\rb* \rb in his arms|וּבְחֵיק֣וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 12:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa in his bosom\ft ; also in verse 8\f* \rb and was|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb like a daughter|כְּבַֽת׃\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Now a traveler|הֵלֶךְ֮\rb* \rb came|וַיָּ֣בֹא\rb* \rb to the rich|הֶֽעָשִׁיר֒\rb*\rb |וַיַּחְמֹ֗ל\rb* \rb man|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb*, \rb who refrained from taking|לָקַ֤חַת\rb* \rb one of his own sheep|מִצֹּאנוֹ֙\rb* \rb or cattle|וּמִבְּקָר֔וֹ\rb* \rb to prepare|לַעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb* \rb for the traveler|לָאֹרֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb who had come|הַבָּא־\rb* \rb to him|ל֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Instead, he took|וַיִּקַּ֗ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poor|הָרָ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb man’s|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb lamb|כִּבְשַׂת֙\rb* \rb and prepared it|וַֽיַּעֲשֶׂ֔הָ\rb* \rb for his guest|לָאִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |הַבָּ֥א\rb*\rb |אֵלָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb with anger|אַ֥ף\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb against the man|בָּאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֔ן\rb*: “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֕ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb the man|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb who did|הָעֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb this|זֹֽאת׃\rb* \rb deserves to die|מָ֔וֶת\rb*! \v 6 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Because|עֵ֗קֶב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb he has done|עָשָׂה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb thing|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb and has shown no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb pity|חָמָֽל׃\rb*, \rb he must pay|יְשַׁלֵּ֣ם\rb* \rb for the lamb|הַכִּבְשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb four times over|אַרְבַּעְתָּ֑יִם\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Then Nathan|נָתָ֛ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are that man|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb*! \rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֨ר\rb*: ‘\rb I|אָנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb anointed|מְשַׁחְתִּ֤יךָֽ\rb* \rb you king|לְמֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and I|וְאָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb delivered you|הִצַּלְתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb I gave|וָאֶתְּנָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your master’s|אֲדֹנֶ֗יךָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb house to you|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and your master’s|אֲדֹנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb wives|נְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb into your arms|בְּחֵיקֶ֔ךָ\rb*. \rb I gave|וָאֶתְּנָ֣ה\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and if|וְאִ֨ם־\rb* \rb that was not enough|מְעָ֔ט\rb*, \rb I would have given|וְאֹסִ֥פָה\rb* \rb you|לְּךָ֖\rb* \rb even more|כָּהֵ֥נָּה\rb*\rb |וְכָהֵֽנָּה׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Why|מַדּ֜וּעַ\rb* \rb then have you despised|בָּזִ֣יתָ׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the command|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb by doing|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb evil|הָרַע֮\rb* \rb in His sight|בְּעֵינוֹ\rb*?\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb You put|הִכִּ֣יתָ\rb* \rb Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַֽחִתִּי֙\rb* \rb to the sword|בַחֶ֔רֶב\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb and took|לָקַ֥חְתָּ\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb as your own|לְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*.\rb |וְאֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb You have slain him|הָרַ֔גְתָּ\rb* \rb with the sword|בְּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Now, therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb the sword|חֶ֛רֶב\rb* \rb will never|לֹא־\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb depart|תָס֥וּר\rb* \rb from your house|מִבֵּיתְךָ֖\rb*, \rb because|עֵ֚קֶב\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have despised Me|בְזִתָ֔נִי\rb* \rb and have taken|וַתִּקַּ֗ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wife|אֵ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb of Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּ֔י\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb own|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 11 \rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִי֩\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb I will raise up|מֵקִ֨ים\rb* \rb adversity|רָעָה֙\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb from your own house|מִבֵּיתֶ֔ךָ\rb*. \rb Before your very eyes|לְעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb I will take|וְלָקַחְתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your wives|נָשֶׁ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and give them|וְנָתַתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to another|לְרֵעֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb and he will lie|וְשָׁכַב֙\rb* \rb with them|עִם־\rb* \rb in broad daylight|נָשֶׁ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁ֥מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb have acted|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb in secret|בַסָּ֑תֶר\rb*, \rb but I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb will do|אֶעֱשֶׂה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb this thing|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְנֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb in broad daylight|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb before|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.’”
\s1 David’s Loss and Repentance
\p \v 13 \rb Then David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֔ן\rb*, “\rb I have sinned|חָטָ֖אתִי\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑הס\rb*.”
\p “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has taken away|הֶעֱבִ֥יר\rb* \rb your sin|חַטָּאתְךָ֖\rb*,” \rb Nathan|נָתָ֜ן\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֗ד\rb*.\rb |גַּם־\rb* “\rb You will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|תָמֽוּת׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Nevertheless|אֶ֗פֶס\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb by|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |גַּ֗ם\rb* \rb this deed|בַּדָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |נִאַ֙צְתָּ֙\rb* \rb you have shown utter contempt|נִאֵ֤ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the word|אֹיְבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,\f + \fr 12:14 \ft DSS; MT \fqa you have brought utter contempt from the enemies of the LORD\f* \rb the son|הַבֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb born|הַיִּלּ֥וֹד\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb will surely die|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יָמֽוּת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb After Nathan|נָתָ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb had gone|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb home|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb struck|וַיִּגֹּ֣ף\rb* \rb the child|הַיֶּ֜לֶד\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Uriah’s|אוּרִיָּ֛ה\rb* \rb wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb had borne|יָלְדָ֧ה\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb*, \rb and he became ill|וַיֵּאָנַֽשׁ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb pleaded|וַיְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb with God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb for|בְּעַ֣ד\rb* \rb the boy|הַנָּ֑עַר\rb*. \rb He|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb fasted|וַיָּ֤צָם\rb*\rb |צ֔וֹם\rb* \rb and went into his house|וּבָ֥א\rb* \rb and spent the night|וְלָ֖ן\rb* \rb lying in sackcloth|וְשָׁכַ֥ב\rb*\f + \fr 12:16 \ft DSS and LXX; MT does not include \fqa in sackcloth\ft .\f* \rb on the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb The elders|זִקְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of his household|בֵיתוֹ֙\rb* \rb stood|וַיָּקֻ֜מוּ\rb* \rb beside him|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb to help him up|לַהֲקִימ֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb but he was unwilling|וְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אָבָ֔ה\rb* \rb and would not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb eat|בָרָ֥א\rb* \rb anything with them|אִתָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |לָֽחֶם׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the child|הַיָּ֑לֶד\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb*. \rb But David’s|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb were afraid|וַיִּֽרְאוּ֩\rb* \rb to tell|לְהַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the child|הַיֶּ֗לֶד\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they said|אָֽמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּה֩\rb*,\rb |בִהְי֨וֹת\rb* \rb while the child|הַיֶּ֜לֶד\rb* \rb was alive|חַ֗י\rb*, \rb we spoke|דִּבַּ֤רְנוּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, \rb and he would not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb listen to us|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb*.\rb |בְּקוֹלֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb So how|וְאֵ֨יךְ\rb* \rb can we tell|נֹאמַ֥ר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֛יו\rb* \rb the child|הַיֶּ֖לֶד\rb* \rb is dead|מֵ֥ת\rb*? \rb He may even harm himself|וְעָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |רָעָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb When David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb were whispering to one another|מִֽתְלַחֲשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb he|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb perceived|וַיָּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the child|הַיָּ֑לֶד\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֣ת\rb*. \rb So he|דָּוִ֧ד\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֛יו\rb*, “\rb Is the child|הַיֶּ֖לֶד\rb* \rb dead|הֲמֵ֥ת\rb*?”
\p “\rb He is dead|מֵֽת׃\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּ֥אמְרוּ\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּקָם֩\rb* \rb from the ground|מֵהָאָ֜רֶץ\rb*, \rb washed|וַיִּרְחַ֣ץ\rb* \rb and anointed himself|וַיָּ֗סֶךְ\rb*, \rb changed|וַיְחַלֵּף֙\rb* \rb his clothes|שִׂמְלָתוֹ\rb*, \rb and went into|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתָּ֑חוּ\rb*. \rb Then he went|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and at his request|וַיִּשְׁאַ֕ל\rb* \rb they set|וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb food|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb before him|ל֛וֹ\rb*, \rb and he ate|וַיֹּאכַֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 “\rb What is|מָֽה־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֑יתָה\rb*?” \rb his servants|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb*. “\rb While|בַּעֲב֞וּר\rb* \rb the child|הַיֶּ֤לֶד\rb* \rb was alive|חַי֙\rb*, \rb you fasted|צַ֣מְתָּ\rb* \rb and wept|וַתֵּ֔בְךְּ\rb*, \rb but when|וְכַֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb he|הַיֶּ֔לֶד\rb* \rb died|מֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb you got up|קַ֖מְתָּ\rb* \rb and ate|וַתֹּ֥אכַל\rb*\rb |לָֽחֶם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb David answered|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb While|בְּעוֹד֙\rb* \rb the child|הַיֶּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb was alive|חַ֔י\rb*, \rb I fasted|צַ֖מְתִּי\rb* \rb and wept|וָֽאֶבְכֶּ֑ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I said|אָמַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb*, ‘\rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵ֔עַ\rb*? \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb may be gracious|יְחָנַּנִי\rb* \rb to me|הַיָּֽלֶד׃\rb* \rb and let him live|וְחַ֥י\rb*.’ \v 23 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb that he is dead|מֵ֗ת\rb*, \rb why|לָ֤מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּה֙\rb* \rb should I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb fast|צָ֔ם\rb*? \rb Can|הַאוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb I bring him back|לַהֲשִׁיב֖וֹ\rb* \rb again|ע֑וֹד\rb*? \rb I will|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb go|הֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb but he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb return|יָשׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*.”
\s1 Solomon’s Birth
\p \v 24 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb*\rb |בַּת־\rb* \rb comforted|וַיְנַחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Bathsheba|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb*, \rb and he went|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and lay|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb with her|עִמָּ֑הּ\rb*. \rb So she gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֗ן\rb*, \rb and they|וַיִּקְרָא\rb*\f + \fr 12:24 \ft Or \fqa she \ft or \fqa he\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb named him|שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*.
\p \rb Now the LORD|וַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb loved the child|אֲהֵבֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 25 \rb and sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb* \rb word through|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb to name him|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jedidiah|יְדִ֣ידְיָ֑הּ\rb* \rb because|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb the LORD loved him|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 12:25 \ft Literally \fqa to name him Jedidiah because of the LORD\ft ; \fqa Jedidiah \ft means \fqa beloved of the LORD\f*
\s1 The Capture of Rabbah
\p \v 26 \rb Meanwhile, Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb fought|וַיִּלָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb against Rabbah|בְּרַבַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb and captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמְּלוּכָֽה׃\rb* \rb fortress|עִ֥יר\rb*. \v 27 \rb Then Joab|יוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb to say|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb I have fought|נִלְחַ֣מְתִּי\rb* \rb against Rabbah|בְרַבָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and have|גַּם־\rb* \rb captured|לָכַ֖דְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the water supply|הַמָּֽיִם׃\rb* \rb of the city|עִ֥יר\rb*.\f + \fr 12:27 \ft Or \fqa and have captured the city of waters\f* \v 28 \rb Now, therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb assemble|אֱסֹף֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the rest|יֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb lay siege|וַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb*, \rb and capture it|וְלָכְדָ֑הּ\rb*. \rb Otherwise|פֶּן־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will capture|אֶלְכֹּ֤ד\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb and it will be named|וְנִקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb after me|שְׁמִ֖י\rb*\rb |עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 29 \rb So David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb assembled|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֥ף\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Rabbah|רַבָּ֑תָה\rb*; \rb and he fought|וַיִּלָּ֥חֶם\rb* \rb against it|בָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb and captured it|וַֽיִּלְכְּדָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb Then he took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the crown|עֲטֶֽרֶת־\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֨ל\rb* \rb the head|רֹאשׁ֜וֹ\rb* \rb of their king|מַלְכָּם֩\rb*.\f + \fr 12:30 \ft Or \fqa from the head of Milcom\ft . Milcom, also called Molech, was god of the Ammonites; see Leviticus 18:21 and 1 Kings 11:7.\f* \rb It weighed|וּמִשְׁקָלָ֨הּ\rb* \rb a talent|כִּכַּ֤ר\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָב֙\rb*\f + \fr 12:30 \fqa A talent \ft is approximately 75.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of gold.\f* \rb and was set with precious|יְקָרָ֔ה\rb* \rb stones|וְאֶ֣בֶן\rb*, \rb and it was|וַתְּהִ֖י\rb* \rb placed on|עַל־\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*. \rb And David took|הוֹצִ֖יא\rb* \rb a great amount|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb of plunder|וּשְׁלַ֥ל\rb* \rb from the city|הָעִ֛יר\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb David brought out|הוֹצִ֗יא\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֨ם\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb there|בָּ֜הּ\rb* \rb and put them to work|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם\rb* \rb with saws|בַּ֠מְּגֵרָה\rb*,\f + \fr 12:31 \ft Literally \fqa put them under saws\f* \rb iron|הַבַּרְזֶ֜ל\rb* \rb picks|וּבַחֲרִצֵ֨י\rb*, \rb and axes|וּֽבְמַגְזְרֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַבַּרְזֶ֗ל\rb*, \rb and he made them work|וְהֶעֱבִ֤יר\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb at the brick kilns|בַּמַּלְכֶּן\rb*.\f + \fr 12:31 \ft Literally \fqa and he made them pass through the brick kilns.\f* \rb He did|יַעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb the same|וְכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the Ammonite|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb*. \rb Then David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֧שָׁב\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\c 13
\s1 Amnon and Tamar
\p \v 1 \rb After some time|וַיְהִ֣י\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb David’s|דָּוִֽד׃\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֥וֹן\rb* \rb fell in love|וַיֶּאֱהָבֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb with Tamar|תָּמָ֑ר\rb*, \rb the beautiful|יָפָ֖ה\rb* \rb sister|אָח֥וֹת\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of David’s|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Absalom|וּלְאַבְשָׁל֧וֹם\rb*. \v 2 \rb Amnon|לְאַמְנ֜וֹן\rb* \rb was sick|לְהִתְחַלּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb with frustration|וַיֵּ֨צֶר\rb* \rb over|בַּֽעֲבוּר֙\rb* \rb his sister|אֲחֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb Tamar|תָּמָ֣ר\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she|הִ֑יא\rb* \rb was a virgin|בְתוּלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and it seemed|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb implausible|וַיִּפָּלֵא֙\rb* \rb for him|אַמְנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb anything|מְאֽוּמָה׃\rb* \rb to her|לָ֖הּ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Now Amnon|וּלְאַמְנ֣וֹן\rb* \rb had a friend|רֵ֗עַ\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb Jonadab|יֽוֹנָדָ֔ב\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of David’s|דָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb* \rb Shimeah|שִׁמְעָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 13:3 \fqa Shimeah \ft is a variant of \fqa Shammah\ft , \fqa Shimea\ft , and \fqa Shimei\ft ; see 1 Samuel 16:9, 2 Samuel 21:21, and 1 Chronicles 2:13.\f* \rb Jonadab|וְי֣וֹנָדָ֔ב\rb* \rb was a very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb shrewd|חָכָ֖ם\rb* \rb man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*, \v 4 \rb and he asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Amnon|ל֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Why|מַדּ֣וּעַ\rb* \rb are you|אַ֠תָּה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb so|כָּ֣כָה\rb* \rb depressed|דַּ֤ל\rb* \rb morning|בַּבֹּ֣קֶר\rb* \rb after morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*? \rb Won’t|הֲל֖וֹא\rb* \rb you tell|תַּגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb*?”
\p \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֔וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I am|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb in love|אֹהֵֽב׃\rb* \rb with Tamar|תָּמָ֗ר\rb*, \rb my brother|אָחִ֖י\rb* \rb Absalom’s|אַבְשָׁלֹ֥ם\rb* \rb sister|אֲח֛וֹת\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Jonadab|יְה֣וֹנָדָ֔ב\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb Lie down|שְׁכַ֥ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your bed|מִשְׁכָּבְךָ֖\rb* \rb and pretend you are ill|וְהִתְחָ֑ל\rb*. \rb When your father|אָבִ֣יךָ\rb* \rb comes|וּבָ֧א\rb* \rb to see you|לִרְאוֹתֶ֗ךָ\rb*, \rb say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֡יו\rb*, ‘\rb Please|נָא֩\rb* \rb let my sister|אֲחוֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb Tamar|תָמָ֨ר\rb* \rb come|תָּ֣בֹא\rb* \rb and give me something|וְתַבְרֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb to eat|לֶ֗חֶם\rb*. \rb Let her prepare|וְעָשְׂתָ֤ה\rb* \rb it|הַבִּרְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb in my sight|לְעֵינַי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I may watch her|אֶרְאֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and eat it|וְאָכַלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb from her hand|מִיָּדָֽהּ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 6 \rb So Amnon|אַמְנ֖וֹן\rb* \rb lay down|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb and feigned illness|וַיִּתְחָ֑ל\rb*. \rb When the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to see him|לִרְאֹת֗וֹ\rb*, \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֤וֹן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֞א\rb* \rb let my sister|אֲחֹתִ֗י\rb*\rb |וּתְלַבֵּ֤ב\rb* \rb Tamar|תָּמָ֣ר\rb* \rb come|תָּֽבוֹא־\rb* \rb and make a couple|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of cakes|לְבִב֔וֹת\rb* \rb in my sight|לְעֵינַי֙\rb*, \rb so that I may eat|וְאֶבְרֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from her hand|מִיָּדָֽהּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Tamar|תָּמָ֖ר\rb* \rb at the palace|הַבַּ֣יְתָה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: “\rb Please|נָ֗א\rb* \rb go|לְכִ֣י\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֚ית\rb* \rb of Amnon|אַמְנ֣וֹן\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֔יךְ\rb* \rb and prepare|וַעֲשִׂי־\rb* \rb a meal|הַבִּרְיָֽה׃\rb* \rb for him|ל֖וֹ\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb So Tamar|תָּמָ֗ר\rb* \rb went|וַתֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֛ית\rb* \rb of her brother|אָחִ֖יהָ\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֥וֹן\rb*, \rb who|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb was lying down|שֹׁכֵ֑ב\rb*. \rb She took|וַתִּקַּ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb some dough|הַבָּצֵ֤ק\rb*, \rb kneaded it|וַתָּלוֹשׁ\rb*, \rb made cakes|וַתְּלַבֵּ֣ב\rb* \rb in his sight|לְעֵינָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and baked|וַתְּבַשֵּׁ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|הַלְּבִבֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Then she brought|וַתִּקַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the pan|הַמַּשְׂרֵת֙\rb* \rb and set it down|וַתִּצֹ֣ק\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb but he refused|וַיְמָאֵ֖ן\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכ֑וֹל\rb*. “\rb Send everyone|כָל־\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽעָלַ֔י\rb* \rb away|הוֹצִ֤יאוּ\rb*!” \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֗וֹן\rb*. \rb And everyone|כָל־\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |מֵעָלָֽיו׃\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצְא֥וּ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then Amnon|אַמְנ֜וֹן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Tamar|תָּמָ֗ר\rb*, “\rb Bring|הָבִ֤יאִי\rb* \rb the food|הַבִּרְיָה֙\rb* \rb into the bedroom|הַחֶ֔דֶר\rb*, \rb so that I may eat it|וְאֶבְרֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from your hand|מִיָּדֵ֑ךְ\rb*.”
\p \rb Tamar|תָּמָ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the cakes|הַלְּבִבוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she had made|עָשָׂ֔תָה\rb* \rb and went|וַתָּבֵ֛א\rb* \rb to her brother|אָחִ֖יהָ\rb* \rb Amnon’s|לְאַמְנ֥וֹן\rb* \rb bedroom|הֶחָֽדְרָה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And when she had brought them|וַתַּגֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb to eat|לֶֽאֱכֹ֑ל\rb*, \rb he took hold|וַיַּֽחֲזֶק־\rb* \rb of her|בָּהּ֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Come|בּ֛וֹאִי\rb* \rb lie|שִׁכְבִ֥י\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֖י\rb*, \rb my sister|אֲחוֹתִֽי׃\rb*!”
\p \v 12 “\rb No|אַל־\rb*, \rb my brother|אָחִי֙\rb*!” \rb she cried|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb violate me|תְּעַנֵּ֔נִי\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb such|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb a thing should never|לֹא־\rb* \rb be done|יֵֽעָשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb do|תַּעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb disgraceful thing|הַנְּבָלָ֥ה\rb*! \v 13 \rb Where|אָ֤נָה\rb* \rb could I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb ever take|אוֹלִיךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my shame|חֶרְפָּתִ֔י\rb*? \rb And you|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb would be|תִּהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb like one|כְּאַחַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the fools|הַנְּבָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*!\rb |וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb speak|דַּבֶּר־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb he will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb withhold me|יִמְנָעֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb from you|מִמֶּֽךָּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb But Amnon refused|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb to listen to her|לִשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb*\rb |בְּקוֹלָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb and being stronger|וַיֶּחֱזַ֤ק\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֙נָּה֙\rb*, \rb he violated her|וַיְעַנֶּ֔הָ\rb* \rb and lay with|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֖ב\rb* \rb her|אֹתָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then Amnon|אַמְנ֗וֹן\rb* \rb hated Tamar|וַיִּשְׂנָאֶ֣הָ\rb* \rb with such intensity|גְּדוֹלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb his hatred|שִׂנְאָה֙\rb*\rb |שְׂנֵאָ֔הּ\rb* \rb was greater than|גְדוֹלָ֗ה\rb*\rb |הַשִּׂנְאָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the love|מֵאַהֲבָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he previously had|אֲהֵבָ֑הּ\rb*. “\rb Get up|ק֥וּמִי\rb*!” \rb he said|וַֽיֹּאמֶר־\rb* \rb to her|לָ֥הּ\rb*. “\rb Be gone|לֵֽכִי׃\rb*!”
\p \v 16 “\rb No|אַל־\rb*,”\rb |אוֹדֹ֞ת\rb* \rb she replied|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb sending me away|לְשַׁלְּחֵ֑נִי\rb* \rb is worse than|מֵאַחֶ֛רֶת\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb wrong|הָרָעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have already done|עָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb to me|עִמִּ֖י\rb*!”
\p \rb But he refused|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb to listen|לִשְׁמֹ֥עַֽ\rb* \rb to her|לָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Instead, he called|וַיִּקְרָ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb to his attendant|נַעֲרוֹ֙\rb*\rb |מְשָׁ֣רְת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Throw|שִׁלְחוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this woman|זֹ֛את\rb*\rb |מֵעָלַ֖י\rb* \rb out|הַח֑וּצָה\rb* \rb and bolt|וּנְעֹ֥ל\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֖לֶת\rb* \rb behind her|אַחֲרֶֽיהָ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 18 \rb So Amnon’s attendant|מְשָֽׁרְתוֹ֙\rb* \rb threw|וַיֹּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb her|אוֹתָ֤הּ\rb* \rb out|הַח֔וּץ\rb* \rb and bolted|וְנָעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֖לֶת\rb* \rb behind her|אַחֲרֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \rb Now Tamar was wearing|וְעָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb a robe|כְּתֹ֣נֶת\rb* \rb of many colors|פַּסִּ֔ים\rb*,\f + \fr 13:18 \ft Or \fqa a robe with long sleeves\ft ; see also Genesis 37:3.\f* \rb because|כִּי֩\rb* \rb this is what|כֵ֨ן\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb virgin|הַבְּתוּלֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |מְעִילִ֑ים\rb* \rb daughters|בְנוֹת־\rb* \rb wore|תִּלְבַּ֧שְׁןָ\rb*. \v 19 \rb And Tamar|תָּמָ֥ר\rb* \rb put|וַתִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb ashes|אֵ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb her head|רֹאשָׁ֔הּ\rb* \rb and tore|קָרָ֑עָה\rb*\rb |הַפַּסִּ֛ים\rb* \rb her|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb robe|וּכְתֹ֧נֶת\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*. \rb And putting|וַתָּ֤שֶׂם\rb* \rb her hand|יָדָהּ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb her head|רֹאשָׁ֔הּ\rb*, \rb she went away|וַתֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָל֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb crying aloud|וְזָעָֽקָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Her brother|אָחִ֗יהָ\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֜יהָ\rb*, “\rb Has your brother|אָחִיךְ֮\rb* \rb Amnon|הַאֲמִינ֣וֹן\rb* \rb been|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּךְ֒\rb*? \rb Be quiet|הַחֲרִ֙ישִׁי֙\rb* \rb for now|וְעַתָּ֞ה\rb*, \rb my sister|אֲחוֹתִ֤י\rb*. \rb He|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is your brother|אָחִ֣יךְ\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb take|תָּשִׁ֥יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb thing|לַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb to heart|לִבֵּ֖ךְ\rb*.”
\p \rb So Tamar|תָּמָר֙\rb* \rb lived|וַתֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb as a desolate|וְשֹׁ֣מֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb woman in the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of her brother|אָחִֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb When King|וְהַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֕ע\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*, \rb he was furious|וַיִּ֥חַר\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb*.\f + \fr 13:21 \ft DSS and LXX include \fqa But he would not punish his son Amnon, because he loved him, since he was his firstborn.\f* \v 22 \rb And Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֛וֹם\rb* \rb never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb said a word|דִבֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֖וֹן\rb*, \rb either good|ט֑וֹב\rb* \rb or bad|לְמֵרָ֣ע\rb*,\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hated|שָׂנֵ֤א\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb*\rb |דְּבַר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb violating|עִנָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb his sister|אֲחֹתֽוֹ׃פ\rb* \rb Tamar|תָּמָ֥ר\rb*.
\s1 Absalom’s Revenge on Amnon
\p \v 23 \rb Two years later|לִשְׁנָתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |יָמִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |וַיִּהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb when Absalom’s|לְאַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּבַ֥עַל\rb* \rb sheepshearers|גֹֽזְזִים֙\rb* \rb were|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb at Baal-hazor|חָצ֖וֹר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb near|עִם־\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb he|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb invited|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb And he|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Your servant|לְעַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb has just|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb hired shearers|גֹזְזִ֖ים\rb*. \rb Will the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his servants|וַעֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb come|יֵֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb me|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 25 “\rb No|אַל־\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִי֙\rb*,” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אַבְשָׁל֗וֹם\rb*, “\rb we should not|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb all|כֻּלָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb go|נֵלֵךְ֙\rb*, \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb we would be a burden|נִכְבַּ֖ד\rb* \rb to you|עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb*.” \rb Although Absalom urged|וַיִּפְרָץ־\rb* \rb him|בּ֛וֹ\rb*, \rb he was not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb willing|אָבָ֥ה\rb* \rb to go|לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb*, \rb but gave him his blessing|וַֽיְבָרֲכֵֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 “\rb If not|וָלֹ֕א\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*, “\rb please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb let my brother|אָחִ֑י\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֣וֹן\rb* \rb go|יֵֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֖נוּ\rb*.”
\p “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb should he go|יֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*?” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb But Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb urged|וַיִּפְרָץ־\rb* \rb him|בּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb so the king sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb*\rb |אִתּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֔וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the rest|כָּל־\rb* \rb of his|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*.\f + \fr 13:27 \ft LXX and Vulgate include \fqa And Absalom prepared a feast fit for a king.\f*
\p \v 28 \rb Now Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֨וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had ordered|וַיְצַו֩\rb* \rb his young men|נְעָרָ֜יו\rb*, “\rb Watch|רְא֣וּ\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֤וֹן\rb* \rb until|נָ֠א\rb* \rb his heart|לֵב־\rb* \rb is merry|כְּט֨וֹב\rb* \rb with wine|בַּיַּ֙יִן֙\rb*, \rb and when I order|וְאָמַרְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to strike|הַכּ֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Amnon down|אַמְנ֛וֹן\rb*, \rb you are to kill him|וַהֲמִתֶּ֥ם\rb*.\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֑אוּ\rb*. \rb Have|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb not|הֲל֗וֹא\rb* \rb commanded|צִוִּ֣יתִי\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*? \rb Be courageous|חִזְק֖וּ\rb* \rb and|וִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb valiant|חָֽיִל׃\rb*!”
\p \v 29 \rb So Absalom’s|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb young men|נַעֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb did|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֞וּ\rb* \rb to Amnon|לְאַמְנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb had ordered|צִוָּ֖ה\rb*. \rb Then all the other|כָּל־\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וַֽיִּרְכְּב֛וּ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּקֻ֣מוּ׀\rb*, \rb and each one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻֽסוּ׃\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his mule|פִּרְדּ֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb While they|הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb were|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb on the way|בַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb*, \rb a report|וְהַשְּׁמֻעָ֣ה\rb* \rb reached|בָ֔אָה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has struck down|הִכָּ֤ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*; \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃ס\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb is left|נוֹתַ֥ר\rb*!”
\p \v 31 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb stood up|וַיָּ֧קָם\rb*, \rb tore|וַיִּקְרַ֥ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and lay down|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb on the ground|אָ֑רְצָה\rb*. \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֥יו\rb* \rb stood|נִצָּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb by with their clothes|בְגָדִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb torn|קְרֻעֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb But Jonadab|יוֹנָדָ֣ב׀\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of David’s|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִֽי־\rb* \rb Shimeah|שִׁמְעָ֨ה\rb*, \rb spoke up|וַיַּ֡עַן\rb*: “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִי֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb must not|אַל־\rb*\rb |יֹאמַ֤ר\rb* \rb think|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb they have killed|הֵמִ֔יתוּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַנְּעָרִ֤ים\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb only|לְבַדּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֥וֹן\rb* \rb is dead|מֵ֑ת\rb*. \rb In fact|כִּֽי־\rb*, \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb*\rb |פִּ֤י\rb*\rb |הָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb has planned this|שׂוּמָ֔ה\rb* \rb since the day|מִיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb Amnon violated|עַנֹּת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb his sister|אֲחֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Tamar|תָּמָ֥ר\rb*. \v 33 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֨י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb take|יָשֵׂם֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb heart|לִבּוֹ֙\rb* \rb the report that|דָּבָ֣ר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb are dead|מֵ֑תוּ\rb*.\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb Only|לְבַדּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Amnon|אַמְנ֥וֹן\rb* \rb is dead|מֵֽת׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Absalom Flees to Geshur
\p \v 34 \rb Meanwhile, Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb had fled|וַיִּבְרַ֖ח\rb*. \rb When the young man|הַנַּ֤עַר\rb* \rb standing watch|הַצֹּפֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֞א\rb*\rb |עֵינוֹ\rb*, \rb he saw|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb many|רַ֜ב\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb* \rb coming|הֹלְכִ֥ים\rb* \rb down the road|מִדֶּ֛רֶךְ\rb* \rb west of him|אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb*,\f + \fr 13:34 \ft Or \fqa behind him\f* \rb along the side|מִצַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the hill. And the watchman went and reported to the king, “I see men coming from the direction of Horonaim, along the side of the hill|הָהָֽר׃\rb*.”\f + \fr 13:34 \ft LXX; Hebrew does not include \fqa And the watchman...\ft .\f*
\p \v 35 \rb So Jonadab|יֽוֹנָדָב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb have arrived|בָּ֑אוּ\rb*! \rb It is just as|כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |הָיָֽה׃\rb* \rb said|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 36 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb And as he finished|כְּכַלֹּת֣וֹ\rb* \rb speaking|לְדַבֵּ֗ר\rb*,\rb |וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb came in|בָּ֔אוּ\rb*, \rb wailing|וַיִּבְכּ֑וּ\rb* \rb loudly|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb*\rb |קוֹלָ֖ם\rb*. \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb wept|בָּכ֕וּ\rb*\rb |בְּכִ֖י\rb* \rb very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb bitterly|גָּד֥וֹל\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb Now Absalom|וְאַבְשָׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb fled|בָּרַ֔ח\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Talmai|תַּלְמַ֥י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ammihud|עַמִּיחוּר\rb*, \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Geshur|גְּשׁ֑וּר\rb*. \rb But David mourned|וַיִּתְאַבֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb day|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb After Absalom|וְאַבְשָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb had fled|בָּרַ֖ח\rb* \rb and gone|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Geshur|גְּשׁ֑וּר\rb*, \rb he stayed|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb*. \v 39 \rb And King|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*\f + \fr 13:39 \ft MT; DSS and LXX \fqa And the spirit of the king \f* \rb longed|וַתְּכַל֙\rb* \rb to go|לָצֵ֖את\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*,\f + \fr 13:39 \ft Or \fqa ceased to go out after Absalom\f* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he had been consoled|נִחַ֥ם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Amnon’s|אַמְנ֖וֹן\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb death|מֵֽת׃ס\rb*.
\c 14
\s1 Absalom’s Return to Jerusalem
\p \v 1 \rb Now Joab|יוֹאָ֣ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרֻיָ֑ה\rb* \rb perceived|וַיֵּ֖דַע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֥ב\rb* \rb longed for|עַל־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb to Tekoa|תְּק֔וֹעָה\rb* \rb to bring|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a wise|חֲכָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb*. \rb He told her|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֵ֠לֶיהָ\rb* “\rb Please|נָ֞א\rb* \rb pretend to be a mourner|הִֽתְאַבְּלִי־\rb*; \rb put on|וְלִבְשִׁי־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb clothes|בִגְדֵי־\rb* \rb for mourning|אֵ֗בֶל\rb* \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb anoint yourself|תָּס֙וּכִי֙\rb* \rb with oil|שֶׁ֔מֶן\rb*. \rb Act|וְהָיִ֕ית\rb* \rb like a woman|כְּאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |זֶ֚ה\rb* \rb who has mourned|מִתְאַבֶּ֖לֶת\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the dead|מֵֽת׃\rb* \rb a long|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb time|יָמִ֣ים\rb*. \v 3 \rb Then go|וּבָאת֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and speak|וְדִבַּ֥רְתְּ\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb words|כַּדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*.” \rb And Joab|יוֹאָ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb put|וַיָּ֧שֶׂם\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in her mouth|בְּפִֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb When the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb from Tekoa|הַתְּקֹעִית֙\rb* \rb went to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb she fell|וַתִּפֹּ֧ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb facedown|אַפֶּ֛יהָ\rb*\rb |אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb in homage|וַתִּשְׁתָּ֑חוּ\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Help me|הוֹשִׁ֥עָה\rb*, \rb O king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 5 “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb troubles you|לָּ֑ךְ\rb*?” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb her|לָ֥הּ\rb*.
\p “\rb Indeed|אֲבָ֛ל\rb*,” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I am|אָ֖נִי\rb*\rb |אִשָּֽׁה־\rb* \rb a widow|אַלְמָנָ֥ה\rb*, \rb for my husband|אִישִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb is dead|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb*. \v 6 \rb And your maidservant|וּלְשִׁפְחָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb had two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|שְׁנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb were fighting|וַיִּנָּצ֤וּ\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb with no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one to separate|מַצִּ֖יל\rb* \rb them|בֵּֽינֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and one|הָאֶחָ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb struck|וַיַּכּ֧וֹ\rb* \rb the other|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb and killed|וַיָּ֥מֶת\rb* \rb him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Now|וְהִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb the whole|כָֽל־\rb* \rb clan|הַמִּשְׁפָּחָ֜ה\rb* \rb has risen up|קָ֨מָה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb your maidservant|שִׁפְחָתֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, ‘\rb Hand over|תְּנִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the one who struck down|מַכֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֗יו\rb*, \rb that we may put him to death|וּנְמִתֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb for the life|בְּנֶ֤פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the brother|אָחִיו֙\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he killed|הָרָ֔ג\rb*. \rb Then we will cut off|וְנַשְׁמִ֖ידָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heir|הַיּוֹרֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb as well|גַּ֣ם\rb*!’ \rb So they would extinguish|וְכִבּ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my one remaining|נִשְׁאָ֔רָה\rb* \rb ember|גַּֽחַלְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb by not|לְבִלְתִּ֧י\rb* \rb preserving|שׂוּם\rb* \rb my husband’s|לְאִישִׁ֛י\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb or posterity|וּשְׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the earth|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 8 “\rb Go|לְכִ֣י\rb* \rb home|לְבֵיתֵ֑ךְ\rb*,” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*, “\rb and I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will give orders|אֲצַוֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb on your behalf|עָלָֽיִךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb But the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb of Tekoa|הַתְּקוֹעִית֙\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*, \rb may any blame be|הֶעָוֺ֖ן\rb* \rb on me|עָלַ֞י\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb my father’s|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and may the king|וְהַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his throne|וְכִסְא֖וֹ\rb* \rb be guiltless|נָקִֽי׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 10 “\rb If anyone speaks|הַֽמְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to you|אֵלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb bring him|וַֽהֲבֵאת֣וֹ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, \rb and he will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb trouble|לָגַ֥עַת\rb* \rb you|בָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb again|יֹסִ֥יף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb*!”
\p \v 11 “\rb Please|נָ֨א\rb*,” \rb she replied|וַתֹּאמֶר֩\rb*, “\rb may the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb invoke|יִזְכָּר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb to prevent the avenger|גֹּאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb of blood|הַדָּם֙\rb* \rb from increasing|מֵהַרְבִּית\rb* \rb the devastation|לְשַׁחֵ֔ת\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that my son|בְּנִ֑י\rb* \rb may not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb be destroyed|יַשְׁמִ֖ידוּ\rb*!”
\p “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*,” \rb he vowed|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb not|אִם־\rb* \rb a hair|מִשַּׂעֲרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of your son’s head|בְּנֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb will fall|יִפֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb to the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb Then the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֧א\rb*, \rb may your servant|שִׁפְחָתְךָ֛\rb* \rb speak|תְּדַבֶּר־\rb* \rb a word|דָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*?”
\p “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּֽרִי׃ס\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb The woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb asked|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Why|וְלָ֧מָּה\rb* \rb have you devised|חָשַׁ֛בְתָּה\rb* \rb a thing like this|כָּזֹ֖את\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*? \rb When the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb says|וּמִדַּבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb*, \rb does he not convict himself|כְּאָשֵׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb since he|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb has not|לְבִלְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb brought back|הָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb his own banished son|נִדְּחֽוֹ׃\rb*? \v 14 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb we will surely die|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |נָמ֔וּת\rb* \rb and be like water|וְכַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb poured out|הַנִּגָּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb on the ground|אַ֔רְצָה\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb cannot|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be recovered|יֵאָסֵ֑פוּ\rb*. \rb Yet God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb does not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb take away|יִשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb a life|נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb*, \rb but He devises|וְחָשַׁב֙\rb* \rb ways|מַֽחֲשָׁב֔וֹת\rb* \rb that the banished one|יִדַּ֥ח\rb* \rb may not|לְבִלְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb be cast out|נִדָּֽח׃\rb* \rb from Him|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Now therefore|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have come|בָּ֜אתִי\rb* \rb to present|לְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb matter|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb have made me afraid|יֵֽרְאֻ֖נִי\rb*. \rb Your servant|שִׁפְחָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb thought|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb I will speak|אֲדַבְּרָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֛י\rb* \rb he|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will grant|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb the request|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of his maidservant|אֲמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb and deliver|לְהַצִּ֥יל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his maidservant|אֲמָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִכַּ֣ף\rb* \rb of the man|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb who would cut off|לְהַשְׁמִ֨יד\rb* \rb both|יַ֔חַד\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֤י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִי֙\rb* \rb from God’s|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb inheritance|מִֽנַּחֲלַ֖ת\rb*.’
\p \v 17 \rb And now your servant|שִׁפְחָ֣תְךָ֔\rb*\rb |נָּ֛א\rb* \rb says|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, ‘\rb May|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb bring me rest|לִמְנוּחָ֑ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֤י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb is able to discern|לִשְׁמֹ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb good|הַטּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb and evil|וְהָרָ֔ע\rb*, \rb just like the angel|כְּמַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 14:17 \ft Or \fqa Angel\ft ; also in verse 20\f* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb*.\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb May the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃פ\rb*.’”
\p \v 18 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיַּ֣עַן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָ֣אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*, “\rb I am|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb going to ask|שֹׁאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb you|אֹתָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb something|דָּבָ֔ר\rb*;\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֨א\rb* \rb conceal|תְכַחֲדִ֤י\rb* \rb it from me|מִמֶּ֙נִּי֙\rb*!”
\p “\rb Let my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb speak|יְדַבֶּר־\rb*,”\rb |נָ֖א\rb* \rb she|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is the hand|הֲיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb behind|אִתָּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֑את\rb*?”
\p \rb The woman|הָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וַתֹּ֡אמֶר\rb* \rb answered|וַתַּ֣עַן\rb*, “\rb As surely as you|נַפְשְׁךָ֩\rb* \rb live|חֵֽי־\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֨י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*, \rb no one|אִם־\rb* \rb can turn|אִ֣שׁ׀\rb* \rb to the right|לְהֵמִ֣ין\rb* \rb or to the left|וּלְהַשְׂמִ֗יל\rb* \rb from anything|מִכֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb says|דִּבֶּר֙\rb*. \rb Yes|כִּֽי־\rb*, \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֤\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb is the one who|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb gave me orders|צִוָּ֔נִי\rb*; \rb he|וְה֗וּא\rb* \rb told|שָׂ֚ם\rb*\rb |בְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb your maidservant|שִׁפְחָֽתְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb exactly what to say|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb to|לְבַעֲב֤וּר\rb* \rb bring about|סַבֵּב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this change|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of affairs|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb*, \rb but my lord|וַאדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb has wisdom|חָכָ֗ם\rb* \rb like the wisdom|כְּחָכְמַת֙\rb* \rb of the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb to know|לָדַ֖עַת\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that happens|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*,\rb |הִנֵּה־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* “\rb I hereby grant|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb request|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*. \rb Go|וְלֵ֛ךְ\rb*, \rb bring back|הָשֵׁ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the young man|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֨ב\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּל֩\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb facedown|פָּנָ֥יו\rb*\rb |אַ֛רְצָה\rb* \rb in homage|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb and blessed|וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*. “\rb Today|הַיּוֹם֩\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֡ב\rb*, “\rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֜\rb* \rb knows|יָדַ֨ע\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb he has found|מָצָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֤ן\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has granted|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb his|עַבְדּוֹ׃\rb* \rb request|דְּבַ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb So Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֥קָם\rb*, \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Geshur|גְּשׁ֑וּרָה\rb*, \rb and brought|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*. \v 24 \rb But the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb added|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb He may return|יִסֹּ֣ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb but he must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb see|יִרְאֶ֑ה\rb* \rb my face|וּפָנַ֖י\rb*.” \rb So Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיִּסֹּ֤ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb but he did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb see|רָאָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb the face|וּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Now there was|הָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb as handsome|יָפֶ֛ה\rb* \rb and highly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb praised|לְהַלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb as Absalom|וּכְאַבְשָׁל֗וֹם\rb*. \rb From the sole|מִכַּ֤ף\rb* \rb of his foot|רַגְלוֹ֙\rb* \rb to|וְעַ֣ד\rb* \rb the top of his head|קָדְקֳד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb have|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb a single flaw|מֽוּם׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb And when he cut the hair|וּֽבְגַלְּחוֹ֮\rb* \rb of|אֶת־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁוֹ֒\rb*—\rb |וְֽ֠הָיָה\rb* \rb he shaved|יְגַלֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb it every year|מִקֵּ֨ץ\rb*\rb |יָמִ֤ים׀\rb*\rb |לַיָּמִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his hair got so heavy|כָבֵ֥ד\rb*\rb |עָלָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְגִלְּח֑וֹ\rb*— \rb he would weigh|וְשָׁקַל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it out|שְׂעַ֣ר\rb*\rb |רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb to be two hundred|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֖ים\rb*,\f + \fr 14:26 \fqa 200 shekels \ft is approximately 5 pounds or 2.3 kilograms of hair.\f* \rb according to the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb standard|בְּאֶ֥בֶן\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Three|שְׁלוֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb were born|וַיִּֽוָּלְד֤וּ\rb* \rb to Absalom|לְאַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb*, \rb and a|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb daughter|וּבַ֥ת\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמָ֣הּ\rb* \rb Tamar|תָּמָ֑ר\rb*, \rb who|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֔ה\rb* \rb a beautiful|יְפַ֥ת\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶֽה׃פ\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*.
\s1 Absalom Reconciled to David
\p \v 28 \rb Now Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֛וֹם\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּ֧שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb two|שְׁנָתַ֣יִם\rb* \rb years|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb without|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb seeing|רָאָֽה׃\rb* \rb the face|וּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*. \v 29 \rb Then he|אַבְשָׁל֜וֹם\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb to send|לִשְׁלֹ֤חַ\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb but Joab refused|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb to come|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*.
\p \rb So Absalom sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb a second time|שֵׁנִ֔ית\rb*, \rb but Joab still would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb come|לָבֽוֹא׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb Then Absalom said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֜יו\rb*, “\rb Look|רְאוּ֩\rb*, \rb Joab’s|יוֹאָ֤ב\rb* \rb field is|חֶלְקַ֨ת\rb* \rb next to|אֶל־\rb* \rb mine|יָדִי֙\rb*, \rb and he has|וְלוֹ־\rb* \rb barley|שְׂעֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֣ם\rb*. \rb Go|לְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb and set it|וְהוֹצִתִּיהָ\rb* \rb on fire|בָאֵ֑שׁ\rb*!”
\p \rb And Absalom’s|אַבְשָׁל֛וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֧י\rb* \rb set the field|הַחֶלְקָ֖ה\rb* \rb on fire|וַיַּצִּ֜תוּ\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 14:30 \ft LXX includes \fqa So the servants of Joab came to him with their clothes torn and said to him, “The servants of Absalom have set your field on fire.”\f*
\p \v 31 \rb |וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb Then Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Absalom’s|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb house|הַבָּ֑יְתָה\rb* \rb and demanded|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb did your servants|עֲבָדֶ֛ךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb set|הִצִּ֧יתוּ\rb* \rb my field|הַחֶלְקָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb on fire|בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 32 “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֣וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |יוֹאָ֡ב\rb*, “\rb I sent|שָׁלַ֣חְתִּי\rb* \rb for|אֵלֶ֣יךָ׀\rb* \rb you and said|לֵאמֹ֡ר\rb*, ‘\rb Come|בֹּ֣א\rb* \rb here|הֵ֠נָּה\rb*. \rb I want to send|וְאֶשְׁלְחָה֩\rb*\rb |אֹתְךָ֨\rb* \rb you to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb to ask|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*: \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb have I come back|בָּ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb from Geshur|מִגְּשׁ֔וּר\rb*? \rb It would be better|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb for me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb if I were|אֲנִי־\rb* \rb still|עֹ֣ד\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*.’ \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb let me see|אֶרְאֶה֙\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb there is|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb iniquity|עָוֺ֖ן\rb* \rb in me|בִּ֥י\rb*, \rb let him kill me|וֶהֱמִתָֽנִי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb So Joab|יוֹאָ֣ב\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּלֶךְ֮\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb the king|לוֹ֒\rb*, \rb and David summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb*, \rb who came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֨חוּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb facedown|אַפָּ֛יו\rb*\rb |אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb before him|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*. \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb kissed|וַיִּשַּׁ֥ק\rb* \rb Absalom|לְאַבְשָׁלֽוֹם׃פ\rb*.
\c 15
\s1 Absalom’s Conspiracy
\p \v 1 \rb Some time later|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb*\rb |מֵאַ֣חֲרֵי\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb provided for|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb himself|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb a chariot|מֶרְכָּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb with horses|וְסֻסִ֑ים\rb* \rb and fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to run|רָצִ֥ים\rb* \rb ahead of him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb He|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb would get up early|וְהִשְׁכִּים֙\rb* \rb and stand|וְעָמַ֕ד\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb*\rb |יַ֖ד\rb* \rb the road|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb leading to the city gate|הַשָּׁ֑עַר\rb*.
\p \rb Whenever|וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb anyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb had|יִהְיֶה־\rb* \rb a grievance|רִיב֩\rb* \rb to bring|לָב֨וֹא\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb for a decision|לַמִּשְׁפָּ֗ט\rb*, \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֤וֹם\rb* \rb would call out|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb and ask|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What|אֵֽי־\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb city|עִיר֙\rb* \rb are you from|אַ֔תָּה\rb*?” \rb And if he replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Your servant is|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb from one|מֵאַחַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the tribes|שִׁבְטֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*,” \v 3 \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb would say|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb Look|רְאֵ֥ה\rb*, \rb your claims|דְבָרֶ֖ךָ\rb* \rb are good|טוֹבִ֣ים\rb* \rb and right|וּנְכֹחִ֑ים\rb*, \rb but the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb has no deputy|אֵין־\rb* \rb to hear|וְשֹׁמֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb*.”\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And he|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb would add|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb If only|מִי־\rb* \rb someone would appoint me|יְשִׂמֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb judge|שֹׁפֵ֖ט\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb then everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb with|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶה־\rb* \rb a grievance|רִ֥יב\rb* \rb or dispute|וּמִשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb could come|יָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to me|וְעָלַ֗י\rb*, \rb and I would give him justice|וְהִצְדַּקְתִּֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Also, when|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb anyone|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb approached|בִּקְרָב־\rb* \rb to bow down|לְהִשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֖ת\rb* \rb to him|ל֑וֹ\rb*, \rb Absalom would reach out|וְשָׁלַ֧ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֛וֹ\rb*, \rb take hold|וְהֶחֱזִ֥יק\rb* \rb of him|ל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and kiss|וְנָ֥שַׁק\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֜וֹם\rb*\rb |כַּדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|יָבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb for justice|לַמִּשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb*. \rb In this way he|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stole|וַיְגַנֵּב֙\rb* \rb the hearts|לֵ֖ב\rb* \rb of the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb After|מִקֵּ֖ץ\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 15:7 \ft Syriac and some LXX manuscripts; Hebrew \fqa forty\f* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb had passed|וַיְהִ֕י\rb*, \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Please|נָּ֗א\rb* \rb let me go|אֵ֣לֲכָה\rb* \rb to Hebron|בְּחֶבְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb to fulfill|וַאֲשַׁלֵּ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a vow|נִדְרִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have made|נָדַ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 8 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb made|נָדַ֣ר\rb* \rb a vow|נֵ֙דֶר֙\rb* \rb while dwelling|בְּשִׁבְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb in Geshur|בִגְשׁ֛וּר\rb* \rb of Aram|בַּאֲרָ֖ם\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: ‘\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb indeed|יָשִׁיב\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb brings me back|יְשִׁיבֵ֤נִי\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb I will worship|וְעָבַדְתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD in Hebron|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.’\f + \fr 15:8 \ft Some LXX manuscripts; Hebrew does not include \fqa in Hebron\ft .\f*”
\p \v 9 “\rb Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*. \rb So Absalom got up|וַיָּ֖קָם\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Hebron|חֶבְרֽוֹנָה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb spies|מְרַגְּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb with this message|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: “\rb When you hear|כְּשָׁמְעֲכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sound|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the horn|הַשֹּׁפָ֔ר\rb*, \rb you are to say|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֕ם\rb*, ‘\rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb reigns|מָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְרֽוֹן׃\rb*!’”
\p \v 11 \rb Two hundred|מָאתַ֤יִם\rb* \rb men|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb accompanied|הָלְכ֞וּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֗וֹם\rb*. \rb They had been invited as guests|קְרֻאִ֖ים\rb* \rb and they went along|וְהֹלְכִ֣ים\rb* \rb innocently|לְתֻמָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb for they knew|יָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb nothing|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb about|כָּל־\rb* \rb the matter|דָּבָֽר׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb While Absalom was offering|בְּזָבְח֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sacrifices|הַזְּבָחִ֑ים\rb*, \rb he|אַ֠בְשָׁלוֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent for|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֨פֶל\rb* \rb the Gilonite|הַגִּֽילֹנִ֜י\rb*, \rb David’s|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb counselor|יוֹעֵ֣ץ\rb*, \rb to come from his hometown|מֵֽעִירוֹ֙\rb* \rb of Giloh|מִגִּלֹ֔ה\rb*.
\p \rb So the conspiracy|הַקֶּ֙שֶׁר֙\rb* \rb gained|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb strength|אַמִּ֔ץ\rb*, \rb and Absalom’s|אַבְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb following|וְהָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb kept|הוֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb increasing|וָרָ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.
\s1 David Flees Jerusalem
\p \v 13 \rb Then a messenger|הַמַּגִּ֔יד\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb and reported|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb The hearts|לֶב־\rb* \rb of the men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb are|הָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb with|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb And David|דָּ֠וִד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the servants|עֲבָדָ֨יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*, “\rb Arise|ק֣וּמוּ\rb* \rb and let us flee|וְנִבְרָ֔חָה\rb*, \rb or|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb we|לָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb will|תִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb escape|פְלֵיטָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*! \rb We must leave|לָלֶ֗כֶת\rb* \rb quickly|מַהֲר֣וּ\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb he will soon|יְמַהֵ֤ר\rb* \rb overtake us|וְהִשִּׂגָ֙נוּ֙\rb*, \rb heap|וְהִדִּ֤יחַ\rb* \rb disaster|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and put|וְהִכָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb to|לְפִי־\rb* \rb the sword|חָֽרֶב׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb The king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵֽי־\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Whatever|כְּכֹ֧ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb our lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb decides|יִבְחַ֛ר\rb*, \rb we are your servants|עֲבָדֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb set out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb*, \rb and his entire|וְכָל־\rb* \rb household|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb* \rb followed him|בְּרַגְלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb But he|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb left behind|וַיַּעֲזֹ֣ב\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֧שֶׂר\rb*\rb |נָשִׁ֛ים\rb* \rb concubines|פִּֽלַגְשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to take care of|לִשְׁמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb the palace|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb set out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb following him|בְּרַגְלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb He stopped|וַיַּעַמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb at|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb the last house|הַמֶּרְחָֽק׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb marched|עֹבְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb past|עַל־\rb* \rb him|יָד֔וֹ\rb* — \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Cherethites|הַכְּרֵתִ֖י\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Pelethites|הַפְּלֵתִ֑י\rb*, \rb and|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb Gittites|הַגִּתִּ֞ים\rb*\rb |אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had followed|בָּ֤אוּ\rb* \rb him|בְרַגְלוֹ֙\rb* \rb from Gath|מִגַּ֔ת\rb*\rb |עֹבְרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ittai|אִתַּ֣י\rb* \rb the Gittite|הַגִּתִּ֔י\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֧מָּה\rb* \rb should you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb go|תֵלֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֑נוּ\rb*? \rb Go back|שׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb and stay|וְשֵׁ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the new king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you are|אַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb both a foreigner|נָכְרִ֣י\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb an exile|גֹּלֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb from your homeland|לִמְקוֹמֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb In fact, you arrived|בּוֹאֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb only yesterday|תְּמ֣וֹל׀\rb*; \rb should I make you|אֲנוֹעֲךָ\rb* \rb wander around|לָלֶ֔כֶת\rb* \rb with us|עִמָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb today|וְהַיּ֞וֹם\rb* \rb while I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb do not know|הוֹלֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am going|הוֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb*? \rb Go back|שׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb and take|וְהָשֵׁ֧ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your brothers|אַחֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֖ךְ\rb*. \rb May the LORD show you loving devotion|חֶ֥סֶד\rb* \rb and faithfulness|וֶאֱמֶֽת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 15:20 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa May loving devotion and faithfulness be with you.\f*”
\p \v 21 \rb But Ittai|אִתַּ֛י\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֧עַן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb and as my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |כִּ֠י\rb* \rb lives|וְחֵי֙\rb*, \rb wherever|בִּמְק֞וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb may be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb*,\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb whether|אִם־\rb* \rb it means life|לְחַיִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb death|לְמָ֙וֶת֙\rb*, \rb there will|שָּׁ֣ם׀\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*!”
\p \v 22 “\rb March on then|וַעֲבֹ֑ר\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ittai|אִתַּ֖י\rb*.\rb |לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb So Ittai|אִתַּ֤י\rb* \rb the Gittite|הַגִּתִּי֙\rb* \rb marched past|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֞ר\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his men|אֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the little ones|הַטַּ֖ף\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Everyone|וְכָל־\rb* \rb in the countryside|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb was weeping|בּוֹכִים֙\rb* \rb loudly|ק֣וֹל\rb*\rb |גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb as all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb passed by|עֹֽבְרִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And as the king|וְהַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb crossed|עֹבֵר֙\rb* \rb the Kidron|קִדְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb Valley|בְּנַ֣חַל\rb*, \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb also passed|עֹבְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb toward|עַל־\rb* \rb the way|דֶ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb of|אֶת־\rb* \rb the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Zadok|צָד֜וֹק\rb* \rb was also|גַם־\rb* \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֣ם\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb were carrying|נֹֽשְׂאִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*. \rb And they set down|וַיַּצִּ֙קוּ֙\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb and Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֑ר\rb* \rb offered sacrifices|וַיַּ֖עַל\rb*\f + \fr 15:24 \ft Or \fqa Abiathar went up\f* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb had passed|תֹּ֥ם\rb*\rb |לַעֲב֥וֹר\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Zadok|לְצָד֔וֹק\rb*, “\rb Return|הָשֵׁ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*. \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I find|אֶמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb He will bring me back|וֶהֱשִׁבַ֕נִי\rb* \rb and let me see|וְהִרְאַ֥נִי\rb* \rb both it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb His dwelling place again|נָוֵֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb But if|וְאִם֙\rb*\rb |כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb He should say|יֹאמַ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb I do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb delight|חָפַ֖צְתִּי\rb* \rb in you|בָּ֑ךְ\rb*,’ \rb then here I am|הִנְנִ֕י\rb*; \rb let Him do|יַֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֕י\rb* \rb whatever|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb seems good|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb to Him|בְּעֵינָֽיו׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zadok|צָד֣וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*, “\rb Are you not a seer|הֲרוֹאֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֔ה\rb*?\f + \fr 15:27 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa Behold,\f* \rb Return|שֻׁ֥בָה\rb* \rb to the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*— \rb you with your son|בִּנְךָ֜\rb* \rb Ahimaaz|וַאֲחִימַ֨עַץ\rb*, \rb and Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֛ר\rb* \rb with his son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Jonathan|וִיהוֹנָתָ֧ן\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אִתְּכֶֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 15:27 \ft Literally \fqa your son Ahimaaz and Jonathan son of Abiathar, your two sons with you\f* \v 28 \rb See|רְאוּ֙\rb*, \rb I will|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb wait|מִתְמַהְמֵ֔הַּ\rb* \rb at the fords|בְּעַבְרוֹת\rb* \rb of the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb word|דָבָ֛ר\rb* \rb comes|בּ֥וֹא\rb* \rb from you|מֵעִמָּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to inform|לְהַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb me|לִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 29 \rb So Zadok|צָד֧וֹק\rb* \rb and Abiathar|וְאֶבְיָתָ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֨שֶׁב\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and stayed|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\s1 David Weeps at the Mount of Olives
\p \v 30 \rb But David|וְדָוִ֡ד\rb* \rb continued up|עֹלֶה֩\rb*\rb |בְמַעֲלֵ֨ה\rb* \rb the Mount of Olives|הַזֵּיתִ֜ים\rb*, \rb weeping|וּבוֹכֶ֗ה\rb* \rb as he went up|עֹלֶ֣ה׀\rb*. \rb His head|וְרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb was covered|חָפ֔וּי\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb was walking|הֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb barefoot|יָחֵ֑ף\rb*. \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb covered|חָפוּ֙\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb their heads|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and went up|וְעָל֥וּ\rb*, \rb weeping|וּבָכֹֽה׃\rb* \rb as they went|עָלֹ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb Now someone told|הִגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb David|וְדָוִד֙\rb*: “\rb Ahithophel is|אֲחִיתֹ֥פֶל\rb* \rb among the conspirators|בַּקֹּשְׁרִ֖ים\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*.”
\p \rb So David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb pleaded|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb O LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*, \rb please|נָ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb turn the counsel|עֲצַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֖פֶל\rb* \rb into foolishness|סַכֶּל־\rb*!”
\p \v 32 \rb When|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the summit|הָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb he used to worship|יִשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb Hushai|חוּשַׁ֣י\rb* \rb the Archite|הָאַרְכִּ֔י\rb* \rb was there|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb to meet him|לִקְרָאתוֹ֙\rb* \rb with his robe|כֻּתָּנְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb torn|קָר֙וּעַ֙\rb* \rb and dust|וַאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*, “\rb If|אִ֚ם\rb* \rb you go on|עָבַ֣רְתָּ\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb you will be|וְהָיִ֥תָ\rb* \rb a burden|לְמַשָּֽׂא׃\rb* \rb to me|עָלַ֖י\rb*. \v 34 \rb But you can thwart|וְהֵפַרְתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the counsel|עֲצַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹֽפֶל׃\rb* \rb for me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you return|תָּשׁ֗וּב\rb* \rb to the city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֤\rb* \rb to Absalom|לְאַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb*: ‘\rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb will be|אֶֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֨\rb*, \rb my king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*; \rb in the past|מֵאָ֔ז\rb* \rb I|וַֽאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb was your father’s|אָבִ֤יךָ\rb* \rb servant|עֶ֣בֶד\rb*, \rb but now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb will be your servant|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*.’
\p \v 35 \rb Will not|וַהֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb Zadok|צָד֥וֹק\rb* \rb and Abiathar|וְאֶבְיָתָ֖ר\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb be there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֙\rb*? \rb Report|תַּגִּ֕יד\rb* \rb to them|לְצָד֥וֹק\rb*\rb |וּלְאֶבְיָתָ֖ר\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֲנִֽים׃\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you hear|תִּשְׁמַע֙\rb* \rb from the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb*. \v 36 \rb Indeed|הִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb their two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb Ahimaaz|אֲחִימַ֣עַץ\rb* \rb son of Zadok|לְצָד֔וֹק\rb* \rb and Jonathan|וִיהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb son of Abiathar|לְאֶבְיָתָ֑ר\rb*, \rb are there|שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּם֙\rb*. \rb Send|וּשְׁלַחְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb them|בְּיָדָם֙\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb with everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you hear|תִּשְׁמָֽעוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 37 \rb So David’s|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb friend|רֵעֶ֥ה\rb* \rb Hushai|חוּשַׁ֛י\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb just as Absalom|וְאַבְשָׁלֹ֔ם\rb* \rb was entering|יָבֹ֖א\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*.
\c 16
\s1 David and Ziba
\p \v 1 \rb When David|וְדָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb had gone|עָבַ֤ר\rb* \rb a little|מְעַט֙\rb* \rb beyond the summit|מֵֽהָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb*, \rb Ziba|צִיבָ֛א\rb* \rb the servant|נַ֥עַר\rb* \rb of|מְפִי־\rb* \rb Mephibosheth|בֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb was there|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb to meet him|לִקְרָאת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb He had a pair|וְצֶ֨מֶד\rb* \rb of saddled|חֲבֻשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb donkeys|חֲמֹרִ֜ים\rb* \rb loaded with|וַעֲלֵיהֶם֩\rb* \rb two hundred loaves|מָאתַ֨יִם\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֜חֶם\rb*, \rb a hundred|וּמֵאָ֧ה\rb* \rb clusters of raisins|צִמּוּקִ֛ים\rb*, \rb a hundred|וּמֵ֥אָה\rb* \rb summer fruits|קַ֖יִץ\rb*, \rb and a skin|וְנֵ֥בֶל\rb* \rb of wine|יָֽיִן׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 “\rb Why|מָה־\rb* \rb do you have these|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb*?” \rb asked|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |צִיבָ֖א\rb*.
\p \rb Ziba|צִ֠יבָא\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The donkeys|הַחֲמוֹרִ֨ים\rb* \rb are for the king’s|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb household|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb to ride|לִרְכֹּ֗ב\rb*, \rb the bread|וּלְהַלֶּחֶם\rb* \rb and summer fruit|וְהַקַּ֙יִץ֙\rb* \rb are for the young men|הַנְּעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכ֣וֹל\rb*, \rb and the wine|וְהַיַּ֕יִן\rb* \rb is to refresh those|לִשְׁתּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb who become exhausted|הַיָּעֵ֖ף\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 “\rb Where|וְאַיֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb is your master’s|אֲדֹנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb grandson|בֶּן־\rb*?” \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \rb And Ziba|צִיבָ֜א\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Indeed|הִנֵּה֙\rb*, \rb he is staying|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he has said|אָמַ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*, \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb will restore|יָשִׁ֤יבוּ\rb* \rb to me|לִי֙\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַמְלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb of my grandfather|אָבִֽי׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 4 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Ziba|לְצִבָ֔א\rb*, “\rb All|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb that belongs|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |לִמְפִי־\rb* \rb to Mephibosheth|בֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb is now yours|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*!”
\p “\rb I humbly bow before you|הִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֵ֔יתִי\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Ziba|צִיבָא֙\rb*. “\rb May I find|אֶמְצָא־\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֥ן\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*!”
\s1 Shimei Curses David
\p \v 5 \rb As King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb approached|וּבָ֛א\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb Bahurim|בַּֽחוּרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb a man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb from the family|מִמִּשְׁפַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb was just|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁם֩\rb* \rb coming out|יוֹצֵ֜א\rb*. \rb His name|וּשְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb was Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֣י\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Gera|גֵּרָ֔א\rb*, \rb and as he approached|יֹצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |יָצ֖וֹא\rb*, \rb he kept yelling out curses|וּמְקַלֵּֽל׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb He threw stones|וַיְסַקֵּ֤ל\rb*\rb |בָּֽאֲבָנִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb at David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and at all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the servants|עַבְדֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb though the troops|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the mighty men were|הַגִּבֹּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb on David’s|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb right|מִימִינ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and left|וּמִשְּׂמֹאלֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb And as|וְכֹֽה־\rb* \rb he yelled curses|בְּקַֽלְל֑וֹ\rb*, \rb Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֖י\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֥ר\rb*, “\rb Get out|צֵ֥א\rb*, \rb get out|צֵ֛א\rb*, \rb you worthless|הַבְּלִיָּֽעַל׃\rb* \rb man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of bloodshed|הַדָּמִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb*! \v 8 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb has paid you back|הֵשִׁיב֩\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb for all|כֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the blood|דְּמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb*, \rb in whose|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb place|תַּחְתּוֹ\rb* \rb you have reigned|מָלַ֙כְתָּ֙\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has delivered|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמְּלוּכָ֔ה\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of your son|בְּנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֣וֹם\rb*. \rb See|וְהִנְּךָ֙\rb*, \rb you have come to ruin|בְּרָ֣עָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you are|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb a man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of bloodshed|דָּמִ֖ים\rb*!”
\p \v 9 \rb Then Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֤י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb should this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb dead|הַמֵּת֙\rb* \rb dog|הַכֶּ֤לֶב\rb* \rb curse|יְקַלֵּ֞ל\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*? \rb Let me go over|אֶעְבְּרָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֖א\rb* \rb and cut off his head|רֹאשֽׁוֹ׃ס\rb*\rb |וְאָסִ֥ירָה\rb*!”\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb But the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb have I|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb to do with you|וְלָכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb O sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרֻיָ֑ה\rb*? \rb If|כִּי\rb* \rb he curses me|יְקַלֵּ֗ל\rb* \rb because|וְכִי\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb told|אָ֤מַר\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb*, ‘\rb Curse|קַלֵּ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*,’ \rb who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb can ask|יֹאמַ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Why|מַדּ֖וּעַ\rb* \rb did you do|עָשִׂ֥יתָה\rb* \rb this|כֵּֽן׃ס\rb*?’”
\p \v 11 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abishai|אֲבִישַׁי֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb my own son|בְנִ֛י\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |יָצָ֥א\rb* \rb my own flesh and blood|מִמֵּעַ֖י\rb*, \rb seeks|מְבַקֵּ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb*.\rb |וְאַ֨ף\rb* \rb How much more|כִּֽי־\rb*, \rb then|עַתָּ֜ה\rb*,\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb this Benjamite|הַיְמִינִ֗י\rb*! \rb Leave him alone|הַנִּ֤חוּ\rb*\rb |לוֹ֙\rb* \rb and let him curse me|וִֽיקַלֵּ֔ל\rb*, \rb for the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has told|אָֽמַר־\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb so|כִּ֥י\rb*. \v 12 \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will see|יִרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb my affliction|בְּעֲוֹנִי\rb* \rb and repay|וְהֵשִׁ֨יב\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb* \rb with good|טוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb for|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the cursing I receive|קִלְלָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb So David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb proceeded|וַיֵּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb along the road|בַּדָּ֑רֶךְס\rb* \rb as Shimei|וְשִׁמְעִ֡י\rb* \rb went|הֹלֵךְ֩\rb* \rb along the ridge|בְּצֵ֨לַע\rb* \rb of the hill|הָהָ֜ר\rb* \rb opposite him|לְעֻמָּת֗וֹ\rb*. \rb As Shimei went|הָלוֹךְ֙\rb*, \rb he yelled curses|וַיְקַלֵּ֔ל\rb*, \rb threw stones|וַיְסַקֵּ֤ל\rb*,\rb |בָּֽאֲבָנִים֙\rb* \rb and flung|וְעִפַּ֖ר\rb* \rb dust|בֶּעָפָֽר׃פ\rb* \rb at David|לְעֻמָּת֔וֹ\rb*. \v 14 \rb Finally, the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb*,\f + \fr 16:14 \ft Some LXX manuscripts \fqa arrived at the Jordan\f* \rb exhausted|עֲיֵפִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And there|שָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb he refreshed himself|וַיִּנָּפֵ֖שׁ\rb*.
\s1 The Counsel of Ahithophel and Hushai
\p \v 15 \rb Then Absalom|וְאַבְשָׁל֗וֹם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָם֙\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb came|בָּ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and Ahithophel was|וַאֲחִיתֹ֖פֶל\rb* \rb with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And|וַיְהִ֗י\rb*\rb |כַּֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb friend|רֵעֶ֥ה\rb* \rb Hushai|חוּשַׁ֧י\rb* \rb the Archite|הָאַרְכִּ֛י\rb* \rb went|בָּ֞א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |חוּשַׁי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|אַבְשָׁלֹ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Long live|יְחִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*! \rb Long live|יְחִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 17 “\rb Is this|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the loyalty|חַסְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb you show|אֶת־\rb* \rb your friend|רֵעֶ֑ךָ\rb*?” \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |חוּשַׁ֔י\rb*. “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb did you not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|הָלַ֖כְתָּ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb your friend|רֵעֶֽךָ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 18 “\rb Not at all|לֹ֕א\rb*,” \rb Hushai|חוּשַׁי֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אַבְשָׁלֹם֒\rb*. “\rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the one|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb chosen|בָּחַ֧ר\rb* \rb by the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb by this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people|וְהָעָ֥ם\rb*, \rb and by all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* — \rb his|לֹא\rb* \rb I will be|אֶהְיֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb and with him|וְאִתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb I will remain|אֵשֵֽׁב׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Furthermore|וְהַשֵּׁנִ֗ית\rb*, \rb whom|לְמִי֙\rb* \rb should I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb serve|אֶֽעֱבֹ֔ד\rb* \rb if not|הֲל֖וֹא\rb* \rb his son|בְנ֑וֹ\rb*? \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I served|עָבַ֙דְתִּי֙\rb* \rb in your father’s|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb*, \rb so also|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb I will serve|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְפָנֶֽיךָ׃פ\rb* \rb in yours|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb Then Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֑פֶל\rb*, “\rb Give me|הָב֥וּ\rb* \rb counsel|עֵצָ֖ה\rb*. \rb What|מַֽה־\rb* \rb should we do|נַּעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 21 \rb Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֙פֶל֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אַבְשָׁלֹ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Sleep with|בּ֚וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your father’s|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb concubines|פִּלַגְשֵׁ֣י\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he has left|הִנִּ֖יחַ\rb* \rb to take care of|לִשְׁמ֣וֹר\rb* \rb the palace|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*. \rb When all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb hears|וְשָׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have become a stench|נִבְאַ֣שְׁתָּ\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb then the hands|יְדֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who are|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb will be strengthened|וְחָ֣זְק֔וּ\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb So they pitched|וַיַּטּ֧וּ\rb* \rb a tent|הָאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb for Absalom|לְאַבְשָׁל֛וֹם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the roof|הַגָּ֑ג\rb*, \rb and he|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb slept with|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb concubines|פִּֽלַגְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Now in those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb the advice|וַעֲצַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֗פֶל\rb*\rb |יָעַץ֙\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb was like|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the consultation|יִשְׁאַלִ֖־\rb* \rb of the word|בִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Such|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb was the regard|כָּל־\rb* \rb that both|גַּם־\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb and|גַּ֥ם\rb* \rb Absalom|לְאַבְשָׁלֹֽם׃ס\rb* \rb had for Ahithophel’s|אֲחִיתֹ֔פֶל\rb* \rb advice|עֲצַ֣ת\rb*.
\c 17
\s1 Hushai Counters Ahithophel’s Advice
\p \v 1 \rb Furthermore, Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֖פֶל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֹ֑ם\rb*, “\rb Let me choose|אֶבְחֲרָ֣ה\rb*\rb |נָּ֗א\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb and set out|וְאָק֛וּמָה\rb* \rb tonight|הַלָּֽיְלָה׃\rb* \rb in pursuit of|וְאֶרְדְּפָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb*. \v 2 \rb I will attack him|וְאָב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |עָלָ֗יו\rb* \rb while he|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb is weak|וּרְפֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |יָדַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and weary|יָגֵ֙עַ֙\rb*; \rb I will throw him into a panic|וְהַֽחֲרַדְתִּ֣י\rb*,\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb will flee|וְנָ֖ס\rb*; \rb I will strike down|וְהִכֵּיתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb only|לְבַדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \v 3 \rb and bring all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb back|וְאָשִׁ֥יבָה\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb as a bride|הַכֹּ֔ל\rb* \rb returning to her husband|כְּשׁ֣וּב\rb*. \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb seek the life|מְבַקֵּ֔שׁ\rb* \rb of only one man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*;\f + \fr 17:3 \ft LXX; see also DSS; MT \fqa and bring all the people back to you. When everyone returns except the man you seek,\f* \rb then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb at peace|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb This proposal|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb seemed|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb good|וַיִּישַׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֹ֑ם\rb*\rb |וּבְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Summon|קְרָ֣א\rb*\rb |נָ֔א\rb* \rb Hushai|לְחוּשַׁ֣י\rb* \rb the Archite|הָאַרְכִּ֑י\rb* \rb as well|גַּ֖ם\rb*, \rb and let us hear|וְנִשְׁמְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb has to say|בְּפִ֖יו\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb So Hushai|חוּשַׁי֮\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֒\rb*, \rb who|אַבְשָׁל֨וֹם\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֜יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb told him|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*, “\rb Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֔פֶל\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb proposal|כַּדָּבָ֤ר\rb*. \rb Should we carry it out|הֲנַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |דְּבָר֑וֹ\rb*? \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb not|אַ֖יִן\rb*, \rb what do you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb say|דַבֵּֽר׃ס\rb*?”
\p \v 7 \rb Hushai|חוּשַׁ֖י\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*, “\rb This|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb time|בַּפַּ֥עַם\rb* \rb the advice|הָעֵצָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֖פֶל\rb*\rb |יָעַ֥ץ\rb* \rb is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb sound|טוֹבָ֧ה\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb He|חוּשַׁ֗י\rb* \rb continued|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb know|יָ֠דַעְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֨יךָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his men|אֲנָשָׁ֜יו\rb*.\rb |כִּ֧י\rb* \rb They are|הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb mighty men|גִבֹּרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and as fierce|וּמָרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |נֶ֙פֶשׁ֙\rb*\rb |הֵ֔מָּה\rb* \rb as a wild|בַּשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb bear|כְּדֹ֥ב\rb* \rb robbed of her cubs|שַׁכּ֖וּל\rb*. \rb Moreover, your father is|וְאָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb who will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb spend the night|יָלִ֖ין\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Surely|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb by now|עַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb is hiding|נֶחְבָּא֙\rb* \rb in a|בְּאַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb cave|הַפְּחָתִ֔ים\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb some other|בְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb location|הַמְּקוֹמֹ֑ת\rb*. \rb If some of your troops fall|כִּנְפֹ֤ל\rb* \rb first|בַּתְּחִלָּ֔ה\rb*,\f + \fr 17:9 \ft Or \fqa If he should attack your troops first\f* \rb whoever hears of it|וְשָׁמַ֤ע\rb*\rb |הַשֹּׁמֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb will say|וְאָמַ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb There|הָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb has been|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb a slaughter|מַגֵּפָ֔ה\rb* \rb among the troops|בָּעָ֕ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb follow|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֹֽם׃\rb*.’ \v 10 \rb Then|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb even|גַם־\rb* \rb the most valiant|חַ֗יִל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb soldier|בֶּן־\rb* \rb with the heart|לִבּ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |כְּלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of a lion|הָאַרְיֵ֖ה\rb* \rb will melt with fear|הִמֵּ֣ס\rb*\rb |יִמָּ֑ס\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb knows|יֹדֵ֤עַ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is a mighty man|גִבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb who has valiant|חַ֖יִל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb men|וּבְנֵי־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Instead|כִּ֣י\rb*, \rb I advise|יָעַ֗צְתִּי\rb* \rb that all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb from Dan|מִדָּן֙\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שֶׁ֔בַע\rb*— \rb a multitude|לָרֹ֑ב\rb* \rb like the sand|כַּח֥וֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the seashore|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*— \rb be gathered|הֵ֠אָסֹף\rb*\rb |יֵאָסֵ֨ף\rb* \rb to you|עָלֶ֤יךָ\rb*, \rb and that you yourself|וּפָנֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb lead them|הֹלְכִ֖ים\rb* \rb into battle|בַּקְרָֽב׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Then we will attack|וּבָ֣אנוּ\rb* \rb David|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*\rb |בְּאַחַת\rb* \rb wherever|הַמְּקוֹמֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb we find him|נִמְצָ֣א\rb*,\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb and we|וְנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb will descend|יִפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb on him|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb like|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb dew|הַטַּ֖ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And of all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb even|גַּם־\rb* \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb will remain|נ֥וֹתַר\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he retreats|יֵֽאָסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a city|עִיר֙\rb*, \rb all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb will bring|וְהִשִּׂ֧יאוּ\rb* \rb ropes|חֲבָלִ֑ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֖יא\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb*, \rb and we will drag|וְסָחַ֤בְנוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb down to|עַד־\rb* \rb the valley|הַנַּ֔חַל\rb* \rb until|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb even|גַּם־\rb* \rb a pebble|צְרֽוֹר׃פ\rb* \rb can be found|נִמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Then Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The advice|עֲצַת֙\rb* \rb of Hushai|חוּשַׁ֣י\rb* \rb the Archite|הָאַרְכִּ֔י\rb* \rb is better|טוֹבָ֗ה\rb* \rb than that|מֵעֲצַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֑פֶל\rb*.” \rb For the LORD|וַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb had purposed|צִוָּ֗ה\rb* \rb to thwart|לְהָפֵ֞ר\rb* \rb the good|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb counsel|עֲצַ֤ת\rb* \rb of Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֙פֶל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in order to|לְבַעֲב֗וּר\rb* \rb bring|הָבִ֧יא\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\s1 Hushai’s Warning Saves David
\p \v 15 \rb So Hushai|חוּשַׁ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Zadok|צָד֤וֹק\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָר֙\rb*, \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb*, “\rb This is what|כָּזֹ֣את\rb*\rb |וְכָזֹ֗את\rb* \rb Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֙פֶל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has advised|יָעַ֤ץ\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֹ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and this is what|וְכָזֹ֥את\rb*\rb |וְכָזֹ֖את\rb* \rb I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb have advised|יָעַ֥צְתִּי\rb*. \v 16 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb send|שִׁלְח֣וּ\rb* \rb quickly|מְהֵרָה֩\rb* \rb and tell|וְהַגִּ֨ידוּ\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֜ד\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb spend|תָּ֤לֶן\rb* \rb the night|הַלַּ֙יְלָה֙\rb* \rb at the fords|בְּעַֽרְב֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb*, \rb but|וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb be sure to cross over|עָב֣וֹר\rb*\rb |תַּעֲב֑וֹר\rb*. \rb Otherwise|פֶּ֚ן\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb will be swallowed up|יְבֻלַּ֣ע\rb*.’”
\p \v 17 \rb Now Jonathan|וִיהוֹנָתָ֨ן\rb* \rb and Ahimaaz|וַאֲחִימַ֜עַץ\rb* \rb were staying|עֹמְדִ֣ים\rb*\rb |בְּעֵין־\rb* \rb at En-rogel|רֹגֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb where a servant girl|הַשִּׁפְחָה֙\rb* \rb would come|וְהָלְכָ֤ה\rb* \rb and pass along information|וְהִגִּ֣ידָה\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb They|וְהֵם֙\rb* \rb in turn would go|יֵֽלְכ֔וּ\rb* \rb and inform|וְהִגִּ֖ידוּ\rb* \rb King|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they dared|יוּכְל֛וּ\rb* \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be seen|לְהֵרָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb entering|לָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽירָה׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb But a young man|נַ֔עַר\rb* \rb did see|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb Absalom|לְאַבְשָׁלֹ֑ם\rb*. \rb So the two|שְׁנֵיהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּלְכוּ֩\rb* \rb quickly|מְהֵרָ֜ה\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb in Bahurim|בְּבַחוּרִ֗ים\rb*. \rb He had|וְל֥וֹ\rb* \rb a well|בְאֵ֛ר\rb* \rb in his courtyard|בַּחֲצֵר֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and they climbed down|וַיֵּ֥רְדוּ\rb* \rb into it|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Then the man’s wife|הָאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a covering|הַמָּסָךְ֙\rb*, \rb spread|וַתִּפְרֹ֤שׂ\rb* \rb it over|עַל־\rb* \rb the mouth|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the well|הַבְּאֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb and scattered|וַתִּשְׁטַ֥ח\rb* \rb grain|הָֽרִפ֑וֹת\rb* \rb over it|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb so nobody|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb would know|נוֹדַ֖ע\rb* \rb a thing|דָּבָֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb When Absalom’s|אַבְשָׁל֨וֹם\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵי֩\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb at the house|הַבַּ֗יְתָה\rb*, \rb they asked|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Where|אַיֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb are Ahimaaz|אֲחִימַ֙עַץ֙\rb* \rb and Jonathan|וִיה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*?”
\p “\rb They have crossed over|עָבְר֖וּ\rb* \rb the brook|מִיכַ֣ל\rb*\rb |הַמָּ֑יִם\rb*,” \rb she|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*. \rb The men searched|וַיְבַקְשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb but did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb find them|מָצָ֔אוּ\rb*, \rb so they returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the men had gone|לֶכְתָּ֗ם\rb*, \rb Ahimaaz and Jonathan climbed up|וַֽיַּעֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb out of the well|מֵֽהַבְּאֵ֔ר\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֣לְכ֔וּ\rb* \rb to inform|וַיַּגִּ֖דוּ\rb* \rb King|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֗ד\rb*, “\rb Get up|ק֣וּמוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and cross over|וְעִבְר֤וּ\rb* \rb the river|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb at once|מְהֵרָה֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹֽפֶל׃\rb* \rb has given this|כָ֛כָה\rb* \rb advice|יָעַ֥ץ\rb* \rb against you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb So David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and crossed|וַיַּעַבְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*. \rb By|עַד־\rb* \rb daybreak|א֣וֹר\rb*\rb |הַבֹּ֗קֶר\rb*,\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb there was no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb one|אַחַד֙\rb* \rb left|נֶעְדָּ֔ר\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb crossed|עָבַ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb When Ahithophel|וַאֲחִיתֹ֣פֶל\rb* \rb saw|רָאָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb his advice|עֲצָתוֹ֒\rb* \rb had not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb been followed|נֶעֶשְׂתָה֮\rb*, \rb he saddled|וַיַּחֲבֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb his donkey|הַחֲמ֗וֹר\rb* \rb and set out|וַיָּ֜קָם\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּיתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb his hometown|עִיר֔וֹ\rb*. \rb He put his affairs|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בֵּית֖וֹ\rb* \rb in order|וַיְצַ֥ו\rb* \rb and hanged himself|וַיֵּחָנַ֑ק\rb*. \rb So he died|וַיָּ֕מָת\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in his father’s|אָבִֽיו׃ס\rb* \rb tomb|בְּקֶ֥בֶר\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Then David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb went|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to Mahanaim|מַחֲנָ֑יְמָה\rb*, \rb and Absalom|וְאַבְשָׁלֹ֗ם\rb* \rb crossed|עָבַר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*\rb |ה֕וּא\rb* \rb with|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*. \v 25 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֹ֛ם\rb* \rb had appointed|שָׂ֧ם\rb* \rb Amasa|עֲמָשָׂ֗א\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the army|הַצָּבָ֑א\rb* \rb in place|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb*. \rb Amasa|וַעֲמָשָׂ֣א\rb* \rb was the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of a man|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb Ithra|יִתְרָ֣א\rb*,\f + \fr 17:25 \fqa Ithra \ft is a variant of \fqa Jether\ft ; see 1 Kings 2:5.\f* \rb the Ishmaelite|הַיִּשְׂרְאֵלִ֔י\rb*\f + \fr 17:25 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also 1 Chronicles 2:17); MT and other LXX manuscripts \fqa Israelite\f* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had married|בָּא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Abigail|אֲבִיגַ֣ל\rb*,\f + \fr 17:25 \ft Or \fqa Abigal\ft , a variant of \fqa Abigail\f* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Nahash|נָחָ֔שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 17:25 \ft Or \fqa of Jesse\ft ; see DSS and 1 Chronicles 2:13–16\f* \rb and sister|אֲח֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֖ה\rb* \rb the mother|אֵ֥ם\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָֽב׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb So the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and Absalom|וְאַבְשָׁלֹ֔ם\rb* \rb camped|וַיִּ֤חַן\rb* \rb in the land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָֽד׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb When David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb came|כְּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to Mahanaim|מַחֲנָ֑יְמָה\rb*, \rb he was met by Shobi|וְשֹׁבִ֨י\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Nahash|נָחָ֜שׁ\rb* \rb from Rabbah|מֵרַבַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֗וֹן\rb*, \rb Machir|וּמָכִ֤יר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ammiel|עַמִּיאֵל֙\rb*\rb |מִלֹּ֣א\rb* \rb from Lo-debar|דְבָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and Barzillai|וּבַרְזִלַּ֥י\rb* \rb the Gileadite|הַגִּלְעָדִ֖י\rb* \rb from Rogelim|מֵרֹגְלִֽים׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb They brought beds|מִשְׁכָּ֤ב\rb*, \rb basins|וְסַפּוֹת֙\rb*, \rb and earthen|יוֹצֵ֔ר\rb* \rb vessels|וּכְלִ֣י\rb*, \rb as well as wheat|וְחִטִּ֥ים\rb*, \rb barley|וּשְׂעֹרִ֖ים\rb*, \rb flour|וְקֶ֣מַח\rb*, \rb roasted grain|וְקָלִ֑י\rb*, \rb beans|וּפ֥וֹל\rb*, \rb lentils|וַעֲדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*,\rb |וְקָלִֽי׃\rb*\f + \fr 17:28 \ft Most LXX manuscripts and Syriac; Hebrew includes \fqa roasted seeds\ft .\f* \v 29 \rb honey|וּדְבַ֣שׁ\rb*, \rb curds|וְחֶמְאָ֗ה\rb*, \rb sheep|וְצֹאן֙\rb*, \rb and cheese|וּשְׁפ֣וֹת\rb* \rb from the herd|בָּקָ֔ר\rb*\rb |הִגִּ֧ישׁוּ\rb* \rb for David|לְדָוִ֛ד\rb* \rb and his people|וְלָעָ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכ֑וֹל\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they said|אָמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb The people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb have become hungry|רָעֵ֛ב\rb*, \rb exhausted|וְעָיֵ֥ף\rb*, \rb and thirsty|וְצָמֵ֖א\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*.”
\c 18
\s1 Absalom Killed
\p \v 1 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb reviewed|וַיִּפְקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb his troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and appointed|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of thousands|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb and of hundreds|מֵאֽוֹת׃\rb*\rb |וְשָׂרֵ֥י\rb*. \v 2 \rb He|דָּוִ֜ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent out|וַיְשַׁלַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֗ם\rb*, \rb a third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֤ית\rb*\rb |בְּיַד־\rb* \rb under Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb*, \rb a third|וְ֠הַשְּׁלִשִׁית\rb*\rb |בְּיַ֨ד\rb* \rb under Joab’s|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb* \rb Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֤י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָה֙\rb*, \rb and a third|וְהַ֨שְּׁלִשִׁ֔ת\rb*\rb |בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb under Ittai|אִתַּ֣י\rb* \rb the Gittite|הַגִּתִּ֑יס\rb*. \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will surely march out|יָצֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֵצֵ֛א\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb as well|גַּם־\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb But the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb pleaded|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go out|תֵצֵ֗א\rb*! \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb we have to flee|נֹ֨ס\rb*\rb |נָנ֜וּס\rb*,\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb they will not care|יָשִׂ֧ימוּ\rb*\rb |לֵ֗ב\rb* \rb about us|אֵלֵ֣ינוּ\rb*. \rb Even if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb half of us|חֶצְיֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb die|יָמֻ֤תוּ\rb*, \rb they will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb care|יָשִׂ֤ימוּ\rb*\rb |לֵ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֵלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*. \rb But|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |עַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb you are worth|כָמֹ֖נוּ\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb thousand of us|אֲלָפִ֑ים\rb*.\f + \fr 18:3 \ft Two Hebrew manuscripts, some LXX manuscripts, and Vulgate; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa care; for now there are ten thousand like us\f* \rb It is better|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb now|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb if|כִּי־\rb* \rb you|תִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb support|לַעְזִיר׃ס\rb* \rb us|לָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb from the city|מֵעִ֖יר\rb*.”
\p \v 4 “\rb I will do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb seems best|יִיטַ֥ב\rb* \rb to you|בְּעֵינֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*,” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*. \rb So he|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֤ד\rb* \rb beside|אֶל־\rb*\rb |יַ֣ד\rb* \rb the gate|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb*, \rb while all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb marched out|יָֽצְא֔וּ\rb* \rb by hundreds|לְמֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb and by thousands|וְלַאֲלָפִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Now the king|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb Joab|י֠וֹאָב\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֤י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Ittai|אִתַּי֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Treat the young man|לַנַּ֣עַר\rb* \rb Absalom|לְאַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb gently|לְאַט־\rb* \rb for my sake|לִ֖י\rb*.” \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמְע֗וּ\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb orders|בְּצַוֺּ֥ת\rb* \rb to each|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the commanders|הַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb regarding|עַל־\rb*\rb |דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb So David’s army|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb marched|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb into the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to engage|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb took place|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb in the forest|בְּיַ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb There|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb were defeated|וַיִּנָּ֤גְפוּ\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and the slaughter|הַמַּגֵּפָ֧ה\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִי־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֞ם\rb* \rb great|גְדוֹלָ֛ה\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*— \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand men|אָֽלֶף׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb |וַתְּהִי־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֧ם\rb* \rb The battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb spread|נָפֹצֵית\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb countryside|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the forest|הַיַּ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb devoured|לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb more|וַיֶּ֤רֶב\rb* \rb people|בָּעָ֔ם\rb* \rb than|מֵאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |אָכְלָ֛ה\rb* \rb the sword|הַחֶ֖רֶב\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Now Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb was riding|רֹכֵ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his mule|הַפֶּ֗רֶד\rb* \rb when he|וְאַבְשָׁל֞וֹם\rb* \rb met|וַיִּקָּרֵא֙\rb* \rb the servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb and as the mule|הַפֶּ֡רֶד\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the thick branches|שׂוֹבֶךְ֩\rb* \rb of a large|הַגְּדוֹלָ֜ה\rb* \rb oak|הָאֵלָ֨ה\rb*,\f + \fr 18:9 \ft Or \fqa large terebinth \ft or \fqa very great tree\ft ; similarly in verses 10 and 14\f* \rb Absalom’s head|רֹאשׁ֣וֹ\rb* \rb was caught fast|וַיֶּחֱזַ֧ק\rb* \rb in the tree|בָאֵלָ֗ה\rb*. \rb The mule|וְהַפֶּ֥רֶד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb under him|תַּחְתָּ֖יו\rb* \rb kept going|עָבָֽר׃\rb*, \rb so that he was suspended|וַיֻּתַּן֙\rb* \rb in midair|בֵּ֤ין\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*. \v 10 \rb When one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb of the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb saw this|וַיַּרְא֙\rb*, \rb he told|וַיַּגֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb Joab|לְיוֹאָ֑ב\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I just|הִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb saw|רָאִ֣יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֹ֔ם\rb* \rb hanging|תָּל֖וּי\rb* \rb in an oak tree|בָּאֵלָֽה׃\rb*!”
\p \v 11 “\rb You just|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb saw him|רָאִ֔יתָ\rb*!” \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb*\rb |לָאִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |הַמַּגִּ֣יד\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb exclaimed|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Why|וּמַדּ֛וּעַ\rb* \rb did you not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb strike him|הִכִּית֥וֹ\rb* \rb to the ground|אָ֑רְצָה\rb*\rb |וְעָלַ֗י\rb* \rb right there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*? \rb I would have given|לָ֤תֶת\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb ten shekels|עֲשָׂ֣רָה\rb* \rb of silver|כֶ֔סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 18:11 \fqa 10 shekels \ft is approximately 4 ounces or 114 grams of silver.\f* \rb and a|אֶחָֽת׃\rb* \rb warrior’s belt|וַחֲגֹרָ֖ה\rb*!”
\p \v 12 \rb The man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, “\rb Even if|וְלֹא\rb*\rb |אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb a thousand shekels|אֶ֣לֶף\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 18:12 \fqa 1,000 shekels \ft is approximately 25.1 pounds or 11.4 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb were weighed out|שֹׁקֵ֤ל\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb my hands|כַּפַּי֙\rb*, \rb I would not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb raise|אֶשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb my hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb we heard|בְאָזְנֵ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֹ֠תְךָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb command you|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֤י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Ittai|אִתַּי֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* ‘\rb Protect|שִׁמְרוּ־\rb* \rb the young man|בַּנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb Absalom|בְּאַבְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb for my sake|מִ֕י\rb*.\f + \fr 18:12 \ft A few Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, Vulgate, and Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Whoever you may be, protect the young man Absalom. \ft or \fqa Let no one touch the young man Absalom.\f*’ \v 13 \rb If|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb I had jeopardized|עָשִׂ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb my own life|בְנַפְשׁוֹ\rb*\f + \fr 18:13 \ft Or \fqa If I had dealt treacherously against his life\f*— \rb and nothing|לֹא־\rb* \rb is hidden|יִכָּחֵ֣ד\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*— \rb you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb would have abandoned|תִּתְיַצֵּ֥ב\rb* \rb me|מִנֶּֽגֶד׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb But Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I am not|לֹא־\rb* \rb going to wait|אֹחִ֣ילָה\rb* \rb like this|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb with you|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*!” \rb And he took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֨ה\rb* \rb spears|שְׁבָטִ֜ים\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּכַפּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and thrust them|וַיִּתְקָעֵם֙\rb* \rb through the heart|בְּלֵ֣ב\rb* \rb of Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb while he was still|עוֹדֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb alive|חַ֖י\rb*\rb |בְּלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb in the oak tree|הָאֵלָֽה׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And ten|עֲשָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb young men|נְעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb who carried|נֹשְׂאֵ֖י\rb* \rb Joab’s|יוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \rb armor|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb surrounded|וַיָּסֹ֙בּוּ֙\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb*, \rb struck|וַיַּכּ֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb*, \rb and killed him|וַיְמִיתֻֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Then Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb blew|וַיִּתְקַ֤ע\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשֹּׁפָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb broke off|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb their pursuit|מִרְדֹ֖ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had restrained them|חָשַׂ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |הָעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb They took|וַיִּקְח֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֗וֹם\rb*, \rb cast|וַיַּשְׁלִ֨יכוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a large|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb pit|הַפַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb in the forest|בַיַּ֙עַר֙\rb*, \rb and piled|וַיַּצִּ֧בוּ\rb* \rb a huge|גָּד֣וֹל\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb mound|גַּל־\rb* \rb of stones|אֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb over him|עָלָ֛יו\rb*. \rb Meanwhile, all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb fled|נָ֖סוּ\rb*, \rb each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his home|לְאָהֳלוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb During his lifetime|בְחַיָּו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb Absalom|וְאַבְשָׁלֹ֣ם\rb*\rb |לָקַ֗ח\rb* \rb had set up|וַיַּצֶּב־\rb* \rb for himself|ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb a pillar|מַצֶּ֙בֶת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the King’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb Valley|בְּעֵֽמֶק־\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he had said|אָמַר֙\rb*, “\rb I have no|אֵֽין־\rb*\rb |לִ֣י\rb* \rb son|בֵ֔ן\rb* \rb to|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb preserve the memory|הַזְכִּ֣יר\rb* \rb of my name|שְׁמִ֑י\rb*.” \rb So he gave|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb the pillar|לַמַּצֶּ֙בֶת֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb his name|שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb it is called|וַיִּקָּ֤רֵא\rb*\rb |לָהּ֙\rb* \rb Absalom’s|אַבְשָׁלֹ֔ם\rb* \rb Monument|יַ֣ד\rb*.
\s1 David Mourns for Absalom
\p \v 19 \rb Then Ahimaaz|וַאֲחִימַ֤עַץ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָדוֹק֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Please|נָּ֔א\rb* \rb let me run|אָר֣וּצָה\rb* \rb and tell the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb the good news|וַאֲבַשְּׂרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has avenged him|שְׁפָט֥וֹ\rb* \rb of|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb his enemies|אֹיְבָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb But Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb are not|לֹא֩\rb* \rb the man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb to take good news|בְּשֹׂרָ֤ה\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*. \rb You may do|וּבִשַּׂרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb it another|אַחֵ֑ר\rb* \rb day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb*, \rb but you must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do so|תְבַשֵּׂ֔ר\rb* \rb today|וְהַיּ֤וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּה֙\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |עַל\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb is dead|מֵֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb So Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to a Cushite|לַכּוּשִׁ֔י\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֛ךְ\rb*, \rb tell|הַגֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have seen|רָאִ֑יתָה\rb*.” \rb The Cushite|כוּשִׁ֛י\rb* \rb bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֧חוּ\rb* \rb to Joab|לְיוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb and took off running|וַיָּרֹֽץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Ahimaaz|אֲחִימַ֤עַץ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָדוֹק֙\rb*, \rb however, persisted|וַיֹּ֨סֶף\rb*\rb |ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*,\rb |וִ֣יהִי\rb* “\rb No matter what|מָ֔ה\rb*, \rb please|נָּ֥א\rb* \rb let me|אָ֖נִי\rb* \rb also|גַם־\rb* \rb run|אָרֻֽצָה־\rb* \rb behind|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Cushite|הַכּוּשִׁ֑י\rb*!”
\p “\rb My son|בְּנִ֔י\rb*,” \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb why|לָֽמָּה־\rb*\rb |זֶּ֞ה\rb* \rb do you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb want to run|רָץ֙\rb*, \rb since you will|וּלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb not|אֵין־\rb* \rb receive|מֹצֵֽאת׃\rb* \rb a reward|בְּשׂוֹרָ֥ה\rb*?”
\p \v 23 “\rb No matter what|מָ֣ה\rb*, \rb I want to run|אָר֔וּץ\rb*!” \rb he replied|וִיהִי־\rb*.
\p “\rb Then run|ר֑וּץ\rb*!” \rb Joab told|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \rb So Ahimaaz|אֲחִימַ֙עַץ֙\rb* \rb ran|וַיָּ֤רָץ\rb* \rb by way|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the plain|הַכִּכָּ֔ר\rb*\f + \fr 18:23 \ft That is, the plain of the Jordan\f* \rb and outran|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Cushite|הַכּוּשִֽׁי׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Now David|וְדָוִ֥ד\rb* \rb was sitting|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb between|בֵּין־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb gates|הַשְּׁעָרִ֑ים\rb* \rb when the watchman|הַצֹּפֶ֜ה\rb* \rb went up|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the roof|גַּ֤ג\rb* \rb of the gateway|הַשַּׁ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb by|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wall|הַ֣חוֹמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb looked out|וַיִּשָּׂ֤א\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֔רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb running alone|רָ֥ץ\rb*\rb |לְבַדּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb So he|הַצֹּפֶה֙\rb* \rb called out|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*.
\p “\rb If he is alone|אִם־\rb*\rb |לְבַדּ֖וֹ\rb*,” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb he bears|בְּפִ֑יו\rb* \rb good news|בְּשׂוֹרָ֣ה\rb*.”
\p \rb As the first runner drew|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָל֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb near|וְקָרֵֽב׃\rb*, \v 26 \rb the watchman|הַצֹּפֶה֮\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb another|אַחֵ֣ר\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb running|רָץ֒\rb*, \rb and he called out|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |הַצֹּפֶה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the gatekeeper|הַשֹּׁעֵ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּה־\rb*! \rb Another man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb is running alone|רָ֣ץ\rb*\rb |לְבַדּ֑וֹ\rb*!”
\p “\rb This one|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb brings good news|מְבַשֵּֽׂר׃\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb The watchman|הַצֹּפֶ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb The first man|הָרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb appears|רֹאֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to me|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb to be running|מְרוּצַ֣ת\rb* \rb like Ahimaaz|אֲחִימַ֣עַץ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָד֑וֹק\rb*\rb |כִּמְרֻצַ֖ת\rb*.”
\p “\rb This|זֶ֔ה\rb* \rb is a good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb man|אִֽישׁ־\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*. “\rb He comes|יָבֽוֹא׃\rb* \rb with|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb good|טוֹבָ֖ה\rb* \rb news|בְּשׂוֹרָ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb Then Ahimaaz|אֲחִימַ֗עַץ\rb* \rb called out|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, “\rb All is well|שָׁל֔וֹם\rb*!” \rb And he bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֧חוּ\rb* \rb facedown|לְאַפָּ֖יו\rb*\rb |אָ֑רְצָהס\rb* \rb before the king|לַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \rb He continued|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Blessed be|בָּרוּךְ֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*!\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb He has delivered up|סִגַּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men|הָ֣אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb raised|נָשְׂא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their hands|יָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb against my lord|בַּֽאדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 29 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is the young man|לַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb Absalom|לְאַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb all right|שָׁל֥וֹם\rb*?”
\p \rb And Ahimaaz|אֲחִימַ֡עַץ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb When Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb sent|לִ֠שְׁלֹחַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb servant|עֶ֨בֶד\rb* \rb and your servant|עַבְדֶּ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb I saw|רָאִיתִי֩\rb* \rb a great|הַגָּד֜וֹל\rb* \rb tumult|הֶהָמ֨וֹן\rb*, \rb but I do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb what it was|מָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 30 “\rb Move aside|סֹ֖ב\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb and stand|הִתְיַצֵּ֣ב\rb* \rb here|כֹּ֑ה\rb*.”
\p \rb So he stepped|וַֽיַּעֲמֹֽד׃\rb* \rb aside|וַיִּסֹּ֖ב\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb Just then|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Cushite|הַכּוּשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb came|בָּ֑א\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |הַכּוּשִׁ֗י\rb*, “\rb May my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb hear the good news|יִתְבַּשֵּׂר֙\rb*: \rb Today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has avenged you|שְׁפָטְךָ֤\rb* \rb of|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who rose up|הַקָּמִ֥ים\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 32 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the Cushite|הַכּוּשִׁ֔י\rb*, “\rb Is the young man|לַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb Absalom|לְאַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb all right|הֲשָׁל֥וֹם\rb*?”
\p \rb And the Cushite|הַכּוּשִׁ֗י\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb May the enemies|אֹֽיְבֵי֙\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹ֛ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb rise up|קָ֥מוּ\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to harm you|לְרָעָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb be|יִהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb like that young man|כַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb was shaken|וַיִּרְגַּ֣ז\rb* \rb and went up|וַיַּ֛עַל\rb* \rb to the chamber|עֲלִיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the gate|הַשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb and wept|וַיֵּ֑בְךְּ\rb*. \rb And as|וְכֹ֣ה׀\rb* \rb he walked|בְּלֶכְתּ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb he cried out|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, “\rb O my son|בְּנִ֤י\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb*! \rb My son|בְּנִ֣י\rb*, \rb my son|בְנִ֣י\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*! \rb If only|מִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb had died|מוּתִי֙\rb* \rb instead of you|תַחְתֶּ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb O Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִ֥י\rb*, \rb my son|בְנִֽי׃\rb*!”
\c 19
\s1 Joab Reproves David
\p \v 1 \rb Then it was reported|וַיֻּגַּ֖ד\rb* \rb to Joab|לְיוֹאָ֑ב\rb*,\rb |הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* “\rb The king|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb is weeping|בֹּכֶ֛ה\rb* \rb and mourning|וַיִּתְאַבֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֹֽם׃\rb*.” \v 2 \rb And that|הַה֛וּא\rb* \rb day’s|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb victory|הַתְּשֻׁעָ֜ה\rb* \rb was turned|וַתְּהִ֨י\rb* \rb into mourning|לְאֵ֖בֶל\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb on that|הַהוּא֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb they|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb were told|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb*, “\rb The king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb is grieving|נֶעֱצַ֥ב\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb So they|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb returned|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb to the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb quietly|וַיִּתְגַּנֵּ֥ב\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb steal away|יִתְגַּנֵּ֗ב\rb* \rb in humiliation|הַנִּכְלָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb after fleeing|בְּנוּסָ֖ם\rb* \rb a battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb But the king|וְהַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb covered|לָאַ֣ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb and cried out|וַיִּזְעַ֥ק\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb at the top|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb of his voice|ק֣וֹל\rb*, “\rb O my son|בְּנִי֙\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*! \rb O Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִ֥י\rb*, \rb my son|בְנִֽי׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 5 \rb Then Joab|יוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Today|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb* \rb you have disgraced|הֹבַ֨שְׁתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb who have saved|הַֽמְמַלְּטִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֙\rb*\rb |הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb and the lives|נֶ֤פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of your sons|בָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb*,\rb |וְנֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of your wives|נָשֶׁ֔יךָ\rb*,\rb |וְנֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb and of your concubines|פִּלַגְשֶֽׁיךָ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb You love|לְאַֽהֲבָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb those who hate you|שֹׂ֣נְאֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and hate|וְלִשְׂנֹ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb those who love you|אֹהֲבֶ֑יךָ\rb*! \rb For you have made it clear|הִגַּ֣דְתָּ\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י׀\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and soldiers|וַעֲבָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb mean nothing|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֙\rb*. \rb I know|יָדַ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*\rb |כִּ֠י\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb if|לֹא\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb were alive|חַי֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכֻלָּ֤נוּ\rb*\rb |הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb of us were dead|מֵתִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |כִּי־\rb*\rb |אָ֖ז\rb* \rb it would have pleased you|יָשָׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb*!
\p \v 7 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb get up|ק֣וּם\rb*! \rb Go out|צֵ֔א\rb* \rb and speak|וְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb comfort to|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb I swear|נִשְׁבַּ֜עְתִּי\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַיהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb that if|כִּי־\rb* \rb you do not|אֵינְךָ֣\rb* \rb go out|יוֹצֵ֗א\rb*, \rb not|אִם־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb will remain|יָלִ֨ין\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּךָ֙\rb* \rb tonight|הַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb*. \rb This|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb will be worse|וְרָעָ֧ה\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb than all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the adversity|הָרָעָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has befallen|בָּ֣אָה\rb* \rb you|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb from your youth|מִנְּעֻרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb now|עָֽתָּה׃ס\rb*!”
\s1 David Restored as King
\p \v 8 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֥קָם\rb* \rb and sat|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the gate|בַּשָּׁ֑עַר\rb*, \rb and all|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֞ם\rb* \rb were told|הִגִּ֣ידוּ\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb is sitting|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in the gate|בַּשַּׁ֔עַר\rb*.” \rb So they|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \rb Meanwhile, the Israelites|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had fled|נָ֖ס\rb*, \rb each man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his home|לְאֹהָלָֽיו׃ס\rb*. \v 9 \rb And|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb were arguing|נָד֔וֹן\rb*, “\rb The king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb rescued us|הִצִּילָ֣נוּ׀\rb* \rb from the hand|מִכַּ֣ף\rb* \rb of our enemies|אֹיְבֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb and|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb delivered us|מִלְּטָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb from the hand|מִכַּ֣ף\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb but now|וְעַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb he has fled|בָּרַ֥ח\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb because|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb of Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb But Absalom|וְאַבְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb*, \rb the man|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb we anointed|מָשַׁ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb over us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb has died|מֵ֖ת\rb* \rb in battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb why|לָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb do you|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb say nothing|מַחֲרִשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb about restoring|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*?”
\p \v 11 \rb Then King|וְהַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb sent this message|שָׁ֠לַח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zadok|צָד֨וֹק\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֥ר\rb*, \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִים֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb*: “\rb Say|דַּבְּר֞וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* ‘\rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb should you be|תִֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb the last|אַֽחֲרֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb to restore|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his palace|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb since the talk|וּדְבַר֙\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb has reached|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb his quarters|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*? \v 12 \rb You|אַתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb are my brothers|אַחַ֣י\rb*, \rb my own flesh|וּבְשָׂרִ֖י\rb* \rb and blood|עַצְמִ֥י\rb*. \rb So why|וְלָ֧מָּה\rb* \rb should you|אַתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb be|תִהְי֛וּ\rb* \rb the last|אַחֲרֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to restore|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*?’ \v 13 \rb And say|תֹּֽמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb to Amasa|וְלַֽעֲמָשָׂא֙\rb*, ‘\rb Aren’t|הֲל֛וֹא\rb* \rb you|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb my flesh|וּבְשָׂרִ֖י\rb* \rb and blood|עַצְמִ֥י\rb*? \rb May God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb punish|כֹּ֣ה\rb*\rb |יַֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֤י\rb*, \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely|יוֹסִ֔יף\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb from now on|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb you are|תִּהְיֶ֧ה\rb* \rb not|לֹ֠א\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of my|לְפָנַ֛י\rb* \rb army|צָבָ֞א\rb* \rb in place|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָֽב׃\rb*!’”
\p \v 14 \rb So he swayed|וַיַּ֛ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the hearts|לְבַ֥ב\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb as though they were one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb man|כְּאִ֣ישׁ\rb*, \rb and they sent|וַֽיִּשְׁלְחוּ֙\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*: “\rb Return|שׁ֥וּב\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb*, \rb and when he arrived|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb at|עַד־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*, \rb the men of Judah|וִיהוּדָ֞ה\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֗לָה\rb* \rb to|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb meet|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and escort him|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb across|לְהַעֲבִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*.
\s1 Shimei Pardoned
\p \v 16 \rb Then Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֤י\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Gera|גֵּרָא֙\rb*,\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb a Benjamite|הַיְמִינִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb from Bahurim|מִבַּֽחוּרִ֑ים\rb*,\rb |וַיֵּ֙רֶד֙\rb* \rb hurried|וַיְמַהֵ֗ר\rb* \rb down with|עִם־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֖את\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb along with a thousand|וְאֶ֨לֶף\rb* \rb men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Benjamin|מִבִּנְיָמִן֒\rb*,\rb |עִמּוֹ֮\rb* \rb as well as Ziba|וְצִיבָ֗א\rb* \rb the steward|נַ֚עַר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb and his fifteen|וַחֲמֵ֨שֶׁת\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb sons|בָּנָ֛יו\rb* \rb and twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אִתּ֑וֹ\rb*.
\p \rb They rushed down|וְצָלְח֥וּ\rb* \rb to the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \v 18 \rb and crossed|וְעָבְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb at the ford|הָעֲבָרָ֗ה\rb* \rb to carry over|לַֽעֲבִיר֙\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and to do|וְלַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb what was good|הַטּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb in his sight|בְּעֵינוֹ\rb*.
\p \rb When Shimei|וְשִׁמְעִ֣י\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Gera|גֵּרָ֗א\rb* \rb crossed|בְּעָבְר֖וֹ\rb* \rb the Jordan|בַּיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*, \rb he fell down|נָפַל֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \v 19 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִי֮\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb hold|יַחֲשָׁב־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb guilty|עָוֺן֒\rb*, \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb remember|תִּזְכֹּ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb your servant’s|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb wrongdoing|הֶעֱוָ֣ה\rb* \rb on the day|בַּיּ֕וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb left|יָׄצָ֥ׄאׄ\rb* \rb Jerusalem|מִירֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*. \rb May the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb not take|לָשׂ֥וּם\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb heart|לִבּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb knows|יָדַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have sinned|חָטָ֑אתִי\rb*, \rb so here I am|וְהִנֵּֽה־\rb*\rb |בָ֣אתִי\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb as the first|רִאשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb to come down|לָרֶ֕דֶת\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֖את\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb But Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֤י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָה֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb said|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*, “\rb Shouldn’t|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֑י\rb* \rb be put to death|יוּמַ֖ת\rb* \rb for|הֲתַ֣חַת\rb* \rb this|זֹ֔את\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he cursed|קִלֵּ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb anointed|מְשִׁ֥יחַ\rb*?”
\p \v 22 \rb And David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb have I to do|לִּ֤י\rb* \rb with you|וְלָכֶם֙\rb*, \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb you should be|תִֽהְיוּ־\rb* \rb my|לִ֥י\rb* \rb adversaries|לְשָׂטָ֑ן\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*? \rb Should any man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb be put to death|י֤וּמַת\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*? \rb Am I not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb indeed|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb aware|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb I am|אֲנִי־\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*?”
\p \v 23 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֖י\rb*, “\rb You shall not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb die|תָמ֑וּת\rb*.” \rb And the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb* \rb swore an oath|וַיִּשָּׁ֥בַֽע\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*.
\s1 Mephibosheth Excused
\p \v 24 \rb Then Mephibosheth|וּמְפִבֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb*, \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb grandson|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb went down|יָרַ֖ד\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*. \rb He had not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb cared|עָשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb for his feet|רַגְלָ֜יו\rb* \rb or|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb trimmed|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb his mustache|שְׂפָמ֗וֹ\rb* \rb or|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb washed|כִבֵּ֔ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָיו֙\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb from|לְמִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb had left|לֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he returned|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb safely|בְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb And|וַיְהִ֛י\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb he came|בָ֥א\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb who|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb Mephibosheth|מְפִיבֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*, \rb why|לָ֛מָּה\rb* \rb did you not|לֹא־\rb* \rb go|הָלַ֥כְתָּ\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֖י\rb*?”
\p \v 26 “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb am lame|פִסֵּ֖חַ\rb*, \rb I|עַבְדְּךָ֜\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֨ר\rb*, ‘\rb I will have my donkey|הַחֲמ֨וֹר\rb*\rb |לִּי֩\rb* \rb saddled|אֶחְבְּשָׁה־\rb*\f + \fr 19:26 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate \fqa Saddle a donkey for me\ft ; Hebrew \fqa I will saddle a donkey for myself\f* \rb so that I may ride|וְאֶרְכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and go|וְאֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*.’ \rb But my servant Ziba|עַבְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb deceived me|רִמָּ֑נִי\rb*,\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \v 27 \rb and he has slandered|וַיְרַגֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb your servant|בְּעַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \rb Yet my lord|וַאדֹנִ֤י\rb* \rb the king is|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb like the angel|כְּמַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 19:27 \ft Or \fqa Angel\f* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb so do|וַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb what is good|הַטּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb*\rb |לֹ֨א\rb*\rb |הָיָ֜ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of my grandfather|אָבִ֗י\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁי־\rb* \rb deserves death|מָ֙וֶת֙\rb* \rb from my lord|לַאדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb yet you have set|וַתָּ֙שֶׁת֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb among those who eat|בְּאֹכְלֵ֖י\rb* \rb at your table|שֻׁלְחָנֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb further|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb right, then|צְדָקָ֔ה\rb*, \rb do I have|יֶּשׁ־\rb*\rb |לִ֥י\rb* \rb to keep|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb appealing|וְלִזְעֹ֥ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃פ\rb*?”
\p \v 29 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֛מָּה\rb* \rb say|תְּדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb any more|ע֖וֹד\rb*? \rb I hereby declare|אָמַ֕רְתִּי\rb* \rb that you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and Ziba|וְצִיבָ֔א\rb* \rb are to divide|תַּחְלְק֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 30 \rb And Mephibosheth|מְפִיבֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Instead|גַּ֥ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb since|אַ֠חֲרֵי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶך\rb* \rb has safely|בְּשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb come|בָּ֞א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own house|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*, \rb let Ziba take|יִקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb it all|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb*!”
\s1 David’s Kindness to Barzillai
\p \v 31 \rb Now Barzillai|וּבַרְזִלַּי֙\rb* \rb the Gileadite|הַגִּלְעָדִ֔י\rb* \rb had come down|יָרַ֖ד\rb* \rb from Rogelim|מֵרֹגְלִ֑ים\rb* \rb to cross|וַיַּעֲבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and send him on his way|לְשַׁלְּח֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from there|בַּיַּרְדֵּן׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb Barzillai|וּבַרְזִלַּי֙\rb* \rb was quite|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb old|זָקֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb eighty|שְׁמֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb of age|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb and since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he was a very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb wealthy|גָּד֥וֹל\rb* \rb man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb*,\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb he|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb had provided|כִלְכַּ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb while he stayed|בְּשִׁיבָת֣וֹ\rb* \rb in Mahanaim|בְמַחֲנַ֔יִם\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Barzillai|בַּרְזִלָּ֑י\rb*,\rb |אַתָּה֙\rb* “\rb Cross over|עֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb and I will provide|וְכִלְכַּלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb for you|אֹתְךָ֛\rb* \rb at my side|עִמָּדִ֖י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 34 \rb But Barzillai|בַּרְזִלַּ֖י\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb How many|כַּמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb years|יְמֵי֙\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of my life remain|חַיַּ֔י\rb*, \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I should go up|אֶעֱלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*? \v 35 \rb I am|אָנֹכִ֨י\rb* \rb now|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb* \rb eighty|שְׁמֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֩\rb*. \rb Can I discern|הַאֵדַ֣ע׀\rb*\rb |בֵּין־\rb* \rb what is good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb and what is not|לְרָ֗ע\rb*?\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb Can your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb taste|יִטְעַ֤ם\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb he eats|אֹכַל֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb or drinks|אֶשְׁתֶּ֔ה\rb*?\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb Can I still|ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb hear|אֶשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of singing men|שָׁרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and women|וְשָׁר֑וֹת\rb*? \rb Why|וְלָמָּה֩\rb* \rb should your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb be|יִֽהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb an added|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb burden|לְמַשָּׂ֔א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*?
\p \v 36 \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֛\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will go with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb only a short distance|כִּמְעַ֞ט\rb* \rb past|יַעֲבֹ֧ר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb*; \rb why|וְלָ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb should the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb repay me|יִגְמְלֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb with such|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb a reward|הַגְּמוּלָ֖ה\rb*? \v 37 \rb Please|נָ֤א\rb* \rb let your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb return|יָֽשָׁב־\rb*, \rb that I may die|וְאָמֻ֣ת\rb* \rb in my own city|בְּעִירִ֔י\rb* \rb near|עִ֛ם\rb* \rb the tomb|קֶ֥בֶר\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִ֖י\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמִּ֑י\rb*. \rb But here|וְהִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb is your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb Chimham|כִמְהָ֗ם\rb*. \rb Let him cross over|יַֽעֲבֹר֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and do|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb for him|ל֕וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is good|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb in your sight|בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 38 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Chimham|כִּמְהָ֔ם\rb* \rb will cross over|יַעֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּי֙\rb*, \rb and I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will do|אֶעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for him|לּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what is good|הַטּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb in your sight|בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb and I will do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for you|לָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb whatever|וְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you desire|תִּבְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb of me|עָלַ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 39 \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb crossed|וַיַּעֲבֹ֧ר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb*, \rb and then the king|וְהַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb crossed over|עָבָ֑ר\rb*. \rb The king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb kissed|וַיִּשַּׁ֨ק\rb* \rb Barzillai|לְבַרְזִלַּי֙\rb* \rb and blessed him|וַיְבָ֣רֲכֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and Barzillai returned|וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb* \rb home|לִמְקֹמֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 40 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb crossed over|וַיַּעֲבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb to Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֔לָה\rb*, \rb and Chimham|וְכִמְהָ֖ן\rb* \rb crossed over|עָבַ֣ר\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the troops|עַ֤ם\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*\rb |וַיַּעֲבִרוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and|וְגַ֕ם\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֖י\rb* \rb the troops|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb escorted the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*.
\s1 Contention over the King
\p \v 41 \rb Soon|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb came|בָּאִ֣ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Why|מַדּוּעַ֩\rb* \rb did our brothers|אַחֵ֜ינוּ\rb*, \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*, \rb take you away secretly|גְּנָב֨וּךָ\rb* \rb and bring the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his household|בֵּיתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb across|וַיַּעֲבִ֨רוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb together with|עִמּֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of David’s|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb*?”
\p \v 42 \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּעַן֩\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, “\rb We did this because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb is our|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb relative|קָר֤וֹב\rb*. \rb Why|וְלָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb does this|זֶּה֙\rb* \rb anger|חָרָ֣ה\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb*?\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb Have we ever eaten|הֶאָכ֤וֹל\rb*\rb |אָכַ֙לְנוּ֙\rb* \rb at|מִן־\rb* \rb the king’s expense|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb*\rb |נִשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb received anything|נִשֵּׂ֥את\rb* \rb for ourselves|לָֽנוּ׃ס\rb*?”
\p \v 43 “\rb We have ten|עֶֽשֶׂר־\rb* \rb shares|יָד֨וֹת\rb* \rb in the king|בַמֶּלֶךְ֮\rb*,”\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֣עַן\rb* \rb the men|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֩\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb so we have more claim|וְגַם־\rb*\rb |אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb to David|בְּדָוִד֮\rb* \rb than you|מִמְּךָ֒\rb*. \rb Why|וּמַדּ֙וּעַ֙\rb* \rb then do you despise us|הֱקִלֹּתַ֔נִי\rb*? \rb Were we not|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb the first|רִאשׁ֛וֹן\rb* \rb to speak|דְבָרִ֥י\rb* \rb of restoring|לְהָשִׁ֣יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our king|מַלְכִּ֑י\rb*?”
\p \rb But the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb spoke more fiercely|וַיִּ֙קֶשׁ֙\rb*\rb |דְּבַר־\rb* \rb than|מִדְּבַ֖ר\rb* \rb the men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\c 20
\s1 Sheba’s Rebellion
\p \v 1 \rb Now a worthless|בְּלִיַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֛וֹ\rb* \rb Sheba|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bichri|בִּכְרִ֖י\rb*,\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb a Benjamite|יְמִינִ֑י\rb*, \rb happened|נִקְרָ֜א\rb* \rb to be there|וְשָׁ֨ם\rb*, \rb and he blew|וַיִּתְקַ֣ע\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשֹּׁפָ֗ר\rb* \rb and shouted|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb We have no|אֵֽין־\rb*\rb |לָ֨נוּ\rb* \rb share|חֵ֜לֶק\rb* \rb in David|בְּדָוִ֗ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb no|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb inheritance|נַֽחֲלָה־\rb*\rb |לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb in Jesse’s|יִשַׁ֔י\rb* \rb son|בְּבֶן־\rb*.
\q1 \rb Every man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his tent|לְאֹהָלָ֖יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*!”
\p \v 2 \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb deserted|וַיַּ֜עַל\rb*\rb |מֵאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb to follow|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb Sheba|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bichri|בִּכְרִ֑י\rb*. \rb But the men|וְאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb stayed by|דָּבְק֣וּ\rb* \rb their king|בְמַלְכָּ֔ם\rb* \rb all the way|וְעַד־\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb When David|דָוִ֣ד\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his palace|בֵּיתוֹ֮\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִַם֒\rb*, \rb he|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the ten|עֶֽשֶׂר־\rb*\rb |נָשִׁ֣ים׀\rb* \rb concubines|פִּלַגְשִׁ֡ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had left|הִנִּיחַ֩\rb* \rb to take care of|לִשְׁמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb the palace|הַבַּ֜יִת\rb*, \rb and he placed them|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֤ם\rb* \rb in a house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb under guard|מִשְׁמֶ֙רֶת֙\rb*. \rb He provided for them|וַֽיְכַלְכְּלֵ֔ם\rb*, \rb but he no longer|לֹא־\rb* \rb slept with|וַאֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb them|בָ֑א\rb*. \rb They were|וַתִּהְיֶ֧ינָה\rb* \rb confined|צְרֻר֛וֹת\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb of their death|מֻתָ֖ן\rb*, \rb living|חַיּֽוּת׃ס\rb* \rb as widows|אַלְמְנ֥וּת\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Amasa|עֲמָשָׂ֔א\rb*, “\rb Summon|הַזְעֶק־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb to come to me|לִ֥י\rb* \rb within three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and be here|פֹּ֥ה\rb*\rb |עֲמֹֽד׃\rb* \rb yourself|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb So Amasa|עֲמָשָׂ֖א\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to summon|לְהַזְעִ֣יק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb but he took longer|וַיֵּיחַר\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the time|הַמּוֹעֵ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb allotted him|יְעָדֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb And David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֔י\rb*, “\rb Now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb Sheba|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bichri|בִּכְרִ֖י\rb* \rb will do us more harm|יֵ֧רַֽע\rb*\rb |לָ֛נוּ\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*.\rb |אַ֠תָּה\rb* \rb Take|קַ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your lord’s|אֲדֹנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb and pursue him|וּרְדֹ֣ף\rb*,\rb |אַחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb he will find|מָ֥צָא\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb fortified|בְּצֻר֖וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and elude|וְהִצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb us|עֵינֵֽנוּ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 20:6 \ft Or \fqa and snatch away our eyes \ft or \fqa and do us serious harm\f*”
\p \v 7 \rb So Joab’s|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |וַיֵּצְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרָיו֙\rb*, \rb along with the Cherethites|וְהַכְּרֵתִ֥י\rb*, \rb the Pelethites|וְהַפְּלֵתִ֖י\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb marched out of|וַיֵּֽצְאוּ֙\rb* \rb Jerusalem|מִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb in pursuit|לִרְדֹּ֕ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Sheba|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bichri|בִּכְרִֽי׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb And while they|הֵ֗ם\rb* \rb were at|עִם־\rb* \rb the great|הַגְּדוֹלָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb stone|הָאֶ֤בֶן\rb* \rb in Gibeon|בְּגִבְע֔וֹן\rb*, \rb Amasa|וַעֲמָשָׂ֖א\rb* \rb joined|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb Now Joab|וְיוֹאָ֞ב\rb* \rb was dressed|חָג֣וּר׀\rb* \rb in military attire|מִדּ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |לְבֻשׁ֗וּ\rb*, \rb with a dagger|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb strapped|מְצֻמֶּ֤דֶת\rb*\rb |וְעָלוֹ\rb* \rb to his belt|חֲג֥וֹר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |מָתְנָיו֙\rb*. \rb And as he|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb stepped forward|יָצָ֖א\rb*, \rb he slipped the dagger|וַתִּפֹּֽל׃ס\rb* \rb from its sheath|בְּתַעְרָ֔הּ\rb*.\f + \fr 20:8 \ft Literally \fqa Now Joab was dressed in military attire, and over it was a belt around his waist with a dagger in its sheath. And as he stepped forward, it fell out.\f* \v 9 “\rb Are you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb well|הֲשָׁל֥וֹם\rb*, \rb my brother|אָחִ֑י\rb*?” \rb Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Amasa|לַעֲמָשָׂ֔א\rb*. \rb And with his right|יְמִ֥ין\rb* \rb hand|יַד־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb grabbed|וַתֹּ֜חֶז\rb* \rb Amasa|עֲמָשָׂ֖א\rb* \rb by the beard|בִּזְקַ֥ן\rb* \rb to kiss|לִנְשָׁק־\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Amasa|וַעֲמָשָׂ֨א\rb* \rb was not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb on guard|נִשְׁמַ֜ר\rb* \rb against the dagger|בַּחֶ֣רֶב׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Joab’s|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb hand|בְּיַד־\rb*, \rb and Joab stabbed|וַיַּכֵּהוּ֩\rb* \rb him|בָ֨הּ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the stomach|הַחֹ֜מֶשׁ\rb* \rb and spilled out his intestines|מֵעָ֥יו\rb*\rb |וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֨ךְ\rb* \rb on the ground|אַ֛רְצָה\rb*. \rb And Joab did not need|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb to strike him again|שָׁ֥נָה\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb for Amasa was dead|וַיָּמֹ֑תס\rb*. \rb Then Joab|וְיוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb and his brother|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb Abishai|וַאֲבִישַׁ֣י\rb* \rb pursued|רָדַ֕ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb Sheba|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bichri|בִּכְרִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb One|וְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb of Joab’s|יוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \rb young men|מִֽנַּעֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb stood|עָמַ֣ד\rb* \rb near Amasa|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Whoever|מִי֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb favors|חָפֵ֧ץ\rb* \rb Joab|בְּיוֹאָ֛ב\rb*, \rb and whoever|וּמִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is for David|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb*, \rb let him follow|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָֽב׃\rb*!” \v 12 \rb But Amasa|וַעֲמָשָׂ֛א\rb* \rb wallowed|מִתְגֹּלֵ֥ל\rb* \rb in his blood|בַּדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the road|הַֽמְסִּלָּ֑ה\rb*, \rb and when the man|הָאִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֨רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb were stopping there|עָמַ֣ד\rb*, \rb he dragged|וַיַּסֵּב֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the body|עֲמָשָׂ֨א\rb* \rb off|מִן־\rb* \rb the road|הַֽמְסִלָּ֤ה\rb* \rb into a field|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb and threw|וַיַּשְׁלֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb a garment|בֶּ֔גֶד\rb* \rb over it|עָלָיו֙\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |רָאָ֔ה\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַבָּ֥א\rb*\rb |עָלָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְעָמָֽד׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb As soon as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Amasa’s body was removed|הֹגָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the road|הַֽמְסִלָּ֑ה\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb went on|עָבַ֤ר\rb* \rb with|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb to pursue|לִרְדֹּ֕ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb Sheba|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bichri|בִּכְרִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Sheba passed|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֞ר\rb* \rb through all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb to Abel-beth-maacah|אָבֵ֛לָה\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ית\rb*\rb |מַעֲכָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 20:14 \ft Hebrew \fqa to Abel and Beth-maacah\ft ; see verse 15.\f* \rb and through the entire region of|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Berites|הַבֵּרִ֑יםס\rb*,\f + \fr 20:14 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate \fqa Bicrites\f* \rb who gathered together|וַיִּקָּלְהוּ\rb* \rb and followed|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb*\rb |אַף־\rb* \rb him|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb And Joab’s troops came|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb and besieged|וַיָּצֻ֣רוּ\rb* \rb Sheba|עָלָ֗יו\rb* \rb in Abel-beth-maacah|בְּאָבֵ֙לָה֙\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַֽמַּעֲכָ֔ה\rb* \rb and built|וַיִּשְׁפְּכ֤וּ\rb* \rb a siege ramp|סֹֽלְלָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb against the outer rampart|בַּחֵ֑ל\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*.
\p \rb |וַֽתַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb As all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb were battering|מַשְׁחִיתִ֖ם\rb* \rb the wall|הַחוֹמָֽה׃\rb* \rb to topple it|לְהַפִּ֥יל\rb*, \v 16 \rb a wise|חֲכָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb called out|וַתִּקְרָ֛א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, “\rb Listen|שִׁמְע֤וּ\rb*! \rb Listen|שִׁמְעוּ֙\rb*! \rb Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb tell|אִמְרוּ־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb to come|קְרַ֣ב\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb here|הֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb so that I may speak|וַאֲדַבְּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb with him|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb When he had come near|וַיִּקְרַ֣ב\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb asked|וַתֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Are you|הַאַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb*?”
\p “\rb I am|אָ֑נִי\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb Listen|שְׁמַע֙\rb* \rb to the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your servant|אֲמָתֶ֔ךָ\rb*,” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb I am|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb* \rb listening|שֹׁמֵ֥עַ\rb*,” \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then the woman said|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Long ago|בָרִֽאשֹׁנָה֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb they used to say|דַּבֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |יְדַבְּר֤וּ\rb*, ‘\rb Seek counsel|שָׁאֹ֧ל\rb*\rb |יְשָׁאֲל֛וּ\rb* \rb at Abel|בְּאָבֵ֖ל\rb*,’ \rb and that is how|וְכֵ֥ן\rb* \rb disputes were settled|הֵתַֽמּוּ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb I am|אָנֹכִ֕י\rb* \rb among the peaceable|שְׁלֻמֵ֖י\rb* \rb and faithful|אֱמוּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb in Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb but you are|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb trying|מְבַקֵּ֗שׁ\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהָמִ֨ית\rb* \rb a city|עִ֤יר\rb* \rb that is a mother|וְאֵם֙\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*. \rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb would you swallow up|תְבַלַּ֖ע\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb inheritance|נַחֲלַ֥ת\rb*?”
\p \v 20 “\rb Far be it|חָלִ֤ילָה\rb*!” \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*. “\rb Far be it|חָלִ֙ילָה֙\rb* \rb from me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb to|אִם־\rb* \rb swallow up|אֲבַלַּ֖ע\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb destroy|אַשְׁחִֽית׃\rb*! \v 21 \rb That is|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb the case|כֵ֣ן\rb*. \rb But|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֩\rb* \rb named|שְׁמ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Sheba|שֶׁ֧בַע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bichri|בִּכְרִ֣י\rb*, \rb from the hill country|מֵהַ֨ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֜יִם\rb*, \rb has lifted|נָשָׂ֤א\rb* \rb up his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb against the king|בַּמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb against David|בְּדָוִ֔ד\rb*. \rb Deliver|תְּנֽוּ־\rb* \rb him|אֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and I will depart|וְאֵלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*.”
\p “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*,” \rb the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, “\rb his head|רֹאשׁ֛וֹ\rb* \rb will be thrown|מֻשְׁלָ֥ךְ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb over|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb the wall|הַחוֹמָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb Then the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֨ה\rb* \rb went|וַתָּבוֹא֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb with her wise counsel|בְּחָכְמָתָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb and they cut off|וַֽיִּכְרְת֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֨אשׁ\rb* \rb of Sheba|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bichri|בִּכְרִי֙\rb* \rb and threw|וַיַּשְׁלִ֣כוּ\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*. \rb So he blew|וַיִּתְקַע֙\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb* \rb and his men dispersed|וַיָּפֻ֥צוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵֽעַל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb*, \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb to his own home|לְאֹהָלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb And Joab|וְיוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb returned|שָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Now Joab|וְיוֹאָ֕ב\rb* \rb was over|אֶ֥ל\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|הַצָּבָ֖א\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*; \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָה֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְה֣וֹיָדָ֔ע\rb* \rb was over|עַל־\rb* \rb the Cherethites|הַכְּרִי\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb Pelethites|הַפְּלֵתִֽי׃\rb*; \v 24 \rb Adoram|וַאֲדֹרָ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 20:24 \fqa Adoram \ft is a variant of \fqa Adoniram \ft and \fqa Hadoram\ft ; see 1 Kings 4:6 and 2 Chronicles 10:18.\f* \rb was in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the forced labor|הַמַּ֑ס\rb*; \rb Jehoshaphat|וִיהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahilud|אֲחִיל֖וּד\rb* \rb was the recorder|הַמַּזְכִּֽיר׃\rb*; \v 25 \rb Sheva|וְשֵׁיָא\rb*\f + \fr 20:25 \fqa Sheva \ft is also called \fqa Seraiah\ft , \fqa Shisha\ft , and \fqa Shavsha\ft ; see 2 Samuel 8:17, 1 Kings 4:3, and 1 Chronicles 18:16.\f* \rb was the scribe|סֹפֵ֑ר\rb*; \rb Zadok|וְצָד֥וֹק\rb* \rb and Abiathar|וְאֶבְיָתָ֖ר\rb* \rb were priests|כֹּהֲנִֽים׃\rb*; \v 26 \rb and|וְגַ֗ם\rb* \rb Ira|עִירָא֙\rb* \rb the Jairite|הַיָּ֣אִרִ֔י\rb*\f + \fr 20:26 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts and Syriac \fqa Ithrite\ft ; see 2 Samuel 23:38.\f* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb David’s|לְדָוִֽד׃ס\rb* \rb priest|כֹהֵ֖ן\rb*.
\c 21
\s1 David Avenges the Gibeonites
\p \v 1 \rb During the reign|בִּימֵ֨י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb there was|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb a famine|רָעָב֩\rb* \rb for three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb successive years|שָׁנִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb*,\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb and David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sought|וַיְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑הס\rb*.
\p \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb It is because of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb shed by Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb his family|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he killed|הֵמִ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Gibeonites|הַגִּבְעֹנִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb At this, David|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb the Gibeonites|וְהַגִּבְעֹנִ֞ים\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. (\rb Now the Gibeonites|לַגִּבְעֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb were|הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb Israelites|מִבְּנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb a remnant|מִיֶּ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb*. \rb The Israelites|וּבְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb had taken an oath concerning them|נִשְׁבְּע֣וּ\rb*,\rb |לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb but in his zeal|בְּקַנֹּאת֥וֹ\rb* \rb for Israel|לִבְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*, \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb had sought|וַיְבַקֵּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb to kill them|לְהַכֹּתָ֔ם\rb*.)
\p \v 3 \rb So David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the Gibeonites|הַגִּבְעֹנִ֔ים\rb*, “\rb What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb shall I do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֑ם\rb*? \rb How|וּבַמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb can I make amends|אֲכַפֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb so that you may bless|וּבָרְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb The Gibeonites|הַגִּבְעֹנִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמְרוּ\rb* \rb to him|ל֣וֹ\rb*, “\rb We need no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb or gold|וְזָהָב֙\rb* \rb from|עִם־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb or|וְעִם־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb nor|וְאֵֽין־\rb* \rb should you|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb put to death|לְהָמִ֣ית\rb* \rb anyone in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb for us|לָ֥נוּ\rb*.”
\p “\rb Whatever|מָֽה־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb ask|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb*, \rb I will do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|אֹמְרִ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb And they answered|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb As for the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb consumed us|כִּלָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and|וַאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb plotted|דִּמָּה־\rb* \rb against us|לָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb to exterminate us|נִשְׁמַ֕דְנוּ\rb* \rb from existing|מֵֽהִתְיַצֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb within any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb border|גְּבֻ֥ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb let seven|שִׁבְעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb of his male descendants|מִבָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb be delivered|יְנָתָן\rb* \rb to us|לָ֜נוּ\rb* \rb so that we may hang them|וְהוֹקַֽעֲנוּם֙\rb*\f + \fr 21:6 \ft Or \fqa expose them \ft or \fqa execute them\ft ; similarly in verse 9\f* \rb before the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb at Gibeah|בְּגִבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*, \rb the chosen|בְּחִ֣יר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑הס\rb*.”
\p “\rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will give them to you|אֶתֵּֽן׃\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Now the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb spared|וַיַּחְמֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Mephibosheth|מְפִי־\rb*\rb |בֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*, \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb the oath|שְׁבֻעַ֤ת\rb* \rb before the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb between|בֵּֽינֹתָ֔ם\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֖ין\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֥ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb But the king|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb Armoni|אַרְמֹנִ֖י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Mephibosheth|מְפִבֹ֑שֶׁת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁ֠נֵי\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Rizpah|רִצְפָּ֤ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Aiah|אַיָּה֙\rb* \rb had borne|יָלְדָ֣ה\rb* \rb to Saul|לְשָׁא֔וּל\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as well as the five|חֲמֵ֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Merab|מִיכַ֣ל\rb*\f + \fr 21:8 \ft Two Hebrew manuscripts, some LXX manuscripts, and Syriac (see also 1 Samuel 18:19); most Hebrew and LXX manuscripts \fqa Michal\f* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb had borne|יָלְדָ֛ה\rb* \rb to Adriel|לְעַדְרִיאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Barzillai|בַּרְזִלַּ֖י\rb* \rb the Meholathite|הַמְּחֹלָתִֽי׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb And he delivered them|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֞ם\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the Gibeonites|הַגִּבְעֹנִ֗ים\rb*, \rb and they hanged them|וַיֹּקִיעֻ֤ם\rb* \rb on the hill|בָּהָר֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb So all seven of them|שִׁבְעָתַיִם\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb together|יָ֑חַד\rb*; \rb they|וְהֵם\rb* \rb were put to death|הֻמְת֜וּ\rb* \rb in the first|בָּרִ֣אשֹׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb days|בִּימֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the harvest|קָצִיר֙\rb*, \rb at the beginning|תְּחִלַּת\rb* \rb of the barley|שְׂעֹרִֽים׃\rb* \rb harvest|קְצִ֥יר\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb And Rizpah|רִצְפָּה֩\rb* \rb the daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Aiah|אַיָּ֨ה\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb sackcloth|הַשַּׂ֜ק\rb* \rb and spread it out|וַתַּטֵּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb for herself|לָ֤הּ\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb a rock|הַצּוּר֙\rb*. \rb From the beginning|מִתְּחִלַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the harvest|קָצִ֔יר\rb* \rb until|עַ֛ד\rb* \rb the rain|מַ֥יִם\rb* \rb from heaven|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb poured down|נִתַּךְ־\rb* \rb on the bodies|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb she did not allow|נָתְנָה֩\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb the birds|ע֨וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֜יִם\rb* \rb to rest|לָנ֤וּחַ\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb by day|יוֹמָ֔ם\rb*, \rb nor|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the beasts|חַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb by night|לָֽיְלָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb When David|לְדָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb was told|וַיֻּגַּ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֧ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb* \rb concubine|פִּלֶ֥גֶשׁ\rb* \rb Rizpah|רִצְפָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Aiah|אַיָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb had done|עָשְׂתָ֛ה\rb*, \v 12 \rb he|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bones|עַצְמ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |עַצְמוֹת֙\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֕ת\rb* \rb the men|בַּעֲלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jabesh-gilead|יָבֵ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb had stolen|גָּנְב֨וּ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb from the public square|מֵרְחֹ֣ב\rb* \rb of Beth-shan|בֵּֽית־\rb*\rb |שַׁ֗ן\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the Philistines|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּים\rb* \rb had hung the bodies|תָּלוּם\rb*\rb |שָׁם\rb* \rb after|בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb they|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had struck down|הַכּ֧וֹת\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb at Gilboa|בַּגִּלְבֹּֽעַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb So David had the bones|עַצְמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |עַצְמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb brought|וַיַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁם֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and they also gathered|וַיַּ֣אַסְפ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bones|עַצְמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of those who had been hanged|הַמּוּקָעִֽים׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb And they buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb the bones|עַצְמוֹת־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb and his son|בְּ֠נוֹ\rb* \rb Jonathan|וִיהוֹנָֽתָן־\rb* \rb in Zela|בְּצֵלָ֗ע\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֜ן\rb*, \rb in the tomb|בְּקֶ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb of Saul’s father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Kish|קִ֣ישׁ\rb*.
\p \rb After|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵֽן׃פ\rb* \rb they had done|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb everything|כֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb answered their prayers|וַיֵּעָתֵ֧ר\rb* \rb for the land|לָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*.
\s1 Four Battles against the Philistines
\p \v 15 \rb Once again|ע֧וֹד\rb*\rb |וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb the Philistines|לַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb waged war|מִלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb and his servants|וַעֲבָדָ֥יו\rb*\rb |עִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּ֨רֶד\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּחֲמ֥וּ\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb*. \rb But David|דָּוִֽד׃\rb* \rb became exhausted|וַיָּ֥עַף\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb |וְיִשְׁבּוֹ\rb* \rb Then Ishbi-benob|בְּנֹ֜ב\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb a descendant|בִּילִידֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Rapha|הָרָפָ֗ה\rb*,\f + \fr 21:16 \ft Or \fqa the giant\ft ; also in verses 18, 20, and 22\f* \rb whose bronze|נְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb spear|קֵינוֹ֙\rb* \rb weighed|וּמִשְׁקַ֤ל\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb shekels|מִשְׁקַ֣ל\rb*\f + \fr 21:16 \fqa 300 shekels \ft is approximately 7.5 pounds or 3.4 kilograms.\f* \rb and who|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb was bearing|חָג֣וּר\rb* \rb a new sword|חֲדָשָׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb resolved|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to kill|לְהַכּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb But Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֣י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֔ה\rb* \rb came to his aid|וַיַּֽעֲזָר־\rb*\rb |לוֹ֙\rb*, \rb struck|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb*, \rb and killed him|וַיְמִיתֵ֑הוּ\rb*.
\p \rb Then|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִ֨ד\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb* \rb swore|נִשְׁבְּעוּ֩\rb* \rb to him|ל֜וֹ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* “\rb You must never|לֹא־\rb* \rb again|ע֤וֹד\rb* \rb go out|תֵצֵ֨א\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb to battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb so that the lamp|נֵ֥ר\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb* \rb may not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb be extinguished|תְכַבֶּ֖ה\rb*.”\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Some time later|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb at Gob|בְּג֖וֹב\rb*, \rb there was|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb another|ע֧וֹד\rb* \rb battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Sibbecai|סִבְּכַי֙\rb* \rb the Hushathite|הַחֻ֣שָׁתִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb killed|הִכָּ֗ה\rb* \rb Saph|סַ֕ף\rb*,\f + \fr 21:18 \fqa Saph \ft is a variant of \fqa Sippai\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 20:4.\f* \rb a|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb descendant|בִּילִדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Rapha|הָרָפָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Once again|ע֧וֹד\rb* \rb there was|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb a battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb at Gob|בְּג֖וֹב\rb*, \rb and Elhanan|אֶלְחָנָן֩\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |יַעְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jair|אֹרְגִ֜ים\rb*\f + \fr 21:19 \ft See 1 Chronicles 20:5; Hebrew \fqa Jaare-oregim\f*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb the Bethlehemite|הַלַּחְמִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb killed|וַיַּ֡ךְ\rb* \rb the brother of Goliath|גָּלְיָ֣ת\rb*\f + \fr 21:19 \ft See 1 Chronicles 20:5; Hebrew does not include \fqa the brother of\ft .\f* \rb the Gittite|הַגִּתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb the shaft|וְעֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of whose spear|חֲנִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb was like a weaver’s|אֹרְגִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb beam|כִּמְנ֖וֹר\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb And there was|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb also|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb a battle|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Gath|בְּגַ֑ת\rb*, \rb where there was a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of great stature|מָדִין\rb* \rb with|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb fingers|וְאֶצְבְּעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb on each hand|יָדָיו֩\rb* \rb and six|וָשֵׁ֗שׁ\rb* \rb toes|וְאֶצְבְּעֹ֨ת\rb* \rb on each foot|רַגְלָ֜יו\rb*— \rb twenty-four|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּע֙\rb* \rb in all|מִסְפָּ֔ר\rb*. \rb He|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb too|וְגַם־\rb* \rb was descended|יֻלַּ֥ד\rb* \rb from Rapha|לְהָרָפָֽה׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb and when he taunted|וַיְחָרֵ֖ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of David’s|דָוִֽד׃\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֥י\rb* \rb Shimei|שִׁמְעִי\rb*\f + \fr 21:21 \fqa Shimei \ft is a variant of \fqa Shammah\ft , \fqa Shimeah\ft , and \fqa Shimea\ft ; see 1 Samuel 16:9, 2 Samuel 13:3, and 1 Chronicles 2:13.\f* \rb killed him|וַיַּכֵּ֙הוּ֙\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb So these|אֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֥עַת\rb* \rb descendants|יֻלְּד֥וּ\rb* \rb of Rapha|לְהָרָפָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Gath|בְּגַ֑ת\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb at the hands|בְיַד־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֥ד\rb* \rb and his servants|עֲבָדָֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 22
\s1 David’s Song of Deliverance
\p \v 1 \rb And David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb sang|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb*\rb |דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb song|הַשִּׁירָ֣ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on the day|בְּיוֹם֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb had delivered|הִצִּ֨יל\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִכַּ֥ף\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his enemies|אֹיְבָ֖יו\rb* \rb and from the hand|וּמִכַּ֥ף\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb He said|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb is my rock|סַֽלְעִ֥י\rb*,
\q2 \rb my fortress|וּמְצֻדָתִ֖י\rb*, \rb and my deliverer|וּמְפַלְטִי־\rb*\rb |לִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb My God is|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb my rock|צוּרִ֖י\rb*, \rb in whom I take refuge|אֶחֱסֶה־\rb*\rb |בּ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb my shield|מָגִנִּ֞י\rb*, \rb and the horn|וְקֶ֣רֶן\rb* \rb of my salvation|יִשְׁעִ֗י\rb*.
\q1 \rb My stronghold|מִשְׂגַּבִּי֙\rb*, \rb my refuge|וּמְנוּסִ֔י\rb*, \rb and my Savior|מֹשִׁעִ֕י\rb*,
\q2 \rb You save me|תֹּשִׁעֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb from violence|מֵחָמָ֖ס\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb I will call upon|אֶקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb who is worthy to be praised|מְהֻלָּ֖ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb so shall I be saved|אִוָּשֵֽׁעַ׃\rb* \rb from my enemies|וּמֵאֹיְבַ֖י\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the waves|מִשְׁבְּרֵי־\rb* \rb of death|מָ֑וֶת\rb* \rb engulfed me|אֲפָפֻ֖נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb the torrents|נַחֲלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of chaos|בְלִיַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb overwhelmed me|יְבַעֲתֻֽנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb The cords|חֶבְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Sheol|שְׁא֖וֹל\rb* \rb entangled me|סַבֻּ֑נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb the snares|מֹֽקְשֵׁי־\rb* \rb of death|מָֽוֶת׃\rb* \rb confronted me|קִדְּמֻ֖נִי\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb In my distress|בַּצַּר־\rb*\rb |לִי֙\rb* \rb I called upon|אֶקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb I cried out|אֶקְרָ֑א\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \rb And from His temple|מֵהֵֽיכָלוֹ֙\rb* \rb He heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb my voice|קוֹלִ֔י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my cry for help|וְשַׁוְעָתִ֖י\rb* \rb reached His ears|בְּאָזְנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Then the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb shook|וַתִּגְעַשׁ\rb* \rb and quaked|וַתִּרְעַשׁ֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb the foundations|מוֹסְד֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*\f + \fr 22:8 \ft Most Hebrew sources; Vulgate, Syriac, and two Hebrew manuscripts (see also Psalm 18:7) \fqa mountains\f* \rb trembled|יִרְגָּ֑זוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb they were shaken|וַיִּֽתְגָּעֲשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He burned with anger|חָ֥רָה\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb Smoke|עָשָׁן֙\rb* \rb rose|עָלָ֤ה\rb* \rb from His nostrils|בְּאַפּ֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and consuming|תֹּאכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb fire|וְאֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb came from|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb His mouth|מִפִּ֖יו\rb*;
\q2 \rb glowing coals|גֶּחָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb blazed forth|בָּעֲר֥וּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb He parted|וַיֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and came down|וַיֵּרַ֑ד\rb*
\q2 \rb with dark clouds|וַעֲרָפֶ֖ל\rb* \rb beneath|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb His feet|רַגְלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb He mounted|וַיִּרְכַּ֥ב\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb a cherub|כְּר֖וּב\rb* \rb and flew|וַיָּעֹ֑ף\rb*;
\q2 \rb He soared|וַיֵּרָ֖א\rb*\f + \fr 22:11 \ft Many Hebrew manuscripts (see also Psalm 18:10); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa He was seen\f* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wings|כַּנְפֵי־\rb* \rb of the wind|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb He made|וַיָּ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb darkness|חֹ֛שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb a canopy|סֻכּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb around Him|סְבִיבֹתָ֖יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb a gathering|חַֽשְׁרַת־\rb* \rb of water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and thick clouds|עָבֵ֥י\rb*\rb |שְׁחָקִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb From the brightness|מִנֹּ֖גַהּ\rb* \rb of His presence|נֶגְדּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb coals|גַּחֲלֵי־\rb* \rb of fire|אֵֽשׁ׃\rb*\f + \fr 22:13 \ft Or \fqa bolts of lightning\f* \rb blazed forth|בָּעֲר֖וּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb thundered|יַרְעֵ֥ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|שָׁמַ֖יִם\rb*;
\q2 \rb the voice|קוֹלֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb of the Most High|וְעֶלְי֖וֹן\rb* \rb resounded|יִתֵּ֥ן\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb He shot|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb His arrows|חִצִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and scattered the foes|וַיְפִיצֵ֑ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb He hurled lightning|בָּרָ֖ק\rb* \rb and routed them|וַיְהֻמֵּם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb The channels|אֲפִ֣קֵי\rb* \rb of the sea|יָ֔ם\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּֽרָאוּ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the foundations|מֹסְד֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the world|תֵּבֵ֑ל\rb* \rb were exposed|יִגָּל֖וּ\rb*
\q1 \rb at the rebuke|בְּגַעֲרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb at the blast|מִנִּשְׁמַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the breath|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of His nostrils|אַפּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb He reached down|יִשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb from on high|מִמָּר֖וֹם\rb* \rb and took hold of me|יִקָּחֵ֑נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb He drew me|יַֽמְשֵׁ֖נִי\rb* \rb out of deep|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb waters|מִמַּ֥יִם\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb He rescued me|יַצִּילֵ֕נִי\rb* \rb from my powerful|עָ֑ז\rb* \rb enemy|מֵאֹיְבִ֖י\rb*,
\q2 \rb from foes|מִשֹּׂ֣נְאַ֔י\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb too mighty|אָמְצ֖וּ\rb* \rb for me|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb They confronted me|יְקַדְּמֻ֖נִי\rb* \rb in my day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of calamity|אֵידִ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb my support|מִשְׁעָ֖ן\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb He brought me out|וַיֹּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb into the open|לַמֶּרְחָ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb He rescued me|יְחַלְּצֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb He delighted|חָ֥פֵֽץ\rb* \rb in me|בִּֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has rewarded me|יִגְמְלֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb according to my righteousness|כְּצִדְקָתִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has repaid|יָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb me|לִֽי׃\rb* \rb according to the cleanness|כְּבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb of my hands|יָדַ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I have kept|שָׁמַ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb the ways|דַּרְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb wickedly departed|רָשַׁ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb from my God|מֵאֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb His ordinances are|מִשְׁפָּטוֹ\rb* \rb before me|לְנֶגְדִּ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb disregarded|אָס֥וּר\rb*\rb |מִמֶּֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb His statutes|וְחֻקֹּתָ֖יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb And I|וָאֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb have been blameless|תָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb before Him|ל֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and kept myself|וָאֶשְׁתַּמְּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb from iniquity|מֵעֲוֺנִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has repaid|וַיָּ֧שֶׁב\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb according to my righteousness|כְּצִדְקָתִ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb according to my cleanness|כְּבֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb in|לְנֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb His sight|עֵינָֽיו׃\rb*.\f + \fr 22:25 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate (see also Psalm 18:24) \fqa according to the cleanness of my hands\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 26 \rb To|עִם־\rb* \rb the faithful|חָסִ֖יד\rb* \rb You show Yourself faithful|תִּתְחַסָּ֑ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb the blameless|תָּמִ֖ים\rb*\rb |גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb You show Yourself blameless|תִּתַּמָּֽם׃\rb*;
\q1 \v 27 \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb the pure|נָבָ֖ר\rb* \rb You show Yourself pure|תִּתָּבָ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb but to|וְעִם־\rb* \rb the crooked|עִקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb You show Yourself shrewd|תִּתַּפָּֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb You save|תּוֹשִׁ֑יעַ\rb* \rb an afflicted|עָנִ֖י\rb* \rb people|עַ֥ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb but Your eyes|וְעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb are on|עַל־\rb* \rb the haughty|רָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb to bring them down|תַּשְׁפִּֽיל׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 29 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb are my lamp|נֵירִ֖י\rb*;
\q2 \rb the LORD|וַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb lights up|יַגִּ֥יהַּ\rb* \rb my darkness|חָשְׁכִּֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 30 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb in You|בְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb I can charge|אָר֣וּץ\rb* \rb an army|גְּד֑וּד\rb*;
\q2 \rb with my God|בֵּאלֹהַ֖י\rb* \rb I can scale|אֲדַלֶּג־\rb* \rb a wall|שֽׁוּר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 31 \rb As for God|הָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb His way|דַּרְכּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb is perfect|תָּמִ֣ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb the word|אִמְרַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb is flawless|צְרוּפָ֔ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb He|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is a shield|מָגֵ֣ן\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb*
\q2 \rb who take refuge|הַחֹסִ֥ים\rb* \rb in Him|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 32 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb who|מִי־\rb* \rb is God|אֵ֖ל\rb* \rb besides|מִבַּלְעֲדֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*?
\q2 \rb And who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb is the Rock|צ֖וּר\rb* \rb except|מִֽבַּלְעֲדֵ֥י\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 33 \rb God|הָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb is my strong|חָ֑יִל\rb* \rb fortress|מָעוּזִּ֖י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He makes|וַיַּתֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb my way|דַּרְכּוֹ׃\rb* \rb clear|תָּמִ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 34 \rb He makes|מְשַׁוֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb my feet|רַגְלָיו\rb* \rb like those of a deer|כָּאַיָּל֑וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb and stations me|יַעֲמִדֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb upon|וְעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the heights|בָּמוֹתַ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 35 \rb He trains|מְלַמֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb my hands|יָדַ֖י\rb* \rb for battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb my arms|זְרֹעֹתָֽי׃\rb* \rb can bend|וְנִחַ֥ת\rb* \rb a bow|קֶֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחוּשָׁ֖ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 36 \rb You have given|וַתִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb Your shield|מָגֵ֣ן\rb* \rb of salvation|יִשְׁעֶ֑ךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and Your gentleness|וַעֲנֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb exalts me|תַּרְבֵּֽנִי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 22:36 \ft Or \fqa and Your help exalts me \ft or \fqa and You stoop down to make me great\f*
\q1 \v 37 \rb You broaden|תַּרְחִ֥יב\rb* \rb the path|צַעֲדִ֖י\rb* \rb beneath me|תַּחְתֵּ֑נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb so that my ankles|קַרְסֻלָּֽי׃\rb* \rb do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb give way|מָעֲד֖וּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 38 \rb I pursued|אֶרְדְּפָ֥ה\rb* \rb my enemies|אֹיְבַ֖י\rb* \rb and destroyed them|וָאַשְׁמִידֵ֑ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb I did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb turn back|אָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they were consumed|כַּלּוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 39 \rb I devoured|וָאֲכַלֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb and crushed them|וָאֶמְחָצֵ֖ם\rb* \rb so they could not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb rise|יְקוּמ֑וּן\rb*;
\q2 \rb they have fallen|וַֽיִּפְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb my feet|רַגְלָֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 40 \rb You have armed me|וַתַּזְרֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb with strength|חַ֖יִל\rb* \rb for battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb You have subdued|תַּכְרִ֥יעַ\rb* \rb my foes|קָמַ֖י\rb* \rb beneath me|תַּחְתֵּֽנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 41 \rb You have made|תַּ֥תָּה\rb* \rb my enemies|וְאֹ֣יְבַ֔י\rb* \rb retreat|עֹ֑רֶף\rb* \rb before me|לִּ֖י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I destroyed|וָאַצְמִיתֵֽם׃\rb* \rb those who hated me|מְשַׂנְאַ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 42 \rb They looked|יִשְׁע֖וּ\rb*, \rb but there was no one|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb to save them|מֹשִׁ֑יעַ\rb* —
\q2 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb but He did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb answer|עָנָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 43 \rb I ground them|וְאֶשְׁחָקֵ֖ם\rb* \rb as the dust|כַּעֲפַר־\rb* \rb of the earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*;
\q2 \rb I crushed|אֲדִקֵּ֖ם\rb* \rb and trampled them|אֶרְקָעֵֽם׃\rb* \rb like mud|כְּטִיט־\rb* \rb in the streets|חוּצ֥וֹת\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 44 \rb You have delivered me|וַֽתְּפַלְּטֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb from the strife|מֵרִיבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of my people|עַמִּ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb You have preserved me|תִּשְׁמְרֵ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb as the head|לְרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of nations|גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb a people|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb I had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb known|יָדַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb shall serve me|יַעַבְדֻֽנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 45 \rb Foreigners|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |נֵכָ֖ר\rb* \rb cower|יִתְכַּֽחֲשׁוּ־\rb* \rb before me|לִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb when they hear me|לִשְׁמ֥וֹעַ\rb*,\rb |אֹ֖זֶן\rb* \rb they obey|יִשָּׁ֥מְעוּ\rb* \rb me|לִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 46 \rb Foreigners|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |נֵכָ֖ר\rb* \rb lose heart|יִבֹּ֑לוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and come trembling|וְיַחְגְּר֖וּ\rb*\f + \fr 22:46 \ft Some LXX manuscripts and Vulgate (see also Psalm 18:45); MT \fqa and arm themselves\f* \rb from their strongholds|מִמִּסְגְּרוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 47 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb and blessed be|וּבָר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb my Rock|צוּרִ֑י\rb*!
\q2 \rb And may God|אֱלֹהֵ֖י\rb*, \rb the Rock|צ֥וּר\rb* \rb of my salvation|יִשְׁעִֽי׃\rb*, \rb be exalted|וְיָרֻ֕ם\rb*—
\q1 \v 48 \rb the God|הָאֵ֕ל\rb* \rb who avenges|הַנֹּתֵ֥ן\rb*\rb |נְקָמֹ֖ת\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and brings down|וּמוֹרִ֥יד\rb* \rb nations|עַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb beneath me|תַּחְתֵּֽנִי׃\rb*,
\q2 \v 49 \rb who frees me from|וּמוֹצִיאִ֖י\rb* \rb my enemies|מֵאֹֽיְבָ֑י\rb*.
\q1 \rb You exalt me|תְּר֣וֹמְמֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb above my foes|וּמִקָּמַי֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb You rescue me|תַּצִּילֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb from violent|חֲמָסִ֖ים\rb* \rb men|מֵאִ֥ישׁ\rb*.
\q1 \v 50 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb I will praise You|אוֹדְךָ֥\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will sing praises|אֲזַמֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb to Your name|וּלְשִׁמְךָ֖\rb*.\f + \fr 22:50 \ft Cited in Romans 15:9\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 51 \rb Great|מַגְדִּיל\rb* \rb salvation|יְשׁוּע֣וֹת\rb* \rb He brings to His king|מַלְכּ֑וֹ\rb*.
\q2 \rb He shows|וְעֹֽשֶׂה־\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֧סֶד\rb* \rb to His anointed|לִמְשִׁיח֛וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb to David|לְדָוִ֥ד\rb* \rb and his descendants|וּלְזַרְע֖וֹ\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃פ\rb*.”
\c 23
\s1 David’s Last Song
\p \v 1 \rb These|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb are the last|הָאַֽחֲרֹנִ֑ים\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִ֖ד\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb The oracle|נְאֻ֧ם\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁ֗י\rb*,
\q2 \rb the oracle|וּנְאֻ֤ם\rb* \rb of the man|הַגֶּ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb raised|הֻ֣קַם\rb* \rb on high|עָ֔ל\rb*,
\q1 \rb the one anointed|מְשִׁ֙יחַ֙\rb* \rb by the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַֽעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the sweet|וּנְעִ֖ים\rb* \rb psalmist|זְמִר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*:\f + \fr 23:1 \ft Or \fqa the hero of the songs of Israel \ft or \fqa the favorite of the Strong One of Israel\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb The Spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb spoke through|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb me|בִּ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb His word|וּמִלָּת֖וֹ\rb* \rb was on|עַל־\rb* \rb my tongue|לְשׁוֹנִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb The God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb spoke|אָמַר֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb the Rock|צ֣וּר\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb said|דִבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb to me|לִ֥י\rb*,
\q1 ‘\rb He who rules|מוֹשֵׁל֙\rb* \rb the people|בָּאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb with justice|צַדִּ֕יק\rb*,
\q2 \rb who rules|מוֹשֵׁ֖ל\rb* \rb in the fear|יִרְאַ֥ת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 4 \rb is like the light|וּכְא֥וֹר\rb* \rb of the morning|בֹּ֖קֶר\rb*
\q2 \rb at sunrise|שָׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |יִזְרַח־\rb* \rb of a cloudless|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |עָב֔וֹת\rb* \rb dawn|בֹּ֚קֶר\rb*,
\q1 \rb the glistening|מִנֹּ֥גַהּ\rb* \rb after the rain|מִמָּטָ֖ר\rb*
\q2 \rb on the sprouting grass|דֶּ֥שֶׁא\rb* \rb of the earth|מֵאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb my house|בֵּיתִ֖י\rb* \rb right|כֵ֥ן\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb God|אֵ֑ל\rb*?
\q2 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb He has established|שָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb with me|לִ֗י\rb*
\q1 \rb an everlasting|עוֹלָ֜ם\rb* \rb covenant|בְרִ֨ית\rb*,
\q2 \rb ordered|עֲרוּכָ֤ה\rb* \rb and secured|וּשְׁמֻרָ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb in every part|בַכֹּל֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb Will He not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb bring about|יַצְמִֽיחַ׃\rb* \rb my full|כָל־\rb* \rb salvation|יִשְׁעִ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb and my every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb desire|חֵ֖פֶץ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb But the worthless|וּבְלִיַּ֕עַל\rb* \rb are all|כֻּלָּ֑הַם\rb* \rb like thorns|כְּק֥וֹץ\rb* \rb raked aside|מֻנָ֖ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they can never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be gathered|יִקָּֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb by hand|בְיָ֖ד\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb The man|וְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb who touches|יִגַּ֣ע\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb must be armed|יִמָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb with iron|בַרְזֶ֖ל\rb*
\q2 \rb or with the shaft|וְעֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of a spear|חֲנִ֑ית\rb*.
\q1 \rb The fire|וּבָאֵ֕שׁ\rb* \rb burns them to ashes|שָׂר֥וֹף\rb*\rb |יִשָּׂרְפ֖וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb in the place where they lie|בַּשָּֽׁבֶת׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 David’s Mighty Men
\p \v 8 \rb These|אֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of David’s|לְדָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִ֖ים\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Josheb-basshebeth|יֹשֵׁ֨ב\rb*\rb |בַּשֶּׁ֜בֶת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the Tahchemonite|תַּחְכְּמֹנִ֣י׀\rb*\f + \fr 23:8 \fqa Tahchemonite \ft is probably a variant of \fqa Hachmonite\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 11:11.\f* \rb was chief|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the Three|הַשָּׁלִשִׁ֗י\rb*.\f + \fr 23:8 \ft Or \fqa chief among the captains\f* \rb He|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb wielded|עֲדִינ֣וֹ\rb* \rb his spear|הָעֶצְנוֹ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb*\f + \fr 23:8 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also 1 Chronicles 11:11); Hebrew \fqa He was called Adino the Eznite because of\f* \rb eight|שְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb hundred men|מֵא֛וֹת\rb*, \rb whom he killed|חָלָ֖ל\rb* \rb at one|אֶחָד׃ס\rb* \rb time|בְּפַ֥עַם\rb*.
\li1 \v 9 \rb Next in command was|וְאַחֲרוֹ\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֥ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Dodo|דֹּדִי\rb*\f + \fr 23:9 \fqa Dodo \ft is a variant of \fqa Dodai\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 27:4.\f*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb the Ahohite|אֲחֹחִ֑י\rb*. \rb As one of the three|בִּשְׁלֹשָׁ֨ה\rb* \rb mighty men|גִבֹּרִים\rb*, \rb he went with|עִם־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb to taunt|בְּחָֽרְפָ֤ם\rb* \rb the Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּים\rb* \rb who had gathered|נֶאֶסְפוּ־\rb* \rb for battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb at Pas-dammim|שָׁ֣ם\rb*. \rb The men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb retreated|וַֽיַּעֲל֖וּ\rb*, \v 10 \rb but Eleazar|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb stood his ground|קָם֩\rb* \rb and struck|וַיַּ֨ךְ\rb* \rb the Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּ֜ים\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד׀\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֗וֹ\rb* \rb grew weary|יָגְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb and stuck|וַתִּדְבַּ֤ק\rb*\rb |יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his sword|הַחֶ֔רֶב\rb*. \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb brought about|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb a great|גְדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb victory|תְּשׁוּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*. \rb Then the troops|וְהָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb returned|יָשֻׁ֥בוּ\rb* \rb to him|אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb*, \rb but only|אַךְ־\rb* \rb to plunder the dead|לְפַשֵּֽׁט׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 11 \rb And after him|וְאַחֲרָ֛יו\rb* \rb was Shammah|שַׁמָּ֥א\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Agee|אָגֵ֖א\rb* \rb the Hararite|הָרָרִ֑י\rb*. \rb When the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֜ים\rb* \rb had banded together|וַיֵּאָסְפ֨וּ\rb* \rb near|לַחַיָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |שָׁ֞ם\rb*\rb |וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb a field|חֶלְקַ֤ת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb full of|מְלֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb lentils|עֲדָשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb Israel’s troops|וְהָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb fled|נָ֖ס\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb them|פְלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb But Shammah took his stand|וַיִּתְיַצֵּ֤ב\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb of the field|הַֽחֶלְקָה֙\rb*, \rb defended it|וַיַּצִּילֶ֔הָ\rb*, \rb and struck down|וַיַּ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb brought about|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb a great|גְדוֹלָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb victory|תְּשׁוּעָ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb At|אֶל־\rb* \rb harvest time|קָצִיר֙\rb*, \rb three|שְׁלֹשִׁים\rb* \rb of the thirty|מֵהַשְּׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb chief men|רֹ֗אשׁ\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּרְד֨וּ\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cave|מְעָרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Adullam|עֲדֻלָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb while a company|וְחַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb was encamped|חֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּעֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Rephaim|רְפָאִֽים׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb was in the stronghold|בַּמְּצוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and the garrison|וּמַצַּ֣ב\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אָ֖ז\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb was at Bethlehem|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb longed for water|וַיִּתְאַוֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Oh, that someone|מִ֚י\rb* \rb would get me a drink|יַשְׁקֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb of water|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb from the well|מִבֹּ֥אר\rb* \rb near the gate|בַּשָּֽׁעַר׃\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethlehem|לֶ֖חֶם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*!”
\p \v 16 \rb So the three|שְׁלֹ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִ֜ים\rb* \rb broke|וַיִּבְקְעוּ֩\rb* \rb through the Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb camp|בְּמַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb*, \rb drew|וַיִּֽשְׁאֲבוּ־\rb* \rb water|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb from the well|מִבֹּ֤אר\rb* \rb near the gate|בַּשַּׁ֔עַר\rb*\rb |וַיִּשְׂא֖וּ\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethlehem|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and brought it|וַיָּבִ֣אוּ\rb* \rb back to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*. \rb But he refused|וְלֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אָבָה֙\rb* \rb to drink it|לִשְׁתּוֹתָ֔ם\rb*; \rb instead , he poured it out|וַיַּסֵּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb saying|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Far be it|חָלִילָה֩\rb* \rb from me|לִּ֨י\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb to do|מֵעֲשֹׂ֣תִי\rb* \rb this|זֹ֗את\rb*! \rb Is this not the blood|הֲדַ֤ם\rb* \rb of the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb*\rb |הַהֹלְכִ֣ים\rb* \rb who risked their lives|בְּנַפְשׁוֹתָ֔ם\rb*?” \rb So he refused|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb to drink it|לִשְׁתּוֹתָ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb Such|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were the exploits|עָשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb of the three|שְׁלֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִֽים׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Now Abishai|וַאֲבִישַׁ֞י\rb*, \rb the brother|אֲחִ֣י׀\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֣ב\rb* \rb and son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֗ה\rb*,\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb was chief|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the Three|הַשְּׁלֹשִׁי\rb*,\f + \fr 23:18 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts (see also 1 Chronicles 11:20); two Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac \fqa the Thirty\f* \rb and he|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb wielded|עוֹרֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his spear|חֲנִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb hundred men|מֵא֖וֹת\rb*, \rb killed them|חָלָ֑ל\rb*, \rb and won|וְלוֹ־\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb along with the Three|בַּשְּׁלֹשָֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Was he not|הֲכִ֣י\rb* \rb more honored|נִכְבָּ֔ד\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the Three|הַשְּׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb*?\f + \fr 23:19 \ft Hebrew; Syriac \fqa the Thirty\f* \rb And he became|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb commander|לְשָׂ֑ר\rb*,\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb even though he was not|לֹא־\rb* \rb included|בָֽא׃ס\rb* \rb among the Three|הַשְּׁלֹשָׁ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb And Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֧ע\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb was a man|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of valor|חַי\rb*\f + \fr 23:20 \ft Or \fqa Benaiah son of Jehoiada was the son of Ishhai\f* \rb from Kabzeel|מִֽקַּבְצְאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb a man of many|רַב־\rb* \rb exploits|פְּעָלִ֖ים\rb*. \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb struck down|הִכָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb champions|אֲרִאֵל֙\rb*\f + \fr 23:20 \ft Or \fqa two sons of Ariel\f* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and on a snowy|הַשָּֽׁלֶג׃\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb he|וְ֠הוּא\rb* \rb went down|יָרַ֞ד\rb* \rb into|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb a pit|הַבֹּ֖אר\rb* \rb and killed|וְהִכָּ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb a lion|הָאֲרִיַּה\rb*. \v 21 \rb He|וְהוּא־\rb* \rb also struck down|הִכָּה֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an Egyptian|מִצְרִ֜י\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁר\rb* \rb a huge|מַרְאֶ֗ה\rb* \rb man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb*. \rb Although the Egyptian|הַמִּצְרִי֙\rb* \rb had a spear|חֲנִ֔ית\rb* \rb in his hand|וּבְיַ֤ד\rb*, \rb Benaiah went against|וַיֵּ֥רֶד\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb with a club|בַּשָּׁ֑בֶט\rb*, \rb snatched|וַיִּגְזֹ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the spear|הַחֲנִית֙\rb* \rb from his|הַמִּצְרִ֔י\rb* \rb hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb*, \rb and killed the Egyptian|וַיַּהַרְגֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with his own spear|בַּחֲנִיתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were the exploits|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb of Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֑ע\rb*, \rb who won|וְלוֹ־\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb along with the three|בִּשְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb He was most honored|נִכְבָּ֔ד\rb* \rb among|מִן־\rb* \rb the Thirty|הַשְּׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*, \rb but he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb become|בָ֑א\rb* \rb one of the Three|הַשְּׁלֹשָׁ֖ה\rb*. \rb And David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb appointed him|וַיְשִׂמֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb his guard|מִשְׁמַעְתּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Now these were members of the Thirty|בַּשְּׁלֹשִׁ֑ים\rb*:\f + \fr 23:24 \ft Literally \fqa In the Thirty (were):\f*
\b 
\li1 \rb |עֲשָׂה־\rb* \rb Asahel|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb the brother|אֲחִֽי־\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb*,
