\c 24
\s1 David’s Military Census
\p \v 1 \rb Again|וַיֹּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb the anger|אַף־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb burned|לַחֲר֖וֹת\rb* \rb against Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and He stirred up|וַיָּ֨סֶת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb against them|בָּהֶם֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb and take a census|מְנֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֣ב׀\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of his army|הַחַ֣יִל\rb*, \rb who was|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 24:2 \ft LXX \fqa to Joab and the army commanders with him\f* “\rb Go|שֽׁוּט־\rb* \rb now|נָ֞א\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb from Dan|מִדָּן֙\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שֶׁ֔בַע\rb* \rb and register|וּפִקְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that I may know|וְיָ֣דַעְתִּ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb their number|מִסְפַּ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָעָֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb But Joab|יוֹאָ֜ב\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֨יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb multiply|וְיוֹסֵ֣ף\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb times|פְעָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb over|כָּהֵ֤ם׀\rb*\rb |וְכָהֵם֙\rb*, \rb and may the eyes|וְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb see it|רֹא֑וֹת\rb*. \rb But why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb does my lord|וַאדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb want|חָפֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb to do such|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb a thing|בַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb Nevertheless , the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb prevailed|וַיֶּחֱזַ֤ק\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb and against|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the army|הֶחָ֑יִל\rb*. \rb So Joab|יוֹאָ֜ב\rb* \rb and the commanders|וְשָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the army|הַחַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb from the presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb to register|לִפְקֹ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb They crossed|וַיַּעַבְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb and camped|וַיַּחֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb near Aroer|בַעֲרוֹעֵ֗ר\rb*, \rb south|יְמִ֥ין\rb* \rb of the town|הָעִ֛יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb of the valley|הַנַּ֥חַל\rb*, \rb and proceeded toward Gad|הַגָּ֖ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Jazer|יַעְזֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Then they went|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֔דָה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb*\rb |תַּחְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb of Tahtim-hodshi|חָדְשִׁ֑י\rb*,\f + \fr 24:6 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa to Gilead and to the land of the Hittites\f* \rb and|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb*\rb |דָּ֣נָה\rb* \rb on to Dan-jaan|יַּ֔עַן\rb* \rb and around|וְסָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Sidon|צִידֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb They went|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb toward the fortress|מִבְצַר־\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Hivites|הַחִוִּ֖י\rb* \rb and Canaanites|וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֑י\rb*. \rb Finally, they went on|וַיֵּֽצְא֛וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Negev|נֶ֥גֶב\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*,\f + \fr 24:7 \ft Or \fqa to the south of Judah\f*\rb |בְּאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb to Beersheba|שָֽׁבַע׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb At the end|מִקְצֵ֨ה\rb* \rb of nine|תִשְׁעָ֧ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁ֛ים\rb* \rb and twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb days|י֖וֹם\rb*, \rb having gone|וַיָּשֻׁ֖טוּ\rb* \rb through the whole|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb they returned|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb And Joab|יוֹאָ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb reported|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb the total|מִסְפַּ֥ר\rb* \rb number|מִפְקַד־\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb*.\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb In Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb there were|וַתְּהִ֣י\rb* \rb 800,000|שְׁמֹנֶה֩\rb*\rb |מֵא֨וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֤לֶף\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb who drew|שֹׁ֣לֵֽף\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb*, \rb and|וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb in Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb there were 500,000|חֲמֵשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ׃\rb*.
\s1 Judgment for David’s Sin
\p \v 10 \rb After|אַחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb David had numbered|סָפַ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֑םס\rb*, \rb his|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb conscience|לֵב־\rb* \rb was stricken|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb and he|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, “\rb I have sinned|חָטָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹד֙\rb* \rb in what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb*. \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb I beg You|נָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to take away|הַֽעֲבֶר־\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I have acted very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb foolishly|נִסְכַּ֖לְתִּי\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb When David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֥קָם\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֑קֶר פ\rb*, \rb the word|וּדְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb had come|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gad|גָּ֣ד\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*, \rb David’s|דָוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb seer|חֹזֵ֥ה\rb*: \v 12 “\rb Go|הָל֞וֹךְ\rb* \rb and tell|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb am offering|נוֹטֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb you three options|שָׁלֹ֕שׁ\rb*. \rb Choose|בְּחַר־\rb* \rb one|אַֽחַת־\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and I will carry it out|וְאֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb against you|לָּֽךְ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 13 \rb So Gad|גָ֥ד\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹא־\rb* \rb and said|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |ל֡וֹ\rb* “\rb Do you choose to endure|הֲתָב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |לְךָ֣\rb* \rb three|שֶֽׁבַע\rb*\f + \fr 24:13 \ft LXX (see also 1 Chronicles 21:12); Hebrew \fqa seven\f* \rb years|שָׁנִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb of famine|רָעָ֣ב׀\rb* \rb in your land|בְּאַרְצֶ֡ךָ\rb*,\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb months|חֳ֠דָשִׁים\rb* \rb of fleeing|נֻסְךָ֨\rb*\rb |וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb the pursuit|רֹדְפֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb of|לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb your enemies|צָרֶ֜יךָ\rb*, \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb of|הֱ֠יוֹת\rb* \rb plague|דֶּ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb upon your land|בְּאַרְצֶ֔ךָ\rb*? \rb Now then|עַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb think it over|דַּ֣ע\rb* \rb and decide|וּרְאֵ֔ה\rb* \rb how|מָה־\rb* \rb I should reply|דָּבָֽר׃ס\rb*\rb |אָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb to Him who sent me|שֹׁלְחִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb Gad|גָּ֖ד\rb*, “\rb I am|לִ֣י\rb* \rb deeply|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb distressed|צַר־\rb*. \rb Please|נָּ֤א\rb*, \rb let us fall|נִפְּלָה־\rb* \rb into the hand|בְיַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb His mercies are|רַחֲמוֹ\rb* \rb great|רַבִּ֣ים\rb*; \rb but do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let me fall|אֶפֹּֽלָה׃\rb* \rb into the hands|וּבְיַד־\rb* \rb of men|אָדָ֖ם\rb*.”
\s1 A Plague on Israel
\p \v 15 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb a plague|דֶּ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb upon Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb from that morning|מֵהַבֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the appointed|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb time|עֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb and seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Dan|מִדָּן֙\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שֶׁ֔בַע\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb*.\f + \fr 24:15 \ft Literally \fqa and of the people from Dan to Beersheba, seventy thousand men died\f*
\p \v 16 \rb But when the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֥ךְ׀\rb* \rb stretched|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb out his hand|יָד֨וֹ\rb* \rb to destroy|לְשַׁחֲתָהּ֒\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִַם֮\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb relented|וַיִּנָּ֤חֶם\rb* \rb from|אֶל־\rb* \rb the calamity|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb and said|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb to the angel|לַמַּלְאָ֞ךְ\rb* \rb who was destroying|הַמַּשְׁחִ֤ית\rb* \rb the people|בָּעָם֙\rb*, “\rb Enough|רַ֔ב\rb*! \rb Withdraw|הֶ֣רֶף\rb* \rb your hand|יָדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb*!” \rb At that time the angel|וּמַלְאַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb by|עִם־\rb* \rb the threshing floor|גֹּ֖רֶן\rb* \rb of Araunah|הָאוֹרְנָה\rb*\f + \fr 24:16 \fqa Araunah \ft is a variant of \fqa Ornan\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 21:15 and 2 Chronicles 3:1.\f* \rb the Jebusite|הַיְבֻסִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb When David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb saw|בִּרְאֹת֣וֹ׀\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb striking down|הַמַּכֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb the people|בָעָ֗ם\rb*,\rb |וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb he said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, “\rb Surely|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb I, the shepherd|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb*,\f + \fr 24:17 \ft DSS and LXX; MT does not include \fqa the shepherd\ft .\f* \rb have sinned|חָטָ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb and|וְאָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb acted wickedly|הֶעֱוֵ֔יתִי\rb*. \rb But these|וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb sheep|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb*, \rb what|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have they done|עָשׂ֑וּ\rb*? \rb Please|נָ֥א\rb*, \rb let Your hand|יָדְךָ֛\rb* \rb fall upon|תְּהִ֨י\rb* \rb me|בִּ֖י\rb* \rb and my father’s|אָבִֽי׃פ\rb* \rb house|וּבְבֵ֥ית\rb*.”
\s1 David Builds an Altar
\p \v 18 \rb And that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Gad|גָ֥ד\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹא־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|ל֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Go up|עֲלֵה֙\rb* \rb and build|הָקֵ֤ם\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb on the threshing floor|בְּגֹ֖רֶן\rb* \rb of Araunah|אָרָנְיָה\rb* \rb the Jebusite|הַיְבֻסִֽי׃\rb*.” \v 19 \rb So David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb at the word|כִּדְבַר־\rb* \rb of Gad|גָּ֔ד\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb When Araunah|אֲרַ֗וְנָה\rb* \rb looked out|וַיַּשְׁקֵ֣ף\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb coming|עֹבְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb toward him|עָלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb he|אֲרַ֔וְנָה\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb and bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֧חוּ\rb* \rb facedown|אַפָּ֖יו\rb*\rb |אָֽרְצָה׃\rb* \rb before the king|לַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*. \v 21 “\rb Why|מַדּ֛וּעַ\rb* \rb has my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb come|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servant|עַבְדּ֑וֹ\rb*?” \rb Araunah|אֲרַ֔וְנָה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb To buy|לִקְנ֧וֹת\rb* \rb your threshing floor|הַגֹּ֗רֶן\rb*\rb |מֵעִמְּךָ֣\rb*,”\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb that I may build|לִבְנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb so that the plague|הַמַּגֵּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb upon|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb may be halted|וְתֵעָצַ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb Araunah|אֲרַ֙וְנָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, “\rb May my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb take|יִקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb whatever seems|רְאֵה֙\rb* \rb good|הַטּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb to him|בְּעֵינוֹ\rb* \rb and offer it up|וְיַ֛עַל\rb*. \rb Here are the oxen|הַבָּקָ֣ר\rb* \rb for a burnt offering|לָעֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb and the threshing sledges|וְהַמֹּרִגִּ֛ים\rb* \rb and ox|הַבָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb yokes|וּכְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb for the wood|לָעֵצִֽים׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb O king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb Araunah|אֲרַ֥וְנָה\rb* \rb gives|נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb all these|הַכֹּ֗ל\rb* \rb to the king|לַמֶּ֑לֶךְס\rb*.” \rb He also|אֲרַ֙וְנָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb accept you|יִרְצֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 24 “\rb No|לֹ֚א\rb*,” \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲרַ֗וְנָה\rb*,\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* “\rb I insist on paying|קָנ֨וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶקְנֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֽוֹתְךָ֙\rb* \rb a price|בִּמְחִ֔יר\rb*, \rb for I will not|וְלֹ֧א\rb* \rb offer|אַעֲלֶ֛ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֖י\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֣וֹת\rb* \rb that cost me nothing|חִנָּ֑ם\rb*.”
\p \rb So David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb bought|וַיִּ֨קֶן\rb* \rb the threshing floor|הַגֹּ֙רֶן֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the oxen|הַבָּקָ֔ר\rb* \rb for fifty|חֲמִשִּֽׁים׃\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֥ים\rb* \rb of silver|בְּכֶ֖סֶף\rb*.\f + \fr 24:24 \fqa 50 shekels \ft is approximately 1.26 pounds or 569.8 grams of silver.\f* \v 25 \rb And|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֨ם\rb* \rb he built|וַיִּבֶן֩\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and offered|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb and peace offerings|וּשְׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*.
\p \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb answered the prayers|וַיֵּעָתֵ֤ר\rb* \rb on behalf of the land|לָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb and the plague|הַמַּגֵּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb upon|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb was halted|וַתֵּעָצַ֥ר\rb*.
